#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II:
# Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004)
#
# The harvest of the second Stupen', kept apart from traditions/transerfing.ttl,
# which declares the tradition and its works. The whole Stupen' was read,
# chapters VII to X of the combined edition (Ves, 2012), in its English
# translation; the nodes follow the chapters. The text layer has no page
# numbers; every source names chapter and section heading.
#
# Two independent passes over three parts with reconciliation, then one
# integrator per part reading the whole part (prima-materia#924). Parts:
# chapter VII; chapters VIII-IX; chapter X. Shared system terms are typed once,
# by the part that introduces them, and linked from the others. The harvest of
# Stupen' I (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl) is linked, not repeated.
#

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II:
# Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), part 1: chapter VII Intention, from 'Lucid
# Dreaming' to the SUMMARY.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 133 records, B 190;
# 25 records of B without counterpart in A: 3 added, 18 covered, 4 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 3 records both passes missed. Stupen' I
# (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl) is not restated: 6 records whose claim
# a node there already carries are left out and linked; 26 nodes that restate
# a Stupen' I node with a difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie,
# pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie, pmc:TranserfingProstranstvoSnovideniy,
# pmp:TranserfingLucidDreaming. pmc:TranserfingNamerenie already stands in
# Stupen' I (chapter V) and is linked, not retyped; chapter VII's fuller
# definition is pmc:TranserfingResolveToHaveAndActCh7. Linked from parts 2
# and 3: pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma, pmc:TranserfingTsel.
# The author's reports of others (sorcerers, yogis, the paralysed, telekinetic
# people, hypnotists) are third-party ascriptions; his polemics are concepts,
# since only his side is read.
#

#
# ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'
#

pmc:TranserfingLucidityInDreamCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lucid dreaming"@en, "Luzides Träumen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming aware inside a dream that one is dreaming, so that the dream can be joined like a virtual game while knowing it is a dream; said to be inducible by the power of intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLucidDreaming a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Practising lucid dreaming"@en, "Luzides Träumen üben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bring on lucid dreams by intention: build through the day the habit of checking whether what one sees is real, let the inner Guardian repeat the check and use sounds heard in sleep as bridges; once aware within the dream, decide to take charge and act by intention rather than by wish; keep awareness high, avoid needless daring and behave as a guest."@en ;
    skos:note "Shared practice term of Stupen' II, typed by this part; its single steps are entered as their own practices (pmp:TranserfingRealityCheckCh7, pmp:TranserfingChimingClockBridgeCh7, pmp:TranserfingBanishingThePursuerCh7, pmp:TranserfingDreamFlightByIntentionCh7). Optional for Transurfing (pmc:TranserfingLucidDreamingOptionalCh7)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRealityCheckCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Daytime reality check (\"Is this real?\")"@en, "Realitätsprüfung am Tag („Ist das echt?“)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through the day, at least ten times, ask oneself whether what one sees is real; instruct the inner Guardian to keep putting the question; answer it conscientiously each time: rouse oneself a little, look around, appraise whether all is ordinary or something odd is going on. Repeated persistently until the habit carries over into sleep and one wakes up inside a dream."@en ;
    skos:note "Key point stressed: answer with awareness, not mechanically, because many dreamers are shifted into lucidity by noticing an anomaly or contradiction in the dream."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealityCheckAsRoutineCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality check turned into routine"@en, "Realitätsprüfung wird zur Routine"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the question is answered mechanically, the rational mind loses its critical attitude and the procedure becomes empty routine, losing the very alertness that triggers lucidity."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the question is answered mechanically, the rational mind loses its critical attitude and the procedure becomes empty routine, losing the very alertness that triggers lucidity; it bears on pmp:TranserfingRealityCheckCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealityCheckYieldsLucidityCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Reality check yields lucid dreaming"@en, "Realitätsprüfung bringt luzides Träumen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Persistent daytime questioning of reality is said to make one eventually wake up in a dream."@en ;
    skos:note "Onset given as within a few days or a few months, depending on the strength of intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRealityCheckCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingLucidityInDreamCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTooLittleMotivationCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Too little motivation to keep asking"@en, "Zu wenig Motivation für das Fragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remembering the question ten times daily proves hard; without strong motivation the technique will not work."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Remembering the question ten times daily proves hard; without strong motivation the technique will not work; it bears on pmp:TranserfingRealityCheckCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLucidityWithinDaysOrMonthsCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lucid dreams within days or months"@en, "Luzide Träume binnen Tagen oder Monaten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced for the reality check: kept up persistently, it is said to bring waking inside a dream after a few days or a few months, according to how strong the intention is."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingRealityCheckCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingChimingClockBridgeCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Chiming clock as bridge into the dream"@en, "Schlaguhr als Brücke in den Traum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Program the inner Guardian to ask whether one is asleep every time a chiming clock sounds; the sound, audible in sleep too, rouses the Guardian out of habit, which wakes the rational mind inside the dream. Any other sound reliably heard while asleep may serve as the bridge."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChimingClockYieldsLucidityCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Chiming clock yields lucid dreaming"@en, "Schlaguhr bringt luzides Träumen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The clock signal heard in sleep is said to trigger the habitual question and wake the mind within the dream."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingChimingClockBridgeCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingLucidityInDreamCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnreliableCueSignalsCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not tie the question to unreliable signals"@en, "Frage nicht an unzuverlässige Signale binden"@de ;
    skos:definition "A trigger such as an incoming phone call is warned against: unless a call comes at night, the cue only arrives once a call is dreamed of."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingChimingClockBridgeCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingUpDoesNotAlwaysWorkCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up to escape a nightmare often fails"@en, "Aufwachen als Flucht aus dem Albtraum misslingt oft"@de ;
    skos:definition "A dreamer who knows he is dreaming usually tries to escape a chase by waking up, which is said not always to succeed; facing the pursuer is offered as the better course."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A dreamer who knows he is dreaming usually tries to escape a chase by waking up, which is said not always to succeed; facing the pursuer is offered as the better course; it bears on pmc:TranserfingDreamControlCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBanishingThePursuerCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing a dream pursuer"@en, "Verfolger im Traum vertreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once aware of dreaming, turn round, look at the pursuer and think a command such as \"go away\"; the pursuer is said to vanish at once. Alternatively decide to swap roles with the pursuer, who will then turn and flee."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBanishingYieldsDreamControlCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing and role swap yield dream control"@en, "Vertreiben und Rollentausch bringen Traumlenkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Facing the pursuer with a command or a decided role swap is said to change the dream at once."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBanishingThePursuerCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDreamControlCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamControlCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Control of the lucid dream"@en, "Lenkung des luziden Traums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within a lucid dream the dreamer is said to be able to steer everything: make a pursuer vanish or tumble, fly, talk with the living and the dead, visit other planets, work out problems, write music, practise a scene, journey."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoConditionsForDreamControlCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Two conditions for dream control"@en, "Zwei Bedingungen der Traumlenkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Control of the dream requires first awareness that one is dreaming and second the realisation that in that place anything can be done."@en ;
    skos:note "Without the decision to take control one stays powerless, a passive victim whom the game controls, even when aware of dreaming."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingDreamControlCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingLucidityInDreamCh7 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Even a dreamer aware of dreaming remains powerless and is run by the game until deciding to take control." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamFlightYieldsDreamControlCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Decided intention yields dream flight"@en, "Entschiedene Absicht bringt Traumflug"@de ;
    skos:definition "The decision to rise, not the wish, is said to carry the dreamer into the air."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDreamFlightByIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDreamControlCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDreamFlightByIntentionCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Flying in a lucid dream by intention"@en, "Fliegen im Klartraum durch Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not wish to rise or analyse whether it is possible; simply decide to go up, as one lifts a hand without thinking how, and one flies where one wills."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFearAndVictimRoleInDreamCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear and the victim role in the dream"@en, "Angst und Opferrolle im Traum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once fear grips the dreamer, the rational mind is beaten at each turn and someone else seems to set the rules; while playing the passive victim the dreamer stays a slave to the dream, even though it is self-generated."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Once fear grips the dreamer, the rational mind is beaten at each turn and someone else seems to set the rules; while playing the passive victim the dreamer stays a slave to the dream, even though it is self-generated; it bears on pmc:TranserfingDreamControlCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInformationFromDreamsCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bringing information back from a dream"@en, "Information aus dem Traum mitbringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Information is said to be retrievable from a dream; material objects are not, as far as the author has heard."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHeadToTheNorthCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sleeping with the head to the north"@en, "Mit dem Kopf nach Norden schlafen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If dreams are not remembered, check the sleeping direction and lie with the head pointing north; dreams are then said to become more vivid and varied."@en ;
    skos:note "Author cannot explain why; attributes it to the effect of the Earth magnetic fields on the body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoHeadToTheWestCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not sleep with the head to the west"@en, "Nicht mit dem Kopf nach Westen schlafen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sleeping head westward is said to harm health."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingHeadToTheNorthCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeadToTheNorthYieldsVividDreamsCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Northward sleeping yields vivid dreams"@en, "Nordausrichtung bringt lebhafte Träume"@de ;
    skos:definition "Head-to-north sleeping is said to make dreams more vivid and diverse."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHeadToTheNorthCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingVividDreamsCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVividDreamsCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vivid, remembered dreams"@en, "Lebhafte, erinnerte Träume"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dreams that are recalled and become richer and more diverse."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLucidDreamingOptionalCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lucid dreaming is optional for Transurfing"@en, "Luzides Träumen ist für Transurfing entbehrlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lucid dreaming plays some role but is not required; failure or no wish to practise it is no obstacle. The real aim is to learn to choose the script in waking life, to become awake within real life rather than a virtual one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHiddenThreatOfLucidDreamingCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Lucid dreaming holds a hidden threat"@en, "Luzides Träumen birgt eine verborgene Gefahr"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author warns against his own positively introduced topic: lucid dreaming opens a hidden door into the unknown with a danger behind it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLucidDreaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Lucid Dreaming'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'
#

pmc:TranserfingProstranstvoSnovideniy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The dream space"@en, "Der Traumraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dream images are not synthesised by the brain; the subconscious, via the heart, tunes in to sectors of the space of alternatives, including unrealised ones. The brain stores only addresses of information located in that space. Hence dreams are real seeing, not illusions, and may show places and versions of people that never materialised."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: prostranstvo snovideniy (пространство сновидений)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMemoryAsAddressesCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Memory as addresses into the field"@en, "Gedächtnis als Adressen ins Feld"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind keeps the addresses of sectors; to recall, it turns to the heart, which tunes to the matching sector of the information field. Imperfect memory is put down to poor tuning, poor address retrieval or poor collaboration of heart and mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamsAreNotSignsCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dreams are not to be read as signs"@en, "Träume sind keine Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dreams show what could have been or could be; since the soul may fly to any sector, dream content cannot be relied on as foretelling. Gut feeling in waking, in which the heart senses coming events, is held to be the most reliable sign."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingComfortAsForesight: the reliance on gut feeling restates Stupen' I; new is that dream content is excluded as a sign because the soul may roam any sector."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGodAngelsHigherPowersCh7 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "God, angels, higher powers"@en, "Gott, Engel, höhere Mächte"@de ;
    skos:definition "God alone is said to know which sector the dreaming soul explores; angels, God and higher powers are held not to answer requests, since universal law is indifferent."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOneSpirit: God is named only as knower of the sector a dreaming soul visits; angels and higher powers are said not to answer requests, against pmp:TranserfingTurningToTheGuardianAngel of Stupen' I."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "God; the Angels; higher powers" ;
    pm:nameRole "not to be petitioned" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExpectationSelectsDreamScriptCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Expectation selects the dream script"@en, "Erwartung wählt das Traumskript"@de ;
    skos:definition "In dreams the soul picks a sector whose script fits the dreamer's expectations, fears and opinions, realising them instantly: the faintest thought of being chased brings a monster. When lucid, it is intention that picks the script; the soul re-attunes to a sector with the corresponding script."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingLawSlowedByMatterCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Same law in waking, slowed by inert matter"@en, "Gleiches Gesetz im Wachen, gebremst durch träge Materie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking events follow the laws of dreams but more slowly because material realisation of an alternative involves dense, resin-like matter. One always creates the object of one's dominant thoughts; thought is energy whose vibration matches a given life line."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingThoughtRadiation: the waking shift is put under the same law as the dream shift and its delay ascribed to inert, resin-like matter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChoosingTheScriptAwakeCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing the script in waking life"@en, "Das Skript im Wachleben wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The aim of the chapter: to become awake within real life and select the wanted script there, as one does in a lucid dream."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingChoosingDestiny: choice is modelled on picking the script in a lucid dream and framed as waking up within waking life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRiskOfNoReturnCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Risk of not returning from a lucid dream"@en, "Gefahr, aus dem Klartraum nicht zurückzukehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Safe while the soul roams unrealised sectors; if it strays into a sector realised as physical reality, a hypothesis holds that the person may manifest physically there and not come back; failing to return is then reported as dying in one's sleep. The mind, tasting unlimited freedom, is tempted to roam recklessly. Advice: take dreaming seriously, keep maximum awareness, avoid needless daring, behave as a guest."@en ;
    skos:note "Author speculates that some of the many people who go missing each year are lost in dreaming. Also notes this risk applies without lucidity."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLucidDreaming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSorcerersPassingOverCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bodily passage into other worlds through dreaming"@en, "Leiblicher Übergang in andere Welten durch Träumen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sorcerers of old are said to have mastered dreaming and to have passed intentionally and permanently into other worlds, their bodies vanishing from this one."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAstralProjectionApartCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Astral projection is also risky and unrelated"@en, "Astralreisen sind ebenfalls riskant und gehören nicht dazu"@de ;
    skos:definition "Astral travel differs from lucid dreaming, has its own risks and has no relation to Transurfing; the task is to make reality comfortable, not to flee into dream worlds."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingProstranstvoSnovideniy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGutCheckOnLucidDreamingCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gut check before taking up lucid dreaming"@en, "Bauchgefühl prüfen, bevor man Klarträumen beginnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Notice the feeling in the gut when reading about lucid dreaming; a negative feeling means it is not for you. The heart senses personal danger better than the mind."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck: the gut check is applied to whether to take up lucid dreaming at all, not to a pending decision."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Dream Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingThoughtSeemsWeightlessCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why thought seems weightless in waking"@en, "Warum Denken im Wachen gewichtslos scheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thoughts carry one into sectors with matching scripts, yet results often oppose striving because balanced forces answer excess potential; and thought alone on the sofa shifts nothing. The apparent contradiction is resolved by intention, not thought."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWhyVisualisationFailsCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why visualisation rarely works"@en, "Warum Visualisierung selten wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reasons given: (1) excess potential from intense attachment to fulfilment; (2) the inertia of material realisation; (3) too little persistence, so the goal lacks time to materialise before passion fades and it is abandoned; (4) expecting everything at once; (5) several unconnected goals at once dissipate thought energy, since the flow allows no swimming in different directions."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Reasons given: (1) excess potential from intense attachment to fulfilment; (2) the inertia of material realisation; (3) too little persistence, so the goal lacks time to materialise before passion fades and it is abandoned; (4) expecting everything at once; (5) several unconnected goals at once dissipate thought energy, since the flow allows no swimming in different directions."@en ;
    skos:note "Told aside: wanted things often arrive late, after hope was given up and the order forgotten."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPicturingTheWorst: Stupen' I deferred why visualisation fails; here five reasons are listed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOneGoalAtATimeCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "One specific goal at a time"@en, "Ein bestimmtes Ziel zur Zeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attuning to a target sector works best when focused on a single specific goal; unconnected parallel goals spread energy thin."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step is a single specific goal; pmc:TranserfingTsel, the goal, is typed by part 3 of Stupen' II."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingChoosingTheScriptAwakeCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingTsel ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Thought energy spread over several unconnected goals dissipates into emptiness." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingResolveToHaveAndActCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention: resolve to have and act"@en, "Absicht: Entschlossenheit zu haben und zu handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Realisation comes not from desire but from one's attitude to the desired: intention, roughly defined as resoluteness in deciding to have and act. Thoughts are foam on its wave. Desire fixes on the goal and is realised as excess potential; intention fixes on the process and is realised as action, without debating attainability. The hand is lifted neither by desire nor by decisiveness but by intention, which the mind cannot fully explain. In dreams a script is chosen by firm expectation of having: no analysing, no desiring, simply having and acting."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNamerenie: Stupen' I defines intention as readiness to act; here it is resoluteness to have as well as to act, lying beyond decision, fixed on the process and not on the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPowerOfIntentionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power of intention"@en, "Kraft der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The force beyond decisiveness that enacts a choice; described as subtle, hard to gain and easily lost."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWalkingAgainAfterParalysisCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Restored power to walk after paralysis"@en, "Wiedergewonnene Gehfähigkeit nach Lähmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paralysed people are reported to have walked again through hypnosis or miraculous healing, read as the power of intention being returned."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnalysingWhetherPossibleCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Analysing whether it is possible"@en, "Zerdenken, ob es möglich ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "If in a dream one starts weighing whether flight is possible, nothing happens; desire alone, as in waking, produces nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If in a dream one starts weighing whether flight is possible, nothing happens; desire alone, as in waking, produces nothing; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDreamFlightByIntentionCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoPetitioningHigherPowersCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not ask higher powers for things"@en, "Höhere Mächte nicht um Dinge bitten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking angels, God or higher powers is pointless: universal laws are dispassionate. Requests, complaints and demands, and words like \"give\" and \"want\", create excess potential and are said to be pendulum inventions for harvesting energy. Only the intention to choose makes sense; requests are reasonable only toward other humans, within limits."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTheNeedy: the needy role begs; here every petition to God, angels or higher powers is called pointless and requests are traced to pendulums."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTheNeedy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGratitudeRadiatesCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gratitude radiates creative energy"@en, "Dankbarkeit strahlt schöpferische Energie aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike a request, sincere gratitude is akin to unconditional love and makes a person radiate creative energy, whereas a request concentrates energy and delays action."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGratitudeThenImaginingYieldsBetterLifeCircumstances: gratitude is likened to unconditional love and set against the request, which concentrates energy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChoiceDischargesPotentialCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choice discharges potential through action"@en, "Wahl entlädt Potenzial durch Handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choosing is deciding to have and to act, not requesting; if the energy one radiates matches the choice and no laws are broken, one receives the choice. Intention joins desire and action and so dissipates the excess potential of desire without calling up balanced forces; acting even loads that energy into one's own field, while waiting, worry, doubt and wanting drain it. Illustrated by learning through doing being inspiring, cramming exhausting."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingThreeTypesOfDesire: adds that action not only discharges the potential of desire but loads its energy into one's own field."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Magical Power of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner intention"@en, "Innere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intention carried out by one's own effort: attention is fixed on the path toward the goal and presses directly on the world of the present life line; it can reach the goal but costs much effort, follows the pattern of insisting, and amounts to the decision to act. Its counterpart is pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: vnutrennee namerenie (внутреннее намерение)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention"@en, "Äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner intention is doing something by one's own effort; outer intention extends intention to the outside world: it does not alter anything but selects a life line where the wish is realised and shifts material realisation there (an apple tree is not changed into pears; the realisation moves to a line where pears stand). All that is called magic or paranormal is said to be its work; it is also the mechanism by which worst expectations come true, acting independently of will. Called the cornerstone of Transurfing and what unlocks the Guardian's riddle. It works unhurried, cool-headed and detached; that the goal will be reached is neither doubted nor debated."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: vneshnee namerenie (внешнее намерение)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTelekinesisAsShiftCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telekinesis as shifting a point of realisation"@en, "Telekinese als Verschieben des Realisierungspunkts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some people with extrasensory abilities are said to move a pencil; on this reading they do not move it but shift the point where it is realised across life lines, so only the pencil layer moves."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPencilExerciseCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pencil exercise of outer intention"@en, "Bleistiftübung der äußeren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "With a pencil on the table, do not push it with thought; firmly intend to picture it beginning to move, letting attention scan sectors where it lies elsewhere; with enough radiated thought energy it is said to materialise in other positions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPencilExerciseYieldsTelekinesisCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pencil exercise yields telekinetic shift"@en, "Bleistiftübung bringt telekinetische Verschiebung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagining the pencil moved, with sufficient energy, is said to shift its realisation point."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPencilExerciseCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTelekinesisAsShiftCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDisbeliefBlocksOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disbelief blocks pure outer intention"@en, "Unglaube verhindert reine äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most people cannot move the pencil, not owing to a feeble energy field but because pure outer intention is hard to call up while struggling to believe such things possible."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Most people cannot move the pencil, not owing to a feeble energy field but because pure outer intention is hard to call up while struggling to believe such things possible; it bears on pmp:TranserfingPencilExerciseCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVictimConquerorMasterCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Victim, conqueror, master"@en, "Opfer, Eroberer, Gebieter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thought experiment on an island of hostile natives: the ingratiating victim gets eaten, the aggressor wins or dies (both inner intention); the one who, without doubt in his might, acts as master is obeyed, because his thought energy tunes to lines where he is king (outer intention)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingClaimingThePossibilityCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Claiming the possibility (parking-space example)"@en, "Die Möglichkeit beanspruchen (Parkplatzbeispiel)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Where inner intention declares an outcome impossible, allow that it may happen, e.g. a space coming free just as one arrives; not by solid belief but by claiming what one deems necessary, dispassionately and unconditionally. Also: step back and widen the view, like a fly that would see the open window beside the pane."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClaimingYieldsOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dispassionate claiming engages outer intention"@en, "Leidenschaftsloses Beanspruchen setzt äußere Absicht in Gang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Claiming the needed possibility without condition is offered as how outer intention chooses the alternative."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingClaimingThePossibilityCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRitualAsPreludeCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ritual is only a prelude to magic"@en, "Ritual ist nur Vorspiel der Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention arises from improvisation, like insight, and cannot be prepared; all magic rituals aim to evoke it but are theatrical preparation. Spells and attributes may help wake the power latent in everyone, and belief in them can stimulate the weak capacity, but they cannot apply it; the power lies in outer intention and the person, not in objects."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingRitualAsProp: the ritual is now said to aim at outer intention, and belief in it to stimulate a weak capacity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionAtrophiedCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention atrophied in modern humans"@en, "Äußere Absicht beim heutigen Menschen verkümmert"@de ;
    skos:definition "The capacity has all but atrophied and been erased from memory, only hinted at in legend; it is blocked, not lost. The pyramids are suggested to have been built by it. Pendulums, living off inner-intention energy, are said to have pushed inner intention to the fore and buried knowledge of outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTrainedOutOfChoosing: what pendulums suppressed is named as the knowledge of outer intention, put behind inner intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstAlchemicalLiteratureCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against alchemical literature and magical relics"@en, "Gegen alchemistische Literatur und magische Reliquien"@de ;
    skos:definition "The alchemists sought the philosopher's stone in vain; the many books on alchemy are called complicated and misguided, the secret said to fit a few lines of the Emerald Tablet. Legends of power-giving objects such as the Holy Grail are naive misconceptions; fetishes and incantations have no power of their own. Surviving magical practice is called frail and superficial, often confused with inner intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Polemic of the author against a view he describes himself; only his side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMasteryBreedsPotentialCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mastery of outer intention breeds excess potential"@en, "Beherrschung der äußeren Absicht erzeugt Überschusspotenzial"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ancient civilisations that perfected outer intention beyond the need for ritual are said to have built up strong excess potential, and that is how ones like Atlantis were destroyed by balanced forces."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumFreedomBeforeOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from pendulums before outer intention"@en, "Freiheit von Pendeln vor äußerer Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Real development of outer intention is possible only after becoming as free as possible from pendulum manipulation."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromPendulum ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDesireInnerOuterCh7 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Desire, inner intention, outer intention"@en, "Wunsch, innere Absicht, äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thought energy aimed at goals takes three forms: desire (attention on the goal itself, powerless), inner intention (attention on the path toward it, works with great effort) and outer intention (attention on the goal realising itself, presupposing the alternative already exists and needs only choosing). Inner achieves, outer chooses."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingObserverThoughtPatternCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer-intention thought pattern"@en, "Denkmuster der äußeren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Replace the inner pattern \"I insist that ...\" with formulas of the kind \"as things stand, ...\" or \"as it happens, ...\", standing as an outside observer to whom things happen without coercion; as in a dream flight that comes from \"oh, I am flying\" rather than insistence. Check oneself against paired contrasts: getting versus being given, fighting versus being embraced, knocking versus the door opening, forcing events versus events arriving."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObserverPatternYieldsOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Observer pattern yields outer intention"@en, "Beobachtermuster bringt äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking the observer stance is presented as the move from changing the world to choosing it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingObserverThoughtPatternCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingActingFromTheReceivingSideCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting from the second half of the contrasts"@en, "Handeln aus der zweiten Hälfte der Gegensätze"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one's actions match the receiving side of the paired contrasts, one has grasped the principle of outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingObserverThoughtPatternCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Working with outer intention"@en, "Mit äußerer Absicht arbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to let a goal realise itself by choosing the alternative in which it already exists, so that the alternatives space moves to oneself; said to have no limit in principle (flying or walking on water given outer intention like that of Christ), though in practice even a tiny share is held to give formidable results."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFlightAsShiftOfRealisationCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Flight as a shift of the realisation point"@en, "Flug als Verschiebung des Verwirklichungspunkts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Flying, in dream or waking, is explained not as motion through physical space against gravity but as the point of realisation moving across sectors, so that space moves relative to the body; the laws of physics are said to hold only within one sector of realisation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingJesusAsExemplarCh7 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus / Christ"@en, "Jesus / Christus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cited as having said that it is done according to one's faith; his outer intention is the measure for walking on water."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Jesus; Christ" ;
    pm:nameRole "exemplar of outer intention" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFaithBeforeIntentionCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Faith before intention"@en, "Glaube vor Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "To fly one must have absolute faith that it is possible; without intention nothing is received or done, and intention needs faith."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step is faith, linked to pmc:TranserfingFaithOutweighsWords; the dependent step is intention (pmc:TranserfingNamerenie)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingNamerenie ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingFaithOutweighsWords ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Lacking faith, intention fails to arise, and lacking intention nothing is received or done." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLevitationOfYogisCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Levitation"@en, "Levitation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Yogis in India are said to leave the ground in meditation, the only reliable levitation cases the author has met; their intention may suffice to tune to the flow of alternatives where the body floats. Called the summit of outer intention; not a goal of Transurfing."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPureOuterIntentionBeyondBeliefCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pure outer intention is beyond belief and doubt"@en, "Reine äußere Absicht steht jenseits von Glauben und Zweifel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Faith leaves room for doubt; knowledge removes it. Pure outer intention holds no doubt and so no belief either. In sleep a hint suffices; in inert material reality it must be absolutely pure. For personal goals, however, ordinary intention is said to suffice, given time for realisation to gain momentum."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHypnoticSuggestionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hypnotic suggestion by thought energy"@en, "Hypnotische Suggestion durch Gedankenenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some people are said to radiate and direct strong energy waves; programmed with thoughts, these put the target under suggestion, independent of gaze, passes or voice. At close range read as inner intention, at a distance outer intention is held to play the main role."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoExerciseForOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No exercise develops outer intention"@en, "Keine Übung entwickelt äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author knows of no exercises that specifically train a feel for outer intention; it must be applied to be experienced, a vicious circle requiring escape from the Procrustean bed of everyday thinking. Lucid dreaming is named as the only route to understanding it more deeply; otherwise he recommends living it rather than training it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLucidDreamingForOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Lucid dreaming for deeper grasp of outer intention"@en, "Luzides Träumen für tieferes Verständnis der äußeren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deeper understanding of the nature of outer intention is said to come only through practising lucid dreaming."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingLucidDreaming ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingConsciousLivingCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious living as living outer intention"@en, "Bewusstes Leben als gelebte äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "In place of a targeted exercise, practise living consciously in physical reality, living outer intention rather than drilling it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConsciousLivingYieldsOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious living yields outer intention"@en, "Bewusstes Leben bringt äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recommended as the practical substitute for training outer intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingConsciousLivingCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerBecomesOuterCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner turns outer where conscious and subconscious merge"@en, "Innere wird äußere Absicht, wo Bewusstes und Unbewusstes verschmelzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Transurfing method leaves inner intention alone and applies outer intention. Inner becomes outer when conscious and subconscious mind meet; the boundary is elusive, felt like free fall, first balance on a bicycle or deliberately rising in a dream. This faculty is said to be weaker trained even than wiggling one's ears."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgreementInAversionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement of heart and mind triggers outer intention"@en, "Einigkeit von Herz und Verstand löst äußere Absicht aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feared and hated events come true because mind and soul agree fully in their aversion; at such moments of union outer intention lets through whatever both agree on, regardless of whether it is wanted, choosing the matching sector. People know well what they do not want and only vaguely what they passionately desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClearNegativityAndUniteCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Clear negativity and unite heart and mind in the goal"@en, "Negatives räumen und Herz und Verstand im Ziel einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To bring outer intention under one's will one must wipe negative thought away and set heart and mind in harmony in the positive aim."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step is heart-mind unity, pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma, typed by part 2 of Stupen' II."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise resentment and dissatisfaction bring balanced forces and destructive pendulums, thought energy fixes on negative sectors and outer intention realises them against one's will." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAvoidImportanceAndNegativityCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Avoid importance and negativity"@en, "Wichtigkeit und Negativität meiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "To escape the unwanted results of outer intention one must create no potential of projected importance and refuse all involvement with negativity."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstSecretKnowledgeGurusCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against secret-knowledge gurus and mystifying schools"@en, "Gegen Geheimwissen-Gurus und vernebelnde Schulen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disputes adepts of some schools and spiritual circles who wrap ideas in mystery; a guru who claims knowledge too precious to be spoken except whispered to a disciple has likely not grasped it himself. Clear thinkers speak clearly."@en ;
    skos:note "Polemic of the author against a view he describes himself; only his side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoClassesNeededCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing needs no classes or mystical practices"@en, "Transurfing braucht keine Kurse oder mystischen Übungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "All needed on outer intention is in the book; the skills come from personal experience of applying the principles; no seminars, meditations, lucid dreaming or other mystical activity are required, only reconsidering one's established worldview. Aim is achieving goals with existing means, not levitation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSoonConvincedCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Soon convinced outer intention works"@en, "Bald überzeugt, dass äußere Absicht wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: after revising one's views one will likely soon become convinced that outer intention can be made to work for oneself and achieve things once thought beyond reach."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'Outer Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'
#

pmc:TranserfingDreamScriptCorrectedCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dream script corrected by passing assessments"@en, "Traumskript, laufend durch Bewertungen korrigiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "In non-lucid dreams the dozing mind watches like a cinema-goer; its passing assessments go to the heart, which retunes to a matching sector, so scenery and characters shift with each opinion (like a kitten before a mirror). What the dreamer does himself is inner intention; everything else is the dreamer's outer intention. The mirror shows inner intention correcting one's face; the dream shows outer intention. Only scripts the dreamer can conceive of can unfold. Information the mind discarded as unreal stays within reach of the subconscious, which tries out outlandish scripts with it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIrrationalSectorsUnrealisedCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Irrational dream sectors stay unrealised"@en, "Irrationale Traumsektoren bleiben unverwirklicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most of the sectors a soul visits in dreams never become physical, because their irrational events would demand very large inputs of energy to materialise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamContinuesInWakingCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The dream goes on after waking"@en, "Der Traum setzt sich nach dem Erwachen fort"@de ;
    skos:definition "A dream is said to carry on to some degree after one wakes, at which point the mind gains more say over what happens; the chapter summary repeats the point for waking reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingLifeAsDozingCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking life as dozing in the game"@en, "Wachleben als Dösen im Spiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind's uncritical stance toward waking reality lets hypnosis and trance work; everyone is to some degree asleep, absorbed in the game so that, like a fan brought onto the field, they cannot judge as an outside observer. Closed specialist groups develop vocabularies and acts that look absurd from outside."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGameAsUnrecognisedDream: extended to hypnosis, trance and the uncritical mind of closed groups."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeYesTranceCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Three-yes trance (Gypsy hypnosis)"@en, "Drei-Ja-Trance („Zigeunerhypnose“)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Described manipulation: getting someone to answer yes to three separate questions makes them feel all is in order, lowers vigilance and puts their critical faculty nearly to sleep; people with a rigid daily routine are especially prone."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWakingLifeAsDozingCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stepping down into the auditorium"@en, "In den Zuschauerraum hinabsteigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "At any moment, rouse yourself and declare your awareness of what you do and what goes on; leave the stage for the auditorium by waking the inner Guardian; then go on playing the role, saying and doing what is required, but consciously, detached, judging events soberly. Distraction by a person, event or problem pulls one back into the game, so it must be renewed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness: the waking is pictured as stepping down from stage to auditorium while still playing the role."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAuditoriumYieldsAwarenessCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Auditorium stance yields awareness"@en, "Zuschauerhaltung bringt Wachheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking the Guardian and playing consciously is presented as how one wakes in waking life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingStepIntoTheAuditoriumCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWhyLucidityAlignsCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why lucidity aligns outer intention"@en, "Warum Klarheit die äußere Absicht ausrichtet"@de ;
    skos:definition "In lucid dreaming outer intention does not adopt the will but stops contradicting it: the mind loosens its hold on the heart and in return gets its sanction; that unity activates outer intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingUpBeforeOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up before working with outer intention"@en, "Aufwachen vor der Arbeit mit äußerer Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention needs a higher level of awareness than inner intention; whether lucid in a dream or awake, one must wake up to work with it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without awareness the dream, and reality, cannot be steered; it just happens and outer intention acts independently of will." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game Script'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'
#

pmc:TranserfingFourResponsesToAttackCh7 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Four types of inner intention"@en, "Vier Arten der inneren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Responses to attack in a dream are classed as flight, fight, awakening and realisation; flight and fight are called primitive responses of inner intention."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFightingByHabitualScriptCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fighting by the habitual script"@en, "Kämpfen nach dem gewohnten Skript"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fighting back in a dream follows the standard waking model; the mind already has the ending: whoever is used to losing loses."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Fighting back in a dream follows the standard waking model; the mind already has the ending: whoever is used to losing loses; it bears on pmc:TranserfingDreamControlCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingOpponentIntoAFrogCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning the dream opponent into a frog"@en, "Den Traumgegner in einen Frosch verwandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without yearning or striving for change, quietly turn to the attacker and simply imagine them backing off and becoming a frog, accepting it as a possible reality; if the mind fully accepts an alternative course the heart will not object, and their union realises the script."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFrogYieldsOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting imagination yields outer intention in dreams"@en, "Annehmendes Vorstellen bringt äußere Absicht im Traum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagining and accepting the event, rather than willing it, is said to activate outer intention through heart-mind union."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingOpponentIntoAFrogCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWillOnlyForHarmonyCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal will only for heart-mind harmony"@en, "Eigener Wille nur für Einklang von Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention arises from harmony of heart and mind, not from will; so inner intention should be aimed only at establishing that harmony."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcknowledgeControllableScriptCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Acknowledge the script can be controlled; be aware"@en, "Steuerbarkeit des Skripts anerkennen; wach sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "To set outer intention one must first acknowledge that the script is controllable, and awareness is required for it to work in one's favour."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "A non-lucid dream is beyond steering; an unconscious person experiences reality as set by outside forces, and others and fate rule their life." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWitnessYieldsAwarenessCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Witness stance yields awareness and control"@en, "Zeugenhaltung bringt Wachheit und Lenkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Presented as the way to gain control both in dreams and in life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingParticipatingWitnessCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingParticipatingWitnessCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Participating witness"@en, "Teilnehmender Zeuge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Switch from immersed participant to witness: keep acting your part while the inner Guardian stays switched on in the background, not intervening, only following and soberly assessing; like an actor who also watches himself and the others from the auditorium. Keep inner and outer importance minimal so as not to be absorbed in the role."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingRentYourselfOut: framed as actor and spectator at once, with the Guardian running in the background and importance kept minimal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLowImportanceForWitnessCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Low importance to stay out of the role"@en, "Geringe Wichtigkeit, um nicht in der Rolle aufzugehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Avoiding total absorption in a role requires minimal inner and outer importance and a Guardian always at the ready."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingParticipatingWitnessCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious awareness (the witness)"@en, "Bewusste Wachheit (der Zeuge)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Playing one's part while an inner observer watches soberly from outside the game; control of a situation is said to rise in direct proportion to it, and susceptibility to other people and destructive pendulums to fall in inverse proportion."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower: control is put in direct and susceptibility in inverse proportion to the level of awareness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDozingOffIntoAProblemCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dozing off into a problem"@en, "In ein Problem hineindösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Faced with an unwelcome task, one frets and runs through scenarios of difficulty and consequences; at that point one has joined the game and dozed off, can be led like a child to the hard work, and once heart and mind agree in concern outer intention shifts one onto the problem line. Root cause: inner and outer importance; fear, despair, dissatisfaction and worry take hold fast."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Faced with an unwelcome task, one frets and runs through scenarios of difficulty and consequences; at that point one has joined the game and dozed off, can be led like a child to the hard work, and once heart and mind agree in concern outer intention shifts one onto the problem line. Root cause: inner and outer importance; fear, despair, dissatisfaction and worry take hold fast."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingVaudevilleAttitudeCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The vaudeville attitude to a problem"@en, "Die Vaudeville-Haltung zu einem Problem"@de ;
    skos:definition "When someone brings a problem: (1) rouse yourself, tell yourself you are not asleep and that you decide whether the pendulum's first prod becomes your problem; (2) resolve to beat the pendulum: before even hearing it, program yourself to take it as a trifle; do not let yourself be led by the hand; take no assertive step, neither refuse nor stall nor get irritated; just listen, nod outwardly, stay the witness inwardly, attentive and clear. Then merely intend to imagine that the simple solution holds, as on a light-comedy life line where no complex problems exist; and trust the flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingRentYourselfOut: adds programming oneself before hearing the problem and imagining the simple solution of a light-comedy line."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVaudevilleYieldsEasyLineCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Vaudeville attitude yields easy solutions"@en, "Vaudeville-Haltung bringt leichte Lösungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagining the simple solution is said to shift one to the line where the problem is easy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVaudevilleAttitudeCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingVaudevilleLineCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPleasantSurpriseCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pleasant surprise: problem solved, gone or passed on"@en, "Angenehme Überraschung: Problem gelöst, verschwunden oder abgegeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once you practise this you will be pleasantly surprised; outcomes may be very improbable; at least the problem is solved easily, vanishes or goes to someone else; with high heart-mind unity results may be astonishing."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingVaudevilleAttitudeCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVaudevilleLineCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Problems resolving the easy way"@en, "Probleme lösen sich auf leichte Weise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being on the life line where complex problems find a simple solution, dissolve or pass to someone else."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingEasySolutions: tied to a life line on which complex problems do not exist; a problem may also pass to someone else."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoPuppeteerCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not play the puppeteer"@en, "Nicht den Puppenspieler spielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beware of thinking oneself the puppeteer: any conceit, sense of superiority, contempt or disdain disturbs balance and brings an instant slap. No one controls all of life, even in dreams; one may choose but not change; be at home but remember you are a guest."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNoControllingTheWorld: aimed at the one who has woken up: the right is to choose, not to change."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingVaudevilleAttitudeCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessNotForcingCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness is not forcing the script"@en, "Wachheit heißt nicht, das Skript zu erzwingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A self-warning on its own method: once in the auditorium one may be tempted to alter the script forcibly and impose one's will on the other actors; that is pure inner intention against the current, nothing to do with Transurfing. Awareness lies in observing; control only extends to imagining a favourable script, allowing it in and embracing it. Only with heart and mind as one does one stop fighting the world."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation: the temptation is named for the moment of reaching the auditorium; control is limited to imagining, admitting and embracing a good script."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuardianRoleCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Guardian as role of the master of one's fate"@en, "Der Wächter als Rolle dessen, der sein Schicksal führt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Of the roles (beggar, indignant, fighter, administrator) the one fitting Transurfing is the Guardian; more awareness in waking means more effective charge of one's destiny; leaders are more often in this role because their position demands being more awake. Taking responsibility for one's fate is freedom, not burden."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingExtremesAndRoles: the further stance Stupen' I left open is named: the Guardian."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBurstOfEnergyCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Burst of energy on taking the Guardian role"@en, "Energieschub beim Einnehmen der Wächterrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once you take the Guardian position you will feel a surge of energy and vitality, because you now create your own destiny rather than doing another's will."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessNotIntellectCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness, not intellect, makes a clear mind"@en, "Wachheit, nicht Intellekt, macht den Geist klar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Humans differ from animals more in awareness than intellect; the secret of clever people is awareness, which gives clarity. Daydreaming breeds mistakes; absorption in the game constricts perception. Unawareness comes from not wanting to face reality (ostrich); fear and rage are extreme absences of awareness; pendulums lull vigilance into a zombie state, which is why waking in a dream is hard."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsDullVigilanceCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums lull vigilance"@en, "Pendel schläfern die Wachsamkeit ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums are said to dull alertness gently into a zombie-like state, relying on most people living half aware and becoming sharp only when adrenaline runs; this is given as why waking in a dream is so hard."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLapsedVigilance: pendulums are said to dull vigilance actively, exploiting the habitual semi-aware state."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMayatnik ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSuddenUrgeYieldsHearingCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Catching the urge yields intuition"@en, "Impuls ertappen bringt Intuition"@de ;
    skos:definition "Noticing sudden urges is said to make intuitive knowledge easier to perceive."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCatchingTheSuddenUrgeCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHearingTheMorningStars ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCatchingTheSuddenUrgeCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Catching the sudden urge"@en, "Den plötzlichen Impuls ertappen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Catch yourself asking why this sudden urge to act has come and listen for the quiet answer of the soul before the mind overrides it; build the habit of continually listening for the morning stars rustling."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSemiConsciousMissesVoiceCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Semi-conscious state misses the inner voice"@en, "Halbbewusster Zustand überhört die innere Stimme"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a semi-conscious state one cannot recall fast enough to note what the inner voice says; even a strict morning resolution to listen to the soul is forgotten at the right moment once one sinks into daydream."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: In a semi-conscious state one cannot recall fast enough to note what the inner voice says; even a strict morning resolution to listen to the soul is forgotten at the right moment once one sinks into daydream; it bears on pmp:TranserfingCatchingTheSuddenUrgeCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHarmonyGeneratesMindfulnessDirectsCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Harmony generates, mindfulness directs"@en, "Einklang erzeugt, Achtsamkeit lenkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Heart-mind harmony generates outer intention; mindfulness makes it work for one. Unity is easy in dreams because the heart escapes the mind's control; in waking the mind clings to common sense, a lifelong cell, and keeps room for doubt, so full alignment with will is hard, though experience shows mindfulness greatly raises the odds."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAreYouAsleepYieldsAwarenessCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Constant self-questioning yields maximal awareness"@en, "Ständiges Fragen bringt höchste Wachheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Maximum awareness is said to be reachable as long as the Guardian is constantly present."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAreYouAsleepCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingConsciousAwarenessCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAreYouAsleepCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking every minute \"Are you asleep?\""@en, "Jede Minute fragen: „Schläfst du?“"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep the inner Guardian constantly present: ask yourself throughout the day, every minute, whether you are asleep, until it becomes a standing attitude; the Guardian judges whose interests the game serves and keeps you from being drawn in like a puppet. Preferred over lucid dreaming, since dreams end and everyday life returns."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness: the reminder is the minute-by-minute question whether one is asleep."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Game According to Your Rules'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingBalancedIntentionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Balanced intention"@en, "Ausgewogene Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention is control and its renunciation at once, deciding to have while giving up the need to attain. Balance means wanting without desiring, caring without worrying, striving without distraction, acting without demanding; it is broken by excess potential born of projected importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTakeCareWithoutWorry: four paired formulas are given and applied to intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPureIntentionVersusDesireCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pure intention versus desire"@en, "Reine Absicht gegenüber dem Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desire is potential by definition and includes possible non-fulfilment; pure intention neither believes nor desires but does, treating the outcome as almost accomplished, like deciding to go buy a newspaper. Desire radiates at the frequency of a failure line; outer intention, already decided, at the frequency of the line where one has it. Two excess potentials block the goal: passionate desire at any cost and the struggle with doubt, each feeding the other. Intention must take the place of desire."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPureIntention: adds the frequencies of the failure line and the line of having, and the paired potentials of desire and doubt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLowerImportanceFirstCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Lower importance before outer intention"@en, "Wichtigkeit senken vor äußerer Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reducing the importance and emotional intensity tied to one's goals is required before any step toward working with outer intention."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One gets not a single step closer to outer intention; importance keeps one pressing on the world with inner intention." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotByInnerIntentionCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention cannot be learned by inner intention"@en, "Äußere Absicht lässt sich nicht mit innerer erlernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting an inner intention to learn outer intention, however strong, will never work; the force lies outside oneself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWorkingWithOuterIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionUnknownCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nature of outer intention admitted unknown"@en, "Wesen der äußeren Absicht eingestanden unbekannt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author confesses he does not know what outer intention is; only aspects can be witnessed: it emerges when heart and mind are in harmony, creating a resonance that carries one to the corresponding sector. Its origin is as unknowable as why God exists; one is to use it as one enjoys sunshine. Likened to gravity, which seizes one only on stepping off the roof."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityNeedsNoImportanceCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of heart and mind needs absence of importance"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand braucht Abwesenheit von Wichtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Giving oneself up to outer intention needs heart-mind unity, which is possible only without intense importance, since importance breeds doubt that blocks unity."@en ;
    skos:note "The dependent step is heart-mind unity, pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma, typed by part 2 of Stupen' II."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Doubt splits heart and mind; any unity reached is usually agreement in rejecting something, so outer intention fobs one off with what one neither needs nor wants." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityInRejectionCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity in non-acceptance"@en, "Einigkeit in der Ablehnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "When heart and mind agree only on rejecting something, outer intention delivers the unwanted; disharmony stems from the mind being held by pendulums, preconceptions pulling on the strings of importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: When heart and mind agree only on rejecting something, outer intention delivers the unwanted; disharmony stems from the mind being held by pendulums, preconceptions pulling on the strings of importance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoConditionsForOuterIntentionCh7 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two conditions for using outer intention"@en, "Zwei Bedingungen für den Gebrauch der äußeren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "First: unity of heart and mind. Second: lowering how intense importance is and dropping attachment to achieving the goal. Inner intention corresponds to deciding to act, outer intention to the decision to have."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Purifying intention of desire"@en, "Die Absicht vom Wunsch reinigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consider the goal. Doubts arising show desire; worrying whether one has the qualities and skills shows desire; even confident belief may hide it. Want and act without feeding the emotion of desire, like the plain intention to scratch one's head. To lower importance: set the intention, and at the very start accept possible failure; run the defeat scenario through a few times, think what you would do then, a fallback or safety net, and admit that failing would not be a catastrophe. Do this once only. Then think neither of failure nor success and simply move toward the goal as if walking to buy a paper."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingNewspaperAttitude: adds the diagnostics of desire and the one-time acceptance of defeat with a fallback."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDesireStillPresentCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs that desire is still present"@en, "Zeichen, dass noch Wunsch im Spiel ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doubts entering the mind, or worrying about having the needed qualities and skills, signal that desire, not pure intention, is at work; belief in success does not exclude it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Doubts entering the mind, or worrying about having the needed qualities and skills, signal that desire, not pure intention, is at work; belief in success does not exclude it; it bears on pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionPurifiedCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention purified of desire"@en, "Vom Wunsch gereinigte Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Resolute intention to have and act, free of excess potential, through which outer intention can work."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPurifyingYieldsPureIntentionCh7 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting defeat yields pure intention"@en, "Annahme der Niederlage bringt reine Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accepting possible failure at the outset is said to remove desire and importance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingIntentionPurifiedCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptDefeatFirstCh7 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Accept possible defeat to eliminate desire"@en, "Mögliche Niederlage annehmen, um den Wunsch zu tilgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desire is not eliminated unless the possibility of defeat is accepted."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingIntentionPurifiedCh7 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Desire, and with it excess potential, remains." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepTheIntentionCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Keep hold of the intention; no dwelling on failure"@en, "Die Absicht festhalten; nicht beim Scheitern verweilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "While purifying, do not lose grip on the intention itself; imagining defeat is a one-time act, revisiting failure in thought repeatedly is pointless; the exercise only frees one from needing the goal exactly as imagined, since how it comes is unknowable."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSuccessInTheBagCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success in the bag, next time if not this"@en, "Erfolg sicher, sonst beim nächsten Mal"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: moving on after accepting failure, success is as good as secured; if not, there is no cause for regret, and one will succeed the next time."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTearingOneselfApartCh7 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tearing oneself apart over a first failure"@en, "Sich über ein erstes Scheitern zerfleischen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The promised later success holds only so long as one does not torment oneself over the initial failure."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The promised later success holds only so long as one does not torment oneself over the initial failure; it bears on pmp:TranserfingPurifyingIntentionCh7."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotFoldingOneArmsCh7 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Letting go is not folding one's arms"@en, "Loslassen heißt nicht, die Hände in den Schoß zu legen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Surrender to outer intention does not mean dropping personal intentions and waiting at home for harmony to appear; usual means stay open, and removing desire and importance benefits inner intention too."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VII Intention, section 'The Purification of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II:
# Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), part 2: chapter VIII Slides and chapter IX
# The Heart and Mind.
#
# The work and the tradition are declared in traditions/transerfing.ttl; the
# harvest of Stupen' I stands in traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl and is
# linked, not repeated. This part types the shared system terms
# pmc:TranserfingSlayd, pmc:TranserfingDusha, pmc:TranserfingRazum,
# pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma, pmc:TranserfingFreyling and
# pmc:TranserfingAngelKhranitel; parts 1 and 3 link to them. Terms typed by
# parts 1 and 3 (pmc:TranserfingTsel, pmc:TranserfingDver) are only linked.
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 232 records, B 257;
# 29 records of B without counterpart in A: 1 added, 26 covered, 2 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 2 records both passes missed. Records whose
# claim a Stupen' I node already carries are not entered again; restatements
# with a difference carry a note "Differs from".
# What the author tells of others (the psychiatric patient, Toulouse-Lautrec,
# the privatisation winners, the teenage leaders) is third-party ascription;
# he tells no case of his own in these chapters. His corrections of the Bible,
# the Babel legend, evolutionary doctrine and common maxims are entered as
# concepts, since only his side is read.
#


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'Illusion'
#

pmc:TranserfingIllusionPerceptionOtherSectorsCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Illusion as perception of other sectors"@en, "Illusion als Wahrnehmung anderer Sektoren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dreams and hallucinations are held to arise from the soul travelling through the alternatives space; so-called illusions are glimpses of field sectors not yet materialised, and reality itself is not an illusion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Illusion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntoxicationPsychosisAttunementUnrealisedSectorsCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intoxication and psychosis as attunement to unrealised sectors"@en, "Rausch und Psychose als Einstimmung auf unrealisierte Sektoren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under drugs, alcohol or in psychosis awareness loses control and the subconscious tunes into unrealised regions of the alternatives space while the body stays in the material sector; the text says the mentally ill may be living an alternative reality rather than imagining it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Illusion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPeakHeartMindConflictShiftsPerceptionCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Peak heart-mind conflict shifts perception into a virtual sector"@en, "Gipfel des Konflikts von Herz und Verstand verlagert die Wahrnehmung in einen virtuellen Sektor"@de ;
    skos:definition "When heart and mind clash at their utmost and the soul cannot bear physical reality, perception is said to settle in a virtual region of the field while the body continues in the material one. Illustrated by a psychiatrist's case of a woman whose excessive importance placed on an ideal family ended in an abusive marriage, childlessness and a withdrawal into an imagined happy family."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Illusion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealisationRequiresHeartMindHarmonyWhyCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Realisation requires heart-mind harmony; why psychotic worlds stay virtual"@en, "Verwirklichung verlangt Einklang von Herz und Verstand; warum psychotische Welten virtuell bleiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "An alternative becomes physical when thought energy is emitted in full harmony of heart and mind; a psychiatric patient cannot hold that connection, and the gap between virtual and material sector may need too much energy. The author leaves room for unknown further reasons."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Illusion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPerceptionBoundedInformationAbsorbedChildhoodCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Perception bounded by information absorbed in childhood"@en, "Wahrnehmung begrenzt durch in der Kindheit aufgenommene Information"@de ;
    skos:definition "How a person perceives depends heavily on what was absorbed in childhood (kittens raised without vertical or without horizontal lines); the mind imagines only within the limits of accumulated experience."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOldBricks: Stupen' I says the mind cannot reach fundamentally new information; here perception itself is bounded by what was absorbed in childhood (the kitten experiment)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Illusion'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'
#

pmc:TranserfingSlayd a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Slide"@en, "Dia (Slide)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A slide is a warped image of reality kept in one's own head and absent from others': like film in a projector it bends the uniform light of the world (world = light, slide = worldview, screen = perception). It works two ways: it skews one's sense of one's place and of others' attitudes, and it distorts perception of the outer world."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: slayd (слайд)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersMostlyPreoccupiedThemselvesCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others are mostly preoccupied with themselves"@en, "Andere sind vorwiegend mit sich selbst befasst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most people are said to be about ninety percent occupied with themselves; only potential partners or competitors actually weigh one's appearance, and ugliness draws notice only at first meeting. Hence a slide about others' judgement is one's own construct."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDroppingImaginedScrutiny: there others' self-preoccupation grounds a practice of release; here it is why the slide of being watched lives only in one's own head."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSlideActedOutThroughBehaviourCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A slide is acted out through behaviour"@en, "Ein Dia wird über das Verhalten ausgespielt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The inferiority slide changes behaviour (awkward gestures, tense face, loss of clear thought), so the imagined picture is enacted in the material dimension."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProjectionDislikedOwnTraitsOntoOthersCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Projection of disliked own traits onto others"@en, "Projektion abgelehnter eigener Eigenschaften auf andere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dissatisfaction with oneself pushed into the subconscious is poured onto others; people tend to criticise in others what they dislike in themselves, though not in every case."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProjectionCheckYieldsRecognitionProjectionsCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Projection check yields recognition of projections"@en, "Projektionsprüfung ergibt Erkennen von Projektionen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Observing from the inner Guardian position is said to let one quickly spot projections."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCheckingWhetherAccusationProjectionCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingQuickRecognitionProjectionsHungCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCheckingWhetherAccusationProjectionCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Checking whether an accusation is a projection"@en, "Prüfen, ob ein Vorwurf eine Projektion ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking the inner Guardian stance during role plays, when someone accuses you unfairly or of being what you are not, ask whether the accuser carries that same trait; if you are truly innocent, the accuser probably projects a slide of their own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingQuickRecognitionProjectionsHungCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quick recognition of projections hung on oneself"@en, "Schnelles Erkennen von Projektionen, die einem angehängt werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to tell quickly whether another person is projecting onto you."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceFoundationEverySlideCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Importance is the foundation of every slide"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit ist die Grundlage jedes Dias"@de ;
    skos:definition "Slides rest on importance, especially on giving too much weight to others' opinions whose content one does not know; an unusual appearance becomes ugly only through the slide of importance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingToulouseLautrecCaseLettingGoImportanceCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Toulouse-Lautrec case: letting go of importance ended the slide"@en, "Fall Toulouse-Lautrec: Loslassen der Bedeutsamkeit beendete das Dia"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told case: the painter, depressed by his deformity, at the peak of distress accepted it and dropped its importance; the slide ceased, and he is said to have then had good fortune, artistic success and popularity with women."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDroppingImportanceSlideCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseNegativeSlideCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNegativeSlidesRealisedOuterIntentionCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Negative slides are realised by outer intention"@en, "Negative Dias werden von der äußeren Absicht verwirklicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "A negative slide is generally produced by unity of heart and mind, under which outer intention works without fault; it gradually carries the owner to a sector where the slide's content is fully expressed, while the slide lasts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNegativeSlidesIntensifyThemselvesCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Negative slides intensify themselves"@en, "Negative Dias verstärken sich selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning: what one worries about grows (weight, a birthmark, sense of inadequacy, guilt finds punishment); the pattern persists until importance is dropped or a positive slide replaces it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDwellingOnFlaws: there one cannot pass to the line of a fit body; here the worried-about trait actively grows, carried by outer intention while the slide persists."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingNegativeSlidesRealisedOuterIntentionCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDroppingImportanceSlideCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping the importance of a slide"@en, "Die Bedeutsamkeit eines Dias fallen lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop ascribing great weight to the matter the negative slide is built on (accept it and turn to life), so that the slide loses its foundation and collapses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDroppingImportanceDissolvesNegativeSlideCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping importance dissolves the negative slide"@en, "Fallenlassen der Bedeutsamkeit löst das negative Dia auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once importance goes, the negative slide is said to lose its base and stop working."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDroppingImportanceSlideCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReleaseNegativeSlideCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReleaseNegativeSlideCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Release from a negative slide"@en, "Befreiung von einem negativen Dia"@de ;
    skos:definition "State in which a negative slide has crumbled and stopped shaping perception and events."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Distorting Reality'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'
#

pmc:TranserfingEmbodyingChosenPositiveQualitiesCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Embodying chosen positive qualities"@en, "Verkörperung gewählter positiver Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Others perceive you in the light of your strongest sides; behaviour adjusts unconsciously to the slide and outer intention realises the depicted qualities, gradually."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Positive slide of oneself"@en, "Positives Dia von sich selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "(1) Take stock of your negative slides consciously: ask what you dislike in yourself or would hide. (2) Do not fight them; withdraw attention and significance from them and turn attention to your virtues and qualities you want. (3) Draw yourself as you wish to be, shining; love that image and embellish it with detail; it may be dynamic (movement, dress, manners, wit, how people warm to you, problem-solving). (4) Feed it into the mind and keep recreating it in thought, systematically and consecutively, until it becomes part of the personality and dissolves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPositiveSelfSlideYieldsEmbodiedQualitiesCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Positive self-slide yields embodied qualities"@en, "Positives Selbstdia ergibt verkörperte Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "The positive slide is said to work just as faultlessly as a negative slide: behaviour adjusts and outer intention fulfils the picture."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEmbodyingChosenPositiveQualitiesCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSlideDissolvesPersonalityCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The slide dissolves into the personality"@en, "Das Dia löst sich in der Persönlichkeit auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: with time the slide becomes an integrated part of the personality and stops existing as a slide; once the desire is achieved its importance vanishes and it melts away, and heart and mind are in harmony."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign: with time the slide becomes an integrated part of the personality and stops existing as a slide; once the desire is achieved its importance vanishes and it melts away, and heart and mind are in harmony."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartAcceptsSlideOnlyAfterSystematicCh8 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart accepts the slide only after systematic consolidation"@en, "Das Herz nimmt das Dia erst nach systematischer Festigung an"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart integrates the slide only if its image is consolidated systematically and repeatedly; the mind alone cannot do it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingEmbodyingChosenPositiveQualitiesCh8 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideCh8 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "If the mind tries to realise the slide by itself, the heart knows it is a game of masks." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionRealisesSlidesOnlyGraduallyCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention realises slides only gradually"@en, "Äußere Absicht verwirklicht Dias nur allmählich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not expect immediate realisation; it takes time and the effect builds up."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealisticStepsBeforeAbsoluteIdealCh8 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Realistic steps before the absolute ideal"@en, "Realistische Schritte vor dem absoluten Ideal"@de ;
    skos:definition "Begin with realistically achievable pictures and move toward the ideal over time; a fulfilled minimum order lets outer intention take on more complex tasks."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingEmbodyingChosenPositiveQualitiesCh8 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingStartingAttainableAspectAdmiredQualityCh8 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotCopyAnotherIntoSlideCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not copy another person into your slide"@en, "Keine andere Person ins Dia kopieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The slide must be your own, never a copy of someone you think already has the desired qualities."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingStartingAttainableAspectAdmiredQualityCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Starting from an attainable aspect of an admired quality"@en, "Mit einem erreichbaren Aspekt einer bewunderten Eigenschaft beginnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Translate an admired quality into an aspect usable at the start: bravery as resoluteness, beauty as charm, strength as dexterity, eloquence as listening, intellect as awareness, physical perfection as confidence."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingCompensatingFlaws: there another quality offsets a flaw; here an attainable aspect of an admired quality is the opening picture of a positive slide."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPositiveSlideAmongStrangersYieldsPeakCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Positive slide among strangers yields peak performance"@en, "Positives Dia unter Fremden ergibt Höchstleistung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Said to act faster and more strongly with new people, who have no prior image of you."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideAmongStrangersCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReachingMaximumPotentialSometimesRemarkableSuccessCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideAmongStrangersCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Positive slide with people who do not know you"@en, "Positives Dia bei Menschen, die einen nicht kennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "At an interview, contest, party or similar first encounter, boldly feed the slide into the mind, keep its picture constantly in awareness, disregard doubts such as fear it will fail, and drop the sense of having something to lose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrongWillToHaveFirstCh8 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Strong will to have"@en, "Starker Wille zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Maximum potential is reached only given a sufficiently strong will to have."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingReachingMaximumPotentialSometimesRemarkableSuccessCh8 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReachingMaximumPotentialSometimesRemarkableSuccessCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reaching maximum potential, sometimes remarkable success"@en, "Erreichen des höchsten Potenzials, mitunter außerordentlicher Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "With strong enough will to have, one is said to reach one's maximum potential and at times extraordinary success."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideTowardOutsideWorldCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Positive slide toward the outside world"@en, "Positives Dia gegenüber der Außenwelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adopt a filter that admits the good and blocks the bad: as at an exhibition, stop at what attracts you, pass the rest indifferently, and accept positive things with joy."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFilteringNews: there the filter is applied to news; here it is a positive slide held toward the whole outside world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNegativityNotPassedFollowsYouCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Negativity not passed by follows you"@en, "Nicht übergangene Negativität folgt einem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike at an exhibition, negativity not ignored is said to keep following you; joyfully accepted positivity does not leave."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWhatYouHateFollowsYou: there hatred binds one to its object; here failing to pass negativity by indifferently is enough, and joyfully accepted good stays as well."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideTowardOutsideWorldCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepPositiveSlidesMeasureCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Keep positive slides in measure"@en, "Positive Dias in Maßen halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner control keeps the distortion from a positive slide minor and beneficial, provided one avoids extremes like imagining oneself a Napoleon and remembers the danger of excess potential; negative-slide distortion by contrast can do great harm."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPositiveSlideCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Positive slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'
#

pmc:TranserfingPermissionHaveCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Permission to have"@en, "Erlaubnis zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fame, wealth and power go to those who first choose themselves and allow themselves to have; others confirm the choice later. A dream one cannot permit oneself does not happen. Outer intention needs the will to have: knowing rather than believing that it is one's choice and that one is worthy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotPermittingDreamCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not permitting oneself the dream"@en, "Sich den Traum nicht erlauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "A dream one does not permit oneself to have will not be realised; outer intention gives nothing to one not ready to have."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A dream one does not permit oneself to have will not be realised; outer intention gives nothing to one not ready to have."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingPermissionHaveCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDiscomfortExpensiveShopsShowsLackPermissionCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discomfort in expensive shops shows lack of permission"@en, "Unbehagen in teuren Geschäften zeigt fehlende Erlaubnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sign of not being ready: feeling uncomfortable or inhibited in an expensive shop means one does not yet permit oneself to own such things; with that fear the goal of wealth is not reached. It also generates importance potentials (desire, envy, inferiority, irritation)."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Sign of not being ready: feeling uncomfortable or inhibited in an expensive shop means one does not yet permit oneself to own such things; with that fear the goal of wealth is not reached. It also generates importance potentials (desire, envy, inferiority, irritation)."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingPermissionHaveCh8."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWantingVersusReadiness: there unease among the wealthy is put down to unfamiliarity and frequency; here it is read as the sign that permission to have is missing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfSuggestionAffordabilityFutileCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-suggestion of affordability is futile"@en, "Selbstsuggestion der Erschwinglichkeit ist vergeblich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to persuade oneself one can afford expensive things is useless; permission belongs to outer intention, not to convincing the mind."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingPermissionHaveCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerIntentionAloneAchievesNothingHereCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner intention alone achieves nothing here"@en, "Innere Absicht allein bewirkt hier nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner intention means resolving to act (find the money); confined to it, the mind gives a pragmatic verdict and nothing happens; outer intention needs the will to have."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLikeFirstRidingBikeWithoutStabilisersCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Like first riding a bike without stabilisers"@en, "Wie das erste Radfahren ohne Stützräder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of granted permission: doubt, hesitation and inner talk suddenly vanish, leaving wordless clarity of knowing."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign of granted permission: doubt, hesitation and inner talk suddenly vanish, leaving wordless clarity of knowing."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Will to have (knowing without words)"@en, "Wille zu haben (wortloses Wissen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "State of wordless clarity, knowing without belief, assurance without wavering, arising where heart and mind are at one, in which one feels one with the silent power governing the universe, which carries one to the sector where what heart and mind agree on is manifest."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Term of the English edition: will to have."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Widened comfort zone"@en, "Erweiterte Komfortzone"@de ;
    skos:definition "The implausible becomes comfortable: the thought that every dream can be reached stops causing unease, doubt melts, faith turns into knowledge, heart harmonises with mind, and then the will to have arises; one attunes to the life line on which the desired things belong to one."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingComfortZoneStagesTowardWillHaveCh8 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Comfort zone stages toward the will to have"@en, "Stufen der Komfortzone zum Willen zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sequence given: the dream stops causing unease, then doubt melts, faith becomes knowledge, heart harmonises with mind, and then the will to have arises."@en ;
    skos:note "No consequence of skipping a stage is named, so no pm:Presupposing pairs are entered."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneCh8 ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Each stage opens the next: once a dream no longer unsettles, doubt goes and faith becomes knowing; then the heart agrees with the mind, and out of that agreement the will to have appears." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamSlideYieldsWidenedComfortZoneCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dream slide yields widened comfort zone"@en, "Traumdia ergibt erweiterte Komfortzone"@de ;
    skos:definition "Slides teach the heart a new comfort zone and gradually bring heart-mind unity, like a fortress taken by long siege."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dream slide to widen the comfort zone"@en, "Traumdia zur Erweiterung der Komfortzone"@de ;
    skos:definition "Build the dream slide and keep it in awareness all the time; return to it again and again, refining and adding details; live it from inside as a participant, not watching it like a film on a screen; keep it in the background whatever you do until seeing it is a habit; take active interest in and absorb information about the dream's object; enact it in real life, if only formally (e.g. in expensive shops choose calmly without looking at prices, treat goods as soon to be bought, pretend ownership, play a discerning buyer without superiority)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAdmittingWealthIntoComfortZone: there only wealth is let into the comfort zone; here any dream is built as a slide lived from inside, the shop exercise being one example."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnsystematicSlideBringsNoResultCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unsystematic slide brings no result"@en, "Unsystematisches Dia bringt kein Ergebnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "A slide yields results only if reproduced methodically over time; viewing it like a flat film image is not very effective."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A slide yields results only if reproduced methodically over time; viewing it like a flat film image is not very effective."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSuperiorityBuyerRoleCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Superiority in the buyer role"@en, "Überheblichkeit in der Käuferrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "When playing the discerning buyer, be careful not to act superior."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLettingDreamLayerAttunesLifeLineCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the dream into one's layer attunes to its life line"@en, "Das Ersehnte in die eigene Schicht lassen stimmt auf seine Lebenslinie ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting desired things into the layer of one's world is said to tune one gradually to the life line on which they belong to one; outer intention finds an unforeseen way."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotAskHowCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not ask how, do not explain away"@en, "Nicht nach dem Wie fragen, nicht wegerklären"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not worry how the wanted things will arrive; when outer intention delivers unexpectedly, do not dismiss it as coincidence or mysticism."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDoNotAskWhyAndHow: there one should not ask how the method works; here one should not ask how the wanted things will arrive."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExpelAweDreamWorldCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Expel awe for the dream world"@en, "Ehrfurcht vor der Traumwelt vertreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any sense of awe for the dream must be driven out: inner and outer importance block heart-mind unity; the dream world should feel joyful yet ordinary, as if already had."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRussianOligarchsPermissionHaveBroughtWealthCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Russian oligarchs: permission to have brought wealth"@en, "Russische Oligarchen: Erlaubnis zu haben brachte Reichtum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told case: during privatisation at the end of the 1980s those near the resources who felt no guilt, doubt or inferiority and permitted themselves to have are said to have received the wealth through outer intention, while equally talented others got nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Told case of others (Russian privatisation at the end of the 1980s). No practice is described, so it is not entered as pm:Yielding; the case attests the will to have (pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8) as the deciding factor."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Widening Your Comfort Zone'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'
#

pmc:TranserfingPilgrimCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pilgrim"@en, "Pilger"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who will not settle for an average life; not fortune's chosen one, rather the Pilgrim chooses fortune; toppling common sense is said to make anything attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Term of the English edition: Pilgrim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVisualisationUnreliabilityCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualisation and its unreliability"@en, "Visualisierung und ihre Unzuverlässigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualisation, picturing the goal in detail and carrying it in mind, is said to be closest to Transurfing among unconventional methods and to weigh as much as the physical process of reaching the goal; common techniques work only sometimes. The author claims that, practised by its rules, the Transurfing variant is a no-fail technique."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeCommonTypesVisualisationCh8 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three common types of visualisation"@en, "Drei gängige Arten der Visualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author's classification: (1) the dream, weakest and useless for transformation; (2) the film, conscious viewing of the realised wish; (3) a third type (given in the following text). Transurfing adds its own."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDaydreamingDoesNotComeTrueCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Daydreaming does not come true"@en, "Tagträumen erfüllt sich nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dreams do not come true: dreamers do not really expect realisation, lacking belief or any intent to possess and act; their goal is the dreaming itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Dreams do not come true: dreamers do not really expect realisation, lacking belief or any intent to possess and act; their goal is the dreaming itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingThreeCommonTypesVisualisationCh8."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWishIsNotChoice: there dreams fail because a wish is no choice; here because the dreamer neither expects realisation nor intends to have and act."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFilmVisualisationWithoutOwnershipDeliversSomeoneCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Film visualisation without ownership delivers someone else's goal"@en, "Filmvisualisierung ohne Besitz liefert das Ziel eines anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the film type one watches the wish realised but not oneself in it; the order is fulfilled literally, so one sees the same house belonging to someone else. Called the key mistake most practitioners make: the film stays a film they never enter."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: In the film type one watches the wish realised but not oneself in it; the order is fulfilled literally, so one sees the same house belonging to someone else. Called the key mistake most practitioners make: the film stays a film they never enter."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingThreeCommonTypesVisualisationCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Participatory visualisation (third type)"@en, "Teilnehmende Visualisierung (dritte Art)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Play a role in the film instead of observing it: create a virtual waking dream of the goal and act in it with all senses as if it were already yours (for a house: walk the rooms touching things, sit by the fire and feel warmth and smell smoke, add logs, check the fridge, sleep in the bed, eat with family, hold a house-warming, move furniture, touch the grass, plant flowers, pick and eat an apple), never with the awe of a longing dreamer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationWidensComfortZoneMaterialisesCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Participatory visualisation widens the comfort zone and materialises"@en, "Teilnehmende Visualisierung erweitert die Komfortzone und materialisiert sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting in the visualised material is said to set thought energy to the matching life line; this slide widens the comfort zone and in time will certainly materialise, at an unknown date."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMaterialisationMayTakeLongCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Materialisation may take long"@en, "Die Materialisierung kann lange dauern"@de ;
    skos:definition "No one can say when the slide materialises; one may wait long, and even a top-quality slide is slow when the goal sits in a remote sector relative to the current life line."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlayingSlideForgettingCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Playing with the slide and forgetting it"@en, "Mit dem Dia spielen und es vergessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one plays with the slide briefly and then forgets it, little can be expected; there are no miracles."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If one plays with the slide briefly and then forgets it, little can be expected; there are no miracles."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLostPassionOrForcedPracticeCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lost passion or forced practice"@en, "Verlorene Leidenschaft oder erzwungene Übung"@de ;
    skos:definition "If passion for the goal fades it dissipates; if one must force oneself to work with it one soon tires of it, and should ask whether the slide is really needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If passion for the goal fades it dissipates; if one must force oneself to work with it one soon tires of it, and should ask whether the slide is really needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPerseveranceUntilVisualisingBecomesHabitCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Perseverance until visualising becomes habit"@en, "Beharrlichkeit, bis das Visualisieren Gewohnheit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention brings one closer gradually; patience is needed throughout and perseverance only at first, until visualising the slide is a habit and no longer needs reminding."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a caution by the integrator: pass A had it as an order whose prior step the text does not name."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalMixedUpPendulumsCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal mixed up with pendulums"@en, "Mit Pendeln vermischtes Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the goal is not one's own but entangled with pendulums, the heart-mind unity needed to achieve it cannot be generated."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the goal is not one's own but entangled with pendulums, the heart-mind unity needed to achieve it cannot be generated."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingImposedGoal: here the reason is named: a goal tied to pendulums cannot produce the heart-mind unity the slide needs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWholeHeartedStrivingMakesSlideVisualisationCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Whole-hearted striving makes slide visualisation succeed"@en, "Ganzherziges Streben lässt die Diavisualisierung gelingen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one strives toward the goal with all one's heart, visualising the slide is said to definitely bring results; once a real will to have is present, outer intention finds the way."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingParticipatoryVisualisationThirdTypeCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'
#

pmc:TranserfingVisualisingEndGoalMoneySuitcaseNeverCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualising the end goal (money suitcase) never works"@en, "Visualisieren des Endziels (Geldkoffer) wirkt nie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualising a suitcase of money, however faithfully, is said to bring no result ever. Two errors: money is an attribute, not the true goal; and attention fixed on the end goal does not move one toward it unless one is already a single step away (the comfort zone widens, but outer intention is not helped)."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Visualising a suitcase of money, however faithfully, is said to bring no result ever. Two errors: money is an attribute, not the true goal; and attention fixed on the end goal does not move one toward it unless one is already a single step away (the comfort zone widens, but outer intention is not helped)."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingVisualisationUnreliabilityCh8."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMoneyAsAttribute: the attribute thesis is applied to visualisation, and a second error is added: attention on the end point moves one only when one is a step away."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDesireVersusIntentionVisualisationCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Desire versus intention in visualisation"@en, "Wunsch gegenüber Absicht in der Visualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desire is attention on the goal, intention is attention on movement toward it; intention, not desire, drives action. Hence visualising the goal is the work of desire, a dummy run; what moves one forward is visualising the process, with the goal only as background."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNamerenie: intention is defined here as attention on movement toward the goal, and the distinction becomes the rule to picture the process rather than the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingArmRaisingDemonstrationDesireIntentionCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Arm-raising demonstration of desire and intention"@en, "Armheben als Vorführung von Wunsch und Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "First think of wishing to lift your arm and picture it raised (nothing happens: desire); then raise it and keep it up (intention acting throughout, attention on the process with the goal as final image)."@en ;
    skos:note "Demonstration exercise; it shows a distinction rather than yielding a capacity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingVisualisingProcessCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualising the process"@en, "Visualisierung des Prozesses"@de ;
    skos:definition "Picture the process of moving toward the goal, on the premise that it must be reached because intention is at work, with the goal only as backdrop. During breaks from a work imagine it steadily improving: today some details, tomorrow new touches, its birth, growth and perfection in your own hands (like a mother tending and admiring her growing child). Examples: a program growing more effective and impressing tomorrow; a business project receiving new ideas daily; a body fed, trained and imagined gaining tone and muscle."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingProcessFocus: there attention moves onto the action being done; here the growth of the work is pictured in imagination between work sessions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingMovementAlongLifeLinesCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing movement along life lines"@en, "Bewegung entlang der Lebenslinien sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forward reference: studying the chapter titled Forward to the Past is said to teach one even to perceive one's movement along life lines."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Practice lies in another chapter outside this part."@en ;
    skos:note "Forward reference to a later chapter; no practice is given here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWorkDoesNotCreateItselfCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The work does not create itself"@en, "Das Werk erschafft sich nicht selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not picture the work painting or building itself; you are its maker and it reaches perfection in your hands."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingVisualisingProcessCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProcessVisualisationQuickensOuterIntentionCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Process visualisation quickens outer intention"@en, "Prozessvisualisierung beschleunigt die äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualising the process, unlike contemplating the result, is said to significantly speed outer intention and effect the physical shift to the target line."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVisualisingProcessCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAcceleratedOuterIntentionTowardGoalCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceleratedOuterIntentionTowardGoalCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accelerated outer intention toward the goal"@en, "Beschleunigte äußere Absicht auf das Ziel hin"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tangible movement toward the goal (slower in waking than in dreams) and a marked quickening of outer intention's work; inner and outer intention are united."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCalmSlideWorkWhenMeansUnknownCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Calm slide work when the means are unknown"@en, "Ruhige Diaarbeit, wenn der Weg unbekannt ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "If you do not know how the goal can be reached, keep visualising the slide calmly and systematically, drop importance, do not rush about seeking a way, trust the alternatives flow; watch and live the slide and right action follows automatically, even subconsciously."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBeingPresentedMeansGoalCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being presented with the means to the goal"@en, "Den Weg zum Ziel vorgelegt bekommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention offers a suitable means once the goal fits the comfort zone; the slide nudges toward the needed actions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMaterialRealisationInertLikeResinCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Material realisation is inert like resin"@en, "Materielle Verwirklichung ist träge wie Harz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The material realising of the alternatives space is sluggish, so the transition must be gradual, meaning continuous and progressive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMessianicMasteryOuterIntentionInstantTransitionCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Messianic mastery of outer intention (instant transition)"@en, "Messianische Meisterschaft der äußeren Absicht (sofortiger Übergang)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mentioned as the exception to gradual realisation: one who commands outer intention like a messiah need not move gradually through the inert material realisation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Only mentioned; no practice given here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Visualising the Process'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'
#

pmc:TranserfingVisualisingProcessDistantStageCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Visualising the process of a distant stage"@en, "Den Prozess eines fernen Abschnitts visualisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualising movement along a stretch of the path one would not naturally walk yet tempts one to jump ahead and rush, which is ineffective, causes frustration that sets balancing forces against one, and can get one lost. Picturing the distant end as a slide does no harm."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingVisualisingProcessCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTransferChainCh8 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transfer chain"@en, "Übergangskette"@de ;
    skos:definition "The consecutive path to a distant goal through the alternatives space; each link is a stage of interconnected, fairly homogeneous sectors (e.g. finish studies, find work, polish skills). The path consists of transfer chains plus the alternatives flow; the space is ordered, so an unordered path never arrives."@en ;
    skos:note "Term of the English edition: transfer chain."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCompletedCurrentLinkCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Completing the current link"@en, "Abschluss des gegenwärtigen Glieds"@de ;
    skos:definition "Finishing the stage of the transfer chain one is now on, such as a first degree before a master's, before moving to the next."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered by the integrator as the prior step of pmc:TranserfingEachLinkRequiresCompletionPreviousCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEachLinkRequiresCompletionPreviousCh8 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Each link requires completion of the previous one"@en, "Jedes Glied verlangt den Abschluss des vorigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One cannot move to a stage without completing the one immediately before it (no master's before a first degree); one cannot attune directly to life lines far from the current coordinates."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step pmc:TranserfingCompletedCurrentLinkCh8 is entered by the integrator."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingTransferChainCh8 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingCompletedCurrentLinkCh8 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "A path to the goals built in unordered fashion will never reach them." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingVisualisingCurrentLinkOnlyTransurfingVisualisationCh8 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualising the current link only (Transurfing visualisation)"@en, "Nur das aktuelle Glied visualisieren (Transurfing-Visualisierung)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Final definition: mentally picture the realisation process of the current link of the transfer chain only, while the end result may be held as a slide as often as liked; do not hurry; live the link's realisation in thought and action. Together with: create no excess potential, do not slap the water, do not fight the current."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCurrentLinkVisualisationMovesTargetLineCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Current-link visualisation moves one to the target line"@en, "Visualisierung des aktuellen Glieds bewegt auf die Ziellinie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living out the link's realisation in thought and action is said to achieve the goal; the push of a mental image continues by momentum."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVisualisingCurrentLinkOnlyTransurfingVisualisationCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAcceleratedOuterIntentionTowardGoalCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalInsideComfortZoneBeforeMeansCh8 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal inside comfort zone before means appear"@en, "Ziel in der Komfortzone, bevor der Weg erscheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "The means are offered only once the comfort zone has widened enough to include the goal."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingBeingPresentedMeansGoalCh8 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCalmSlideWorkYieldsMeansCh8 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Calm slide work yields the means"@en, "Ruhige Diaarbeit ergibt den Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Systematic calm slide work is said to lead outer intention to present the means."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCalmSlideWorkWhenMeansUnknownCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBeingPresentedMeansGoalCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsRelateOnlyCurrentLinkCh8 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Signs relate only to the current link"@en, "Zeichen betreffen nur das aktuelle Glied"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sign seeming to point to the goal concerns only the road currently walked; with several chains between oneself and the goal, signs of the distant goal cannot be read reliably from here."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignInterpretationLeastReliableTechniqueCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign interpretation is the least reliable technique"@en, "Zeichendeutung ist die unzuverlässigste Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on method reliability: apart from a negative answer of the inner voice, interpreting signs is said to be Transurfing's least reliable technique and should not be given much weight."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNotSignsEverywhere: here reading signs is ranked as the least reliable technique of all, the negative answer of the inner voice excepted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDivisionLabourBetweenGoalSlideProcessCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Division of labour between goal slide and process visualisation"@en, "Arbeitsteilung zwischen Zieldia und Prozessvisualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Goal visualisation in any convenient form is called essential: held as a slide it widens the comfort zone and tunes thought energy to the target line, its sole function. The physical shift is done by process visualisation, the workhorse, which unites inner with outer intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'Transfer Chains'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. VIII Slides, section 'SUMMARY'
#

pmc:TranserfingNothingComesWithoutWillToHaveCh8 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nothing comes that does not trigger the will to have"@en, "Nichts kommt, was den Willen zu haben nicht auslöst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Summary rule: nothing comes to one that fails to awaken one's will to have."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Summary rule: nothing comes to one that fails to awaken one's will to have."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. VIII Slides, section 'SUMMARY'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'
#

pmp:TranserfingBeingCleanSheetCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Being a clean sheet"@en, "Ein unbeschriebenes Blatt sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Close the eyes, stop the inner chatter and contemplate blackness, so that for a short while the mind is empty; then imagine the social environment, Earth, sun, past and future gone and yourself alone in empty space, and ask what remains of the self."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingContemplatingEmptiness: there emptiness is regarded to hear intuition; here it shows that a sense of self remains once thought and social identity are removed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingContemplatingBlacknessYieldsMomentWithoutThoughtCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Contemplating blackness yields a moment without thought"@en, "Betrachten der Schwärze ergibt einen Moment ohne Gedanken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contemplating blackness with chatter stopped is said to let one not think for a short time."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBeingCleanSheetCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBriefThoughtlessStateIntactSelfSenseCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBriefThoughtlessStateIntactSelfSenseCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Brief thoughtless state with intact self-sense"@en, "Kurzer gedankenfreier Zustand mit erhaltenem Selbstgefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "For a moment the mind is completely empty yet one's sense of being a whole self persists."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDusha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The soul (heart)"@en, "Die Seele (Herz)"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the working division of the psyche, everything unconscious is the heart or soul, which may also be called the subconscious; its province is feeling (elation, openness, inspiration, oppression, depression). It is present from birth, understands feelings and wordless thought but not words, knows without reasoning, and can merge with outer intention yet lacks will of its own."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: dusha (душа); the English edition says heart or soul."@en ;
    skos:note "The author declares the question of the soul's eternal existence beside the purpose of the method; one may call it the subconscious."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingReasonAndHeart: there only the division is made; here the soul is given feeling, wordless knowing and kinship with outer intention, but no will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRazum a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind"@en, "Der Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the working division of the psyche, everything conscious is the mind; its province is thought. It is acquired with society's concepts and words, holds the will and governs inner intention, but cannot rule outer intention; it is said to be wholly ruled by pendulums that impose narrowing beliefs and a fixed template of perception."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: razum (разум); the English edition says mind or reason."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingReasonAndHeart: there only the division is made; here the mind is given will and inner intention and is placed under pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDropOceanCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drop and ocean"@en, "Tropfen und Ozean"@de ;
    skos:definition "A person is a drop of spray briefly separated from the ocean; separated it cannot feel oneness or draw the ocean's energy, and believes itself separate until it falls back. Water's many forms share one essence, which the particle finds hard to see. Near-death reports of serenity and bliss from oneness with the cosmos are read as the drop rejoining the ocean, the whole energy of the ocean then passing through it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOneSpirit: there each being holds a fragment of God; here the image is the drop that forgets its sameness with the ocean and regains it near death."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImageLikenessMisreadCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Image and likeness misread"@en, "Ebenbild missverstanden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explicit reinterpretation of the Bible: the statement that God made man in his image is true but usually distorted by the mind; the likeness lies in shared essence (water in drop and ocean), not in having a head, hands and feet."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit dispute with a named tradition or received view; only the author's side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnlightenmentOnenessWorldCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enlightenment: oneness with the world"@en, "Erleuchtung: Einssein mit der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The common goal of religious schools: oneness with the world, melting into the energy ocean. The enlightened master is said to have all the universe's energy at disposal, sees no basic difference between self and infinity, and their intention becomes identical with outer intention. People say the Buddha attained this in life."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "The author explicitly declines it as a task: too hard and unnecessary for personal goals; no meditation retreat needed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFeelingWindOuterIntentionCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the wind of outer intention"@en, "Den Wind der äußeren Absicht spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sensing outer intention as clearly as air or water currents; needed to travel through the space purposefully. Outer intention lifts a person like a kite of the right shape and carries them to the sector matching their thought energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessOnenessBeforeGraspingOuterIntentionCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of one's oneness before grasping outer intention"@en, "Bewusstsein des Einsseins, bevor die äußere Absicht fassbar wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "As long as one is unaware of one's essence and of being one with the ocean, how outer intention works stays out of reach."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFeelingWindOuterIntentionCh9 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEnlightenmentOnenessWorldCh9 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Outer intention stays beyond one's grasp." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSteeringOuterIntentionWillLimitedCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Steering outer intention by one's will (limited)"@en, "Äußere Absicht nach eigenem Willen lenken (begrenzt)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Compelling outer intention to one's will to a small degree, enough to fulfil personal desires and realise best rather than worst expectations."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLoopholeHeartMindUnityCommandsOuterCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The loophole: heart-mind unity commands outer intention"@en, "Das Schlupfloch: Einheit von Herz und Verstand lenkt die äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind has will but cannot rule outer intention; the heart can be one with it but has no will and drifts like an uncontrolled kite. Unity of heart and mind suffices to bring outer intention under one's will, to a small but sufficient degree; called difficult yet realistically achievable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartMindUnityBeforeControlOuterCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart-mind unity before control of outer intention"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand vor der Lenkung der äußeren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Heart-mind unity is stated to suffice for placing outer intention under one's will."@en ;
    skos:note "The next section, 'The Heart's Sail', restates the pair: union of heart and mind is called essential, after which the heart's sail catches outer intention's wind."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingSteeringOuterIntentionWillLimitedCh9 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeyConditionsMasteryOuterIntentionCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Key conditions for the mastery of outer intention"@en, "Schlüsselbedingungen der Meisterung der äußeren Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recalled from the chapter on Intention: awareness, lowered importance, and releasing the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Restates the key conditions of ch. VII Intention: awareness, lowered importance and releasing the goal; the third is held in part 1 of this Stupen' and is not linked here."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingSteeringOuterIntentionWillLimitedCh9 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wind of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'
#

pmc:TranserfingTemplatePerceptionCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Template of perception"@en, "Wahrnehmungsschablone"@de ;
    skos:definition "From childhood attention is trained on separate elements, and the mind channels data through an established template describing the world; what lies outside it (e.g. the energy field of another person) the mind keeps the eyes from seeing. The world does not in itself look like anything; only perceivable manifestations can be spoken of."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingAurasCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing auras"@en, "Auren sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visual perception of the energy field (aura) is acknowledged as possible in theory but said to be poorly developed because it was left out of the childhood template."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Mentioned only; no practice given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSoulIlliterateCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The soul is illiterate"@en, "Die Seele ist analphabetisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consciousness is acquired from society's concepts; the soul is there from birth and does not understand words, only feelings. Thoughts precede words and are the language the subconscious understands."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingHeartFeelsAndKnows: it adds that thought comes before words and is the language the subconscious understands."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotAddressSubconsciousIntellectLanguageCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not address the subconscious in the intellect's language"@en, "Das Unterbewusste nicht in der Sprache des Intellekts ansprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Communicating with the subconscious in intellectual language is pointless."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingSoulIlliterateCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingArtLanguageHeartCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Art as the language of the heart"@en, "Kunst als Sprache des Herzens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Works made with love and passion speak wordlessly to everyone; technically perfect works from the mind stay empty. The smile of the Mona Lisa is likened to the Buddha's, recalling the forgotten feeling of oneness."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOldBricks: here art made with love is the heart's own wordless language, set against technically perfect but empty work of the mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRightDoorBeforeMasterpieceCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The right door before the masterpiece"@en, "Die richtige Tür vor dem Meisterwerk"@de ;
    skos:definition "A masterpiece follows from doing what suits one's soul (going through one's own door)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingCreatingMasterpieceCh9 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingDver ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatingMasterpieceCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating a masterpiece"@en, "Ein Meisterwerk schaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who walks toward the deepest dream through the right door, doing what best suits the soul, is said to become capable of a masterpiece; only the heart makes an original, the mind a perfect copy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTowerBabelDistortedAccountCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tower of Babel as distorted account"@en, "Turmbau zu Babel als verzerrter Bericht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Babel legend is said to distort the atrophy of the soul's language after human language arose; most myths are read as truths filtered through mental constructs, the tower perhaps standing for the power gained by expressing will consciously in words."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit dispute with a named tradition or received view; only the author's side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartSailCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The heart's sail"@en, "Das Segel des Herzens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart senses outer intention's wind but cannot set a sail; the mind's will can. Once the two were easily joined; the mind's focus on its own worldview cost it knowledge of outer intention, which it can regain only through connection with the heart, which knows directly from the information field without analysis."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Heart's Sail'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'
#

pmc:TranserfingHeartAlreadyHoldsEverythingWizardOzCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The heart already holds everything (Wizard of Oz)"@en, "Das Herz hat schon alles (Zauberer von Oz)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like the Oz characters, one already has the desired qualities and needs only to permit oneself to have them; a ritual may serve to strengthen faith (Ellie needed to put her whole will into wanting to have). The heart is said to have access to all knowledge and humanity's past achievements."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsSeparateHeartMindCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums separate heart from mind"@en, "Pendel trennen Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums profit from uniform adherents; conditioning from childhood suppresses individuality, so people cannot say what they want or know their capacity. Breaking the heart's link to the mind suffices to suppress mastery of outer intention; religion, science, industry and media have widened the split, called humanity's greatest loss."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGeniusLevelOriginalCreationAchievementCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Genius-level original creation and achievement"@en, "Geniale ursprüngliche Schöpfung und Leistung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ability to create remarkable art, make unique discoveries, reach phenomenal results in sport, business or any field, as the geniuses did by turning to their hearts."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGenius: there genius is thought free of pendulums; here it is open to anyone who turns to the heart."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningHeartYieldsGeniusCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Turning to the heart yields genius"@en, "Zuwendung zum Herzen ergibt Genialität"@de ;
    skos:definition "All great geniuses are said to have succeeded through turning to their hearts; whoever does the same can do likewise."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTurningHeartPermittingCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingGeniusLevelOriginalCreationAchievementCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTurningHeartPermittingCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning to the heart and permitting oneself"@en, "Sich dem Herzen zuwenden und sich erlauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take as an axiom that the heart already holds all it requires, and permit yourself to use it; embrace the knowledge of being worthy and capable of what you want with all your heart; ignore the reasonable arguments of convention and pendulums against your goal and shield yourself with the conviction that heart and mind together can do anything; begin by believing in the heart's unlimited possibilities, then turn the mind to face it."@en ;
    skos:note "The source orders the steps: first believe in the heart's unlimited possibilities, then turn the mind toward it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstHardestBattleCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against 'the hardest battle is with oneself'"@en, "Gegen „der schwerste Kampf ist der mit sich selbst“"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explicit rejection of the common maxims that overcoming the self is hardest and of a Russian saying about stifling one's own song for others' sake: called among the greatest delusions of humankind, since negativity is only dust on the surface and a pure heart lies beneath."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit dispute with a named tradition or received view; only the author's side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRemovingMasksAllowingCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Removing the masks, allowing oneself to be oneself"@en, "Die Masken ablegen, sich erlauben, man selbst zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of trying to change yourself, wipe off the dust and remove the masks pendulums impose, permitting yourself to be the unique being you are; make sure the mind lets the heart create."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBeingOneself: here the obstacle is named as masks put on by pendulums, and being oneself is set against every attempt at self-change."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTryingChangeYourselfMakesNewMaskCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Trying to change yourself makes a new mask"@en, "Sich ändern wollen erzeugt eine neue Maske"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-change is futile; it only creates another mask."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingRemovingMasksAllowingCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnmaskingRevealsHeartTreasureCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Unmasking reveals the heart's treasure"@en, "Demaskierung legt den Schatz des Herzens frei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Removing the imposed masks is said to reveal the treasure of the heart, which alone produces ingenious creation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRemovingMasksAllowingCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingGeniusLevelOriginalCreationAchievementCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Wizard Within'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'
#

pmc:TranserfingStarWorshipPersonalStarSectorCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Star worship and the personal star sector"@en, "Starkult und der eigene Stern-Sektor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums light up stars to spur adherents to serve harder and hide that everyone has unique abilities. Every soul has its own star sector in the field (conditionally one goal or path) where its qualities manifest fully; the heart's potential cannot be realised in a sector not its own."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPendulumFavourites: there favourites are exploited tools; here star worship makes the mass of adherents work harder and hides that each has a star sector."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingHeartFindOwnPathCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the heart find its own path"@en, "Das Herz den eigenen Weg finden lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind forgets other people's experience, acknowledges how extraordinary the heart is and lets it find its path unhindered; treat role models only as demonstration copies, not as yardsticks; your soul is the yardstick, explore its qualities in your present sector; rather admire a photo of yourself than of an idol; reject others' experience and permit yourself to be a star; listen to the heart, not the mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCrowdInstinctCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Crowd instinct cuts off individuality"@en, "Herdentrieb schneidet die Eigenart ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "Teenagers, still new to the world, are said to be especially open to pendulums: mixing with the crowd feels safer, but the herd instinct cuts the shoots of individuality, so most adopt one style and one slang while believing themselves independent."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered from pass B (reconciliation)."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingCommonFieldHerdInstinct ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTeenagersWhoPermitThemselvesBecomeLeadersCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Teenagers who permit themselves become leaders"@en, "Jugendliche, die sich erlauben, werden Anführer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Among teenagers the few who permit themselves to reveal the soul's hidden qualities are said to become leaders, mavericks and later trendsetters."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLettingHeartFindOwnPathCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBecomingStarOwnSectorCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnPathMakesStarCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own path makes one a star"@en, "Eigener Weg macht zum Star"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one stops trying to be like others or repeating their scripts, everything is said to work out; others must then agree with one's brilliance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLettingHeartFindOwnPathCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBecomingStarOwnSectorCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGreatActorsPlayThemselvesCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Great actors play themselves"@en, "Große Schauspieler spielen sich selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Putting on a mask is easy; removing it and being oneself is the hardest role, and doing so turns role play into life on the stage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsSeedOppressiveThoughtsAboutLackingCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums seed oppressive thoughts about lacking talent"@en, "Pendel säen bedrückende Gedanken über fehlendes Talent"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums cannot stop one but can instil thoughts that a star must be beautiful, talented, able to sing, and that one lacks it; celebrities in fact have many flaws."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLettingHeartFindOwnPathCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIndividualityBeforeBirthStarCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Individuality before the birth of a star"@en, "Individualität vor der Geburt eines Stars"@de ;
    skos:definition "Individuality is named as indispensable for a star to be born; copying never made anyone a star."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingBecomingStarOwnSectorCh9 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingRemovingMasksAllowingCh9 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Wearing an existing star's mask makes one at most a copy, at worst a parody." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChasingAnotherGoalEndsDisappointmentCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chasing another's goal ends in disappointment"@en, "Das Ziel eines anderen verfolgen endet in Enttäuschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being provoked onto another pendulum hook into chasing someone else's goal will only lead to disappointment."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Being provoked onto another pendulum hook into chasing someone else's goal will only lead to disappointment."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingLettingHeartFindOwnPathCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBecomingStarOwnSectorCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a star in one's own sector"@en, "Ein Star im eigenen Sektor werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Manifesting one's soul's qualities in one's own sector so that pendulums must accept one as a favourite; leaders, mavericks and trendsetters arise this way."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Mirage'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'
#

pmc:TranserfingAngelKhranitel a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Guardian Angel"@en, "Schutzengel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to exist if one believes in it, thoughts making it real (possibly an informational-energetic being created by thought); it may also exist regardless of belief, love and guard us, and be weakened by neglect while we give energy to pendulums. It cares for its ward alone, knows what to shield one from, has no form of its own (imagine it as cherub, cloud, bird, or identify it with the soul), needs our energy without asking, and is not subject to balanced forces."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: angel-khranitel' (ангел-хранитель)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGuardianAngel: Stupen' I only refers to the Angel; here what it is held to be is set out, including that it may exist whether believed in or not and is not touched by balancing forces."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Guardian Angel" ;
    pm:nameRole "a protective being of one ward, perhaps an informational-energetic being made real by thought" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCultivatingGuardianAngelCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cultivating one's Guardian Angel"@en, "Den eigenen Schutzengel pflegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Think of your Angel, address it confidently and gratefully, love it sincerely and thank it for every small help; picture it in whatever form is comfortable; share loneliness with it; remind it constantly that you love and thank it; never neglect it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTurningToTheGuardianAngel: Stupen' I only refers to the practice; here the procedure is given: love, gratitude and a freely chosen form."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSupportProtectionStrengthenedAngelCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Support and protection by a strengthened Angel"@en, "Unterstützung und Schutz durch einen gestärkten Engel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Angel grows stronger and supports, guides and rewards one generously; knowing it is there steadies confidence and gives inner calm."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCommunicatingAngelCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Communicating with one's Angel"@en, "Mit dem eigenen Engel kommunizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "People with extrasensory abilities are said to be able to communicate with their Angel; others are guided anyway."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Mentioned only; no practice given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTakeOffenceOrAngryCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not take offence at or be angry with the Angel"@en, "Dem Engel nicht grollen oder zürnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not reproach or get angry with the Angel; compared with it one is a blind kitten and does not know what misfortunes it averts."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCultivatingGuardianAngelCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPrideSuccessCreatesExcessPotentialCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pride in success creates excess potential"@en, "Stolz auf Erfolg erzeugt Überschusspotenzial"@de ;
    skos:definition "Praising oneself is better than self-reproach, but being very pleased with oneself can create a little excess potential, enough for balanced forces to spoil the celebration with an error or unpleasantness."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGuiltPaidWithPunishment: there pride after a good deed brings punishment; here only strong self-satisfaction makes a little potential, and self-praise still beats self-reproach."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingSelfLoveAndVanity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGivingPrideAngelCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving the pride to the Angel"@en, "Den Stolz dem Engel übergeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "When delighting in a success, remember the Angel and celebrate together: talk to it, praise and thank it unsparingly and sincerely, count the success as its merit; keep the joy, hand over the pride."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThankingAngelDissolvesPridePotentialCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thanking the Angel dissolves pride's potential"@en, "Dank an den Engel löst das Potenzial des Stolzes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Considering the success the Angel's merit is said to dissipate excess potential while leaving the joy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGivingPrideAngelCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRejoicingSuccessWithoutExcessPotentialCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRejoicingSuccessWithoutExcessPotentialCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rejoicing in success without excess potential"@en, "Sich ohne Überschusspotenzial über Erfolg freuen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The excess potential of pride dissipates while one celebrates in the heart without caution."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThankingPendulumCostsEnergyCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Thanking a pendulum costs energy"@en, "Dank an ein Pendel kostet Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "One may thank a pendulum that helped, but it always takes a portion of one's energy; better to give thanks to the Angel."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingGivingPrideAngelCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLoveGratitudeStrengthenAngelCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Love and gratitude strengthen the Angel"@en, "Liebe und Dank stärken den Engel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more sincerely the Angel is loved and thanked, the stronger it becomes and the more it helps; constant reminders of love make it reward one handsomely."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCultivatingGuardianAngelCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSupportProtectionStrengthenedAngelCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Guardian Angels'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'
#

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsFeedNegativeEmotionRivalryCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums feed on negative emotion and rivalry"@en, "Pendel nähren sich von negativen Gefühlen und Rivalität"@de ;
    skos:definition "A pendulum arises from a group's shared thoughts and actions, then lives independently, compelling adherents through informational-energetic exchange and harvesting energy from dissatisfaction, irritation, anger, worry, fear and battles between pendulums; without them the world would hold much happiness and little suffering."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMayatnik: here the pendulum's food is named as negative emotion and rivalry, and a world without pendulums is said to hold much happiness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNaturalSelectionNotNecessaryConditionLifeCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Natural selection is not a necessary condition of life"@en, "Natürliche Auslese ist keine notwendige Bedingung des Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explicit dispute with the received evolutionary view that the struggle for survival and natural selection are essential to life's development: they drive an aggressive kind of development, but life could grow by more humane laws and a positive script where whoever feels good survives."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit dispute with a named tradition or received view; only the author's side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomPendulumsLifeCelebrationCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from pendulums for a life as celebration"@en, "Freiheit von Pendeln für ein Leben als Fest"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living life as a feast requires freeing oneself from binding pendulums and seeking one's own goal and door; union of heart and mind then brings anything wished for."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFreedomOfChoice ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromPendulum ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingTsel ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingDver ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBreakingOutConditioningBoxCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking out of the conditioning box"@en, "Aus der Schachtel der Konditionierung ausbrechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Refuse to believe those who say you must work for others' good, that all comes from hard work alone, that you must fight for your place, what your place is, that a sect needs your contribution, that you must stay poor, or that your options are limited. When pendulums provoke, do not respond, keep importance minimal and act consciously; if thrown off balance, find where you inflated importance and change your relation to it; remember the pendulum, not you, craves importance; take what is yours calmly without insistence; when a pendulum tries to hook you, chuckle and firmly lower importance, until this is habit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsStrikeWhenWillHaveAppearsCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums strike when the will to have appears"@en, "Pendel schlagen zu, wenn der Wille zu haben erscheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "As soon as the will to have shows, pendulums arrange situations to make one accept limited options, upset one's plans when one feels strong, and hook in when one grows calm."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBombardmentWhenChanging: there the trigger is changed behaviour; here it is the first sign of the will to have."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingBreakingOutConditioningBoxCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEffortTenacityWrongResponseCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Effort and tenacity are the wrong response"@en, "Anstrengung und Zähigkeit sind die falsche Antwort"@de ;
    skos:definition "The situation calls for keeping importance at zero, not massive effort; a failure should not be made important either."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingBreakingOutConditioningBoxCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSoulBoxCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The soul box"@en, "Die Seelenschachtel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Limitations and conditioning cram the soul into a box with the convention-captured mind as jailer; the box is made of the importance one attributes. Pendulum power rests on the importance and unawareness of adherents; the conditioning drains energy, sets balanced forces against one, leads to false goals and lets outer intention realise worst expectations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnySlackImportanceLosesGameCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Any slack to importance loses the game"@en, "Jedes Nachgeben gegenüber Bedeutsamkeit verliert das Spiel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The moment one gives importance any slack, one loses the pendulum game; pendulums wait for one's spirits to fall."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The moment one gives importance any slack, one loses the pendulum game; pendulums wait for one's spirits to fall."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingBreakingOutConditioningBoxCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingZeroImportanceAwarenessYieldFreedomChoiceCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Zero importance and awareness yield freedom of choice"@en, "Null-Bedeutsamkeit und Bewusstheit ergeben Wahlfreiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "With importance at zero and awareness of the game, pendulums are said to be unable to hook in or enforce scripts, and the clay golem falls apart."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBreakingOutConditioningBoxCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomOfChoice ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFeelingStrengthOnceLoweringImportanceHabitCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling one's strength once lowering importance is habit"@en, "Die eigene Stärke spüren, wenn das Senken der Bedeutsamkeit Gewohnheit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: when reducing importance at every hook has become habit, one feels one's strength and understands one can determine the script oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign: when reducing importance at every hook has become habit, one feels one's strength and understands one can determine the script oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingBreakingOutConditioningBoxCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Soul Box'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'
#

pmc:TranserfingFreyling a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fraile"@en, "Frail (Fraile)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The soul's unique set of parameters, modelled as its characteristic frequency, unique like a snowflake; it manifests implicitly under the intellect's masks and is the wordless integral image of a person beyond character, habits and looks. When, with heart-mind unity, thought energy matches a sector's frequency, outer intention moves one there."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: freyling (фрейлинг); the English edition writes 'fraile'."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRadiantCharmBeautyHarmonyCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Radiant charm (beauty of harmony)"@en, "Strahlender Charme (Schönheit der Harmonie)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Indefinable charm and beauty radiating from within, unlike doll-like conventional beauty; said to lie not in the heart but in harmony between heart and mind, an inner light showing the mind is tuned to the soul's fraile; it can provoke envy (people ask why one looks so radiant)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfLoveBeforeRadiatingCharmCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-love before radiating charm"@en, "Selbstliebe vor dem Ausstrahlen von Charme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only one who is happy, has learned to love themselves, enjoys life and does what they want radiates the inner light."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRadiantCharmBeautyHarmonyCh9 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingLearningLoveCh9 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Anyone self-critical, resentful of their work, inwardly turbulent or in conflict with their soul can never radiate charm." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingListeningStringsFraileCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Listening for the strings of fraile"@en, "Auf die Saiten des Frail horchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Notice when a passing remark or a seen thing strikes a chord and draws you with a vague, repeated urging (the soul's outer intention without aim); listen to these dictates of the heart so that the mind picks them up and gives them direction. Fraile may also show as a hobby or anything done with love."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeedingHeartLetsCatchOuterIntentionCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Heeding the heart lets one catch outer intention"@en, "Auf das Herz hören lässt die äußere Absicht ergreifen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Listening to the heart's dictates so the mind can follow is said to give quick achievement."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingListeningStringsFraileCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCatchingOuterIntentionQuicklyAchievingDesireCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCatchingOuterIntentionQuicklyAchievingDesireCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Catching outer intention and quickly achieving a desire"@en, "Die äußere Absicht ergreifen und einen Wunsch rasch erreichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the mind takes up the heart's urging, one can seize outer intention and achieve the desire quickly."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTryingMakeFraileFitStandardsCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trying to make fraile fit standards"@en, "Das Frail an Normen anpassen wollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Comparing oneself with pendulum standards, the mind finds faults, hates itself and the heart, tries on masks or tries to change fraile; nothing good comes of it, the rift widens. If heart and mind agree on negating the imagined flaws, outer intention moves one to a line where they materialise."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Comparing oneself with pendulum standards, the mind finds faults, hates itself and the heart, tries on masks or tries to change fraile; nothing good comes of it, the rift widens. If heart and mind agree on negating the imagined flaws, outer intention moves one to a line where they materialise."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingFreyling."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindTunedFraileYieldsCharmCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mind tuned to fraile yields charm"@en, "Auf das Frail gestimmter Verstand ergibt Charme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tuning the mind to the fraile of the heart by self-love is presented as the only way to the inner light of charm."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLearningLoveCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRadiantCharmBeautyHarmonyCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLearningLoveCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning to love oneself"@en, "Sich selbst lieben lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Convince the mind that the heart deserves love above all; love yourself first, then attend to others' virtues. Knock outer importance off its pedestal by ceasing to worship others' standards and creating your own; release inner importance by no longer forcing yourself to follow them; remember that pendulums, not you, need importance; accept yourself unconditionally as you are; start today with a favourite treat, a private party, tender care for yourself."@en ;
    skos:note "The source orders the steps: love oneself first, only then attend to the virtues of others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfLoveNotComplacencyMustUnconditionalCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-love is not complacency and must be unconditional"@en, "Selbstliebe ist keine Selbstgefälligkeit und muss bedingungslos sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-love must not be confused with vanity or complacency, which come from feeling superior and create dangerous excess potential; conditional self-love also turns into excess potential."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSelfLoveAndVanity: it adds that self-love must be unconditional, since conditional self-love itself turns into excess potential."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLearningLoveCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotLikingExcessPotentialCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not liking oneself is excess potential"@en, "Sich nicht mögen ist Überschusspotenzial"@de ;
    skos:definition "For one who fought their fraile too long, the objection that one cannot love what one does not even like is called pure excess potential from heightened outer importance (taking others' standards as truth) and inner importance (forcing oneself to follow them)."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLearningLoveCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLifeLineFullSelfAcceptanceUnsuspectedCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life line of full self-acceptance and unsuspected qualities"@en, "Lebenslinie voller Selbstannahme und ungeahnter Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention carries one to life lines of total self-acceptance where one truly has something to be proud of; liking oneself regardless is said to outwit outer intention and reveal qualities one never suspected."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfLoveYieldsSelfAcceptanceNewCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-love yields self-acceptance and new qualities"@en, "Selbstliebe ergibt Selbstannahme und neue Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one loves one's heart with all one's mind and thought energy radiates self-acceptance, outer intention is said to carry one there."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLearningLoveCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingLifeLineFullSelfAcceptanceUnsuspectedCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLoveYourNeighbourYourselfPresupposesSelfCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love your neighbour as yourself presupposes self-love"@en, "Liebe deinen Nächsten wie dich selbst setzt Selbstliebe voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading of the commandment: its usual emphasis on loving the neighbour overlooks that it presumes love for oneself already exists. The Holy Grail is said to be one's own fraile."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Fraile'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'
#

pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of heart and mind"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Agreement of the mind's will and the heart's striving on one matter. In it thought energy takes the nature of outer intention, which carries one to the sector of what both agree on; it suffices to bring outer intention under one's will. It arises by itself in strong feelings, mostly negative, so it is to be reached deliberately for one's chosen goal and the resolve to have and act; called difficult but realistically attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: edinstvo dushi i razuma (единство души и разума)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingHeartAsAlly: there the heart only stops fighting the mind; here the unity is what makes outer intention controllable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindForbidsHeartToyCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind forbids the heart's toy"@en, "Der Verstand verbietet dem Herzen das Spielzeug"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under pendulum conditioning the mind handles the heart like a child in a toy shop and answers that there is no money, putting a taboo on the dream though the heart asked for the toy, not money, and would wait. The mind should have agreed; outer intention would have found how. Heart-mind agreement arises mostly in negation, fear and hatred."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAllowingHaveCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Allowing oneself to have"@en, "Sich zu haben erlauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing oneself to have is called the chief condition for the fulfilment of wishes: brush away pendulum prejudice, believe you deserve the dream, and it will come."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingAchievingWhatOneWants ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingPermissionHaveCh8 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindGovernsInnerHeartGovernsOuterCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mind governs inner, heart governs outer intention"@en, "Der Verstand lenkt die innere, das Herz die äußere Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Alone the heart cannot aim outer intention; merged with the mind it becomes controllable for definite goals. What seems unattainable is indeed unattainable by inner intention alone. Happiness and unhappiness both come down to unity or disunity of heart and mind, and discord grows with age."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPostponingDreamLifetimeCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Postponing the dream for a lifetime"@en, "Den Traum ein Leben lang aufschieben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind finds ever more proof the dream is hard and defers it; the deferral usually lasts a lifetime and the dream ends in a dusty box."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The mind finds ever more proof the dream is hard and defers it; the deferral usually lasts a lifetime and the dream ends in a dusty box."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmc:TranserfingMindGovernsInnerHeartGovernsOuterCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIdentifyGoalBeforeSeekingUnityCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Identify the goal before seeking unity"@en, "Das Ziel bestimmen, bevor man Einheit sucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "To reach unity of heart and mind, first determine what they should agree on, i.e. one's goals."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "There can be no unity of heart and mind while the mind chases a mirage while the heart yearns for something different." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding one's true goal"@en, "Das wahre Ziel finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deliberately set aside quiet time; recall the heart's childhood longings, what attracted you, which dreams you gave up; ask whether that goal still draws you, whether it is false, whether you want it wholeheartedly or only want to want it. While considering it, ignore prestige (lowers outer importance) and how to reach it (lowers inner importance); attend only to how comfortable it feels, imagining you already have it: does the heart sing or feel weighed down?"@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeightenedImportanceDistortsGoalChoiceCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Heightened importance distorts goal choice"@en, "Erhöhte Bedeutsamkeit verzerrt die Zielwahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "High outer importance makes a goal look prestigious and unattainable (perhaps a pendulum hook); high inner importance makes it seem beyond one's abilities and attractive for that reason."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartSingsThoughtGoalCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The heart sings at the thought of the goal"@en, "Das Herz singt beim Gedanken an das Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of a true goal: the heart sings when one thinks of it; doubts about feasibility do not mean the goal is unneeded."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign of a true goal: the heart sings when one thinks of it; doubts about feasibility do not mean the goal is unneeded."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeavinessHeartMarksFalseGoalCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heaviness in the heart marks a false goal"@en, "Schwere im Herzen kennzeichnet ein falsches Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "However attractive, a goal that brings a heavy feeling in the heart may be false."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: However attractive, a goal that brings a heavy feeling in the heart may be false."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWantingNothingWeakLifeForceOrCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wanting nothing: weak life force or boxed heart"@en, "Nichts wollen: schwache Lebenskraft oder eingesperrtes Herz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having no goal or desire signals either weak vitality or that the mind has finally shut the heart in its box; the heart itself cannot want nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Having no goal or desire signals either weak vitality or that the mind has finally shut the heart in its box; the heart itself cannot want nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCareHealthYieldsVitalityCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Care of health yields vitality"@en, "Gesundheitspflege ergibt Vitalität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Better health care is offered as the way to raise vitality and desire."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRaisingVitalityThroughCareHealthCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingVitalityZestLifeCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRaisingVitalityThroughCareHealthCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Raising vitality through care of health"@en, "Lebenskraft durch Gesundheitspflege steigern"@de ;
    skos:definition "When desirelessness stems from weak life force, look after your health better; when healthy, life is a pleasure and one wants to experience everything."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVitalityZestLifeCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Vitality and zest for life"@en, "Vitalität und Lebenslust"@de ;
    skos:definition "Healthy life force in which life is pleasurable and one wants everything at once."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPuttingFirstCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Putting oneself first"@en, "Sich selbst an die erste Stelle setzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the heart is boxed, love yourself, stop overdoing care for others, put yourself first and care for yourself with tenderness, attention and enthusiasm, so the soul warms and spreads its wings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfSacrificeBoxesHeartCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-sacrifice boxes the heart"@en, "Selbstaufopferung sperrt das Herz ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shutting away the heart by serving others, even loved ones, creates strong excess potential of hidden unfulfilment that spills into trials for oneself and those close; seemingly good deeds then do more harm overall."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPuttingFirstCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstChangeYourselfSucceedCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against 'change yourself to succeed'"@en, "Gegen „ändere dich, um erfolgreich zu sein“"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explicit rejection of the common advice to work on or change oneself when things fail: called the pendulums' favourite recipe, meaning turn from yourself and do as they do. Transurfing instead recommends accepting oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Explicit dispute with a named tradition or received view; only the author's side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAgainstSelfImprovement: here the advice to change oneself is called the pendulums' favourite recipe, meaning to turn from oneself and follow their rule."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFalseGoalsBringNothingOrWrongCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "False goals bring nothing or the wrong place"@en, "Falsche Ziele bringen nichts oder an den falschen Ort"@de ;
    skos:definition "The soul rejects false aims; working toward them either achieves nothing or arrives where one finally sees one did not want to be."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The soul rejects false aims; working toward them either achieves nothing or arrives where one finally sees one did not want to be."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAcceptingHeedingHeartCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting oneself and heeding the heart"@en, "Sich annehmen und dem Herzen folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rather than changing yourself, accept yourself; turn from the husks pendulums impose and draw the mind's attention to the heart; heed its dictates while consciously lowering importance; allow yourself to have."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBeingOneself: here acceptance is joined to drawing the mind's attention to the heart and heeding it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfAcceptanceHeedingHeartYieldWhatCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-acceptance and heeding the heart yield what the heart desires"@en, "Selbstannahme und Achten auf das Herz ergeben, was das Herz begehrt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following this path one is said to receive anything the heart desires."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAcceptingHeedingHeartCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRustleMorningStarsCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rustle of the morning stars"@en, "Rascheln der Morgensterne"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart's voice: a vague, furtive presentiment of unease despite the mind's reassurances, as against mental tension whose cause the mind knows and can solve. The soul is said to see the sectors a mental decision will realise and to answer positively or negatively."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingRustleOfTheMorningStars: here the heart's vague unease is set apart from mental tension, whose cause the mind knows and can deal with."@en ;
    skos:note "Term of the English edition: rustle of the morning stars."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHabitNotingInnerPeaceYieldsHearingCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Habit of noting inner peace yields hearing the heart"@en, "Gewohnheit, die innere Ruhe zu beachten, ergibt das Hören des Herzens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text says this habit is the only way to learn to hear the morning stars rustle."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCheckingLevelInnerPeaceDecisionsCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRecognisingTheInnerNo ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCheckingLevelInnerPeaceDecisionsCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Checking the level of inner peace at decisions"@en, "Den Grad innerer Ruhe bei Entscheidungen prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make a habit of noting your inner peace. At each decision first hear reason, then the heart's feeling once the mind has decided; a vague inner tension is the heart's no. If you missed it, recall afterwards the first fleeting feeling at the moment of decision; an oppressive feeling beneath optimistic reasoning means no. When the heart answers no while the mind answers yes, boldly refuse where possible; if it must be, act as well as you can."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingHeartCheck: it adds recalling afterward the first fleeting feeling, and the rule to decline whenever heart answers no while mind answers yes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTrustPremonitionsEventsCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not trust premonitions of events"@en, "Vorahnungen von Ereignissen nicht trauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Felt premonitions of particular events deserve little trust because the mind may misread the heart's information; only inner tension reacting to a decision is reliable, and inner peace does not guarantee a yes (the heart may simply be indifferent)."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCheckingLevelInnerPeaceDecisionsCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartWantsNoHarmCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The heart wants nothing bad"@en, "Das Herz will nichts Schlechtes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart is said to be unable to want anything bad; this is the ground for following its no against the mind's yes wherever one can."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator's own reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityGoalsThenUnityDecisionHaveCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity on goals, then unity on resolving to have and to act"@en, "Einheit über die Ziele, dann Einheit im Entschluss zu haben und zu handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "After agreement on goals comes agreement in resolving to possess and to act, the mind's inner intention fusing with the heart's outer intention; acting within inner intention while steering outer intention makes the goal as good as reached. When the means are unclear, strengthen the resolve to possess, since outer intention is stronger and finds a way."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingSteeringOuterIntentionWillLimitedCh9 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrongFeelingsUniteHeartMindCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Strong feelings unite heart and mind"@en, "Starke Gefühle vereinen Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Strong feelings usually join heart and mind (adoration, hostility, fear, worst expectations), giving passion; the same unity must be reached for the decision to have."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartSingsMindRubsHandsCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart sings, mind rubs its hands"@en, "Das Herz singt, der Verstand reibt sich die Hände"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of unity on a correctly chosen goal: passionate joy in which both heart and mind are satisfied."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign of unity on a correctly chosen goal: passionate joy in which both heart and mind are satisfied."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingTellingInhibitionInnerTensionSlidesCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTellingInhibitionInnerTensionSlidesCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling inhibition from inner tension with slides"@en, "Hemmung und innere Spannung mit Dias unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Judge the goal only by whether thinking of it feels good or bad, not by prestige, feasibility or method. Shyness or reluctance before the unfamiliar (can this really be for me?) is inhibition; inner tension feels like dejection, chore, oppressive responsibility, apprehension. Work slides to widen the comfort zone; if they ease the feeling it was inhibition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSlidesDoNotEaseFeelingGenuineCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Slides do not ease the feeling: genuine inner tension"@en, "Dias lindern das Gefühl nicht: echte innere Spannung"@de ;
    skos:definition "If creating slides does not relieve the inhibition, it is a negative gut sense of inner tension; then honestly decide whether the goal is really essential."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If creating slides does not relieve the inhibition, it is a negative gut sense of inner tension; then honestly decide whether the goal is really essential."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingTellingInhibitionInnerTensionSlidesCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Unity of Heart and Mind'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'
#

pmc:TranserfingThreeTypesPerceptionCh9 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three types of perception"@en, "Drei Wahrnehmungstypen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author's division of perception into auditory, visual and kinetic; no one is a pure type, so affirmations suit auditory people best but anyone can use them."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation as a sound slide"@en, "Affirmation als Klangdia"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeat the goal as a positive statement aloud or silently, with these rules: (1) feel the content while repeating, since the heart ignores words; (2) one narrow goal per affirmation; (3) avoid monotony, bring fresh feeling to each series; (4) address the cause, not the effect, and first remove the cause; (5) phrase it positively toward the wanted result and specifically; (6) use the present tense, as if already had; (7) repeat it dispassionately, relaxed, in a zero-emotion state. Can be combined with visual slides into one integrated slide (e.g. sitting by the crackling fire in the new home, rain outside, a treat beside you, saying I feel comfortable, living the scene)."@en ;
    skos:note "Affirmation is attributed to some spiritual development practices; Zeland adapts it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAffirmationWorksLikeSlideCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation works like a slide"@en, "Affirmation wirkt wie ein Dia"@de ;
    skos:definition "Affirmations are said to act like slides, best when repeated without passion and relaxed; then the mind may reach the subconscious."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindlessRepetitionHasNoEffectHeartCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mindless repetition has no effect on the heart"@en, "Gedankenloses Wiederholen wirkt nicht auf das Herz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Words mean nothing to the heart, so mechanical repetition does nothing; feeling something once beats repeating it a thousand times."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Words mean nothing to the heart, so mechanical repetition does nothing; feeling something once beats repeating it a thousand times."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAffirmationsFail: there self-talk fails because one cannot fool oneself; here because the heart has no grasp of words, so feeling must go with them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMonotonousAffirmationsLoseMeaningCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Monotonous affirmations lose meaning"@en, "Eintönige Affirmationen verlieren Bedeutung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Constantly repeating the same phrase without fresh feeling soon empties it of meaning; desire must be nurtured, whereas intention acts at once (be confident with intent)."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Constantly repeating the same phrase without fresh feeling soon empties it of meaning; desire must be nurtured, whereas intention acts at once (be confident with intent)."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAffirmingAgainstEffectWhileCauseRemainsCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirming against an effect while its cause remains"@en, "Gegen eine Wirkung affirmieren, solange die Ursache bleibt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Affirming freedom from fear while the cause of worry is still present is pointless."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Affirming freedom from fear while the cause of worry is still present is pointless."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFutureTenseAffirmationNeverArrivesCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Future-tense affirmation never arrives"@en, "Affirmation im Futur kommt nie an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Phrased in the future tense, the goal never becomes present but stays an oasis just ahead."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Phrased in the future tense, the goal never becomes present but stays an oasis just ahead."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerPeaceCannotOrderedCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Inner peace cannot be ordered"@en, "Innere Ruhe lässt sich nicht bestellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner peace comes from heart-mind harmony on a specific issue, not from general abstract autosuggestion; a slide can teach and soothe the heart instead."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEmotionPressureRuinAffirmationCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Emotion and pressure ruin affirmation"@en, "Gefühl und Druck verderben die Affirmation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any emotion destroys balance; the subconscious cannot be persuaded or ordered, and hammering a thought in makes the heart plug its ears. A mind that must desperately convince the heart does not believe it either."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAffirmationSoundSlideCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAssertivenessMistakenWillHaveCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Assertiveness mistaken for will to have"@en, "Durchsetzungsdrang mit dem Willen zu haben verwechselt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The will to have cannot be generated on an emotional high; mistaking assertiveness for it leads one to spin in place, take a pendulum's hand and be dropped back into indecision. A will to have that is free of wanting gives the pendulum no hook."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWillToHaveCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'Sound Bite Slides'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'
#

pmc:TranserfingInnerMonologueApparentSilenceCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner monologue and the apparent silence"@en, "Innerer Monolog und die scheinbare Stille"@de ;
    skos:definition "The so-called inner dialogue is a monologue of the mind; it drowns the silent heart so intuition is rare. Quieting it does give access to intuition, but in waking it cannot be fully switched off: apparent emptiness is the mind still alert and watching, its silence deafening. It is truly muted only in sleep or deep meditation, which helps only with lucid dreaming or deep meditation that keeps consciousness."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMindDoesNotListen: it adds that stilling the monologue while awake only seems to work, since the watching mind stays alert."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTrainingOuterIntentionLucidDreamingCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Training outer intention in lucid dreaming"@en, "Äußere Absicht im Klartraum üben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lucid dreaming is said to serve as an experimental way to train the skill of outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Refers back to ch. VII; no new practice here."@en ;
    skos:note "Restates ch. VII Intention, where lucid dreaming is set out; the practice pmp:TranserfingLucidDreaming is typed in part 1."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWindowOntoAlternativesSpaceCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The window onto the alternatives space"@en, "Das Fenster zum Variantenraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the mind slackens control for an instant (a micro-sleep said to happen several times a day unnoticed), a narrow window opens and the heart sees the sector behind the mind's current thoughts; its knowledge breaks into consciousness as intuition, the inner voice, or a solution out of a hat. Revelation, the missing link logic cannot supply, arrives from the alternatives space via the heart."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingReleasingControlForIntuition: here the loosening is a micro-sleep several times a day, and the heart sees the sector behind the mind's current thought."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFeelingDistractedMomentsYieldsIntuitionCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling in distracted moments yields intuition"@en, "Fühlen in abgelenkten Momenten ergibt Intuition"@de ;
    skos:definition "In those moments the heart's knowledge is said to be easy to intuit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFeelingInsteadThinkingWhenMindDistractedCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingIntuitiveKnowing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFeelingInsteadThinkingWhenMindDistractedCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling instead of thinking when the mind is distracted"@en, "Fühlen statt Denken, wenn der Verstand abgelenkt ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whenever the mind is distracted, do not think; feel intuitively the elusive sense that arises."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindMustAttendSoulImpressionWakingCh9 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mind must attend to the soul's impression on waking"@en, "Der Verstand muss beim Erwachen den Eindruck der Seele beachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intuitive knowledge is received only if, on waking from the micro-sleep, the mind notices and remembers the soul's brief impression; usually it ignores it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingIntuitiveKnowing ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingFeelingInsteadThinkingWhenMindDistractedCh9 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLingeringAnxietyRealisesWorstExpectationsCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Lingering anxiety realises worst expectations"@en, "Anhaltende Angst verwirklicht die schlimmsten Erwartungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Vexation (anxiety, guilt, burdensome responsibility, depression) unites heart and mind on worst expectations; outer intention then shifts one to bad life lines, misfortunes come in runs, and an induced shift can trap one in long bad luck. The heart helps materialise the misfortune it foresaw."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWorryBreedsFailure: here the mechanism is named: lingering vexation unites heart and mind on the worst expectation, and outer intention realises it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingWindowOntoAlternativesSpaceCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningOuterIntentionBestExpectationCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning outer intention to one's best expectation"@en, "Die äußere Absicht auf die beste Erwartung richten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention can be used to advantage by uniting heart and mind on the best expectation: drop importance and negativity and direct thought energy consciously at the goal, e.g. with slides."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'A Window onto the Alternatives Space'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'
#

pmc:TranserfingFrameWindowPropelsRealisationCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Frame in the window propels realisation"@en, "Rahmen im Fenster treibt die Verwirklichung voran"@de ;
    skos:definition "A slide placed through the open window is said to make the mind touch outer intention and to move material realisation far."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrameInsertingSlideOpenWindowCh9 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingStrongPushMaterialRealisationThroughWindowCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPremonitionOrCauseTransitionalZoneCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Premonition or cause: the transitional zone"@en, "Vorahnung oder Ursache: die Übergangszone"@de ;
    skos:definition "Between an intuitive premonition and the event shaped by outer intention lies a transitional zone; whether one foresaw the event or subconscious thought induced it is left open, both said to have their place. The event tends to materialise especially when mind and heart agree."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRunningSlideWhileFallingAsleepOrCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Running a slide while falling asleep or in dreams"@en, "Ein Dia beim Einschlafen oder im Traum abspielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Running the slide in bed before sleep or even in a lucid dream does not work for material realisation and brings one no step closer to the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Running the slide in bed before sleep or even in a lucid dream does not work for material realisation and brings one no step closer to the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPaperBoatFrigateWhyDreamIntentionCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paper boat and frigate: why dream intention does not materialise"@en, "Papierboot und Fregatte: warum Traumabsicht nicht materialisiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "In dreams outer intention works flawlessly and instantly but its only function is to move the soul between virtual sectors, with the sail of material realisation lowered. In waking the mind anchors the heart in the material sector; a slide sets the frigate's sail, whose size depends on the strength of heart-mind unity, and outer intention works slowly until realisation arrives. Inertia is explicitly not the reason."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSlideLucidDreamingWidensComfortZoneCh9 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Slide in lucid dreaming widens the comfort zone"@en, "Dia im Klartraum erweitert die Komfortzone"@de ;
    skos:definition "For lucid dreamers the slide in sleep can widen the comfort zone, its only function there, which is enough."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of the slide run in a lucid dream (pmp:TranserfingLucidDreaming, typed in part 1)."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDreamSlideWidenComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneCh8 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSimpleMetaphorsCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Simple metaphors for complex processes"@en, "Einfache Metaphern für verwickelte Vorgänge"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author defends describing outer intention with plain images (paper boat, frigate, sail): they are said to convey the essence more clearly, and the mind's stock of symbols is said to hold no apter analogies."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on the status of the model's descriptions."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator's own reading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrongPushMaterialRealisationThroughWindowCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Strong push of material realisation through the window"@en, "Starker Schub der materiellen Verwirklichung durch das Fenster"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deliberately sending information into the target sector instead of receiving randomly; the mind touches outer intention. Because heart-mind connection is strongest at that instant and the sail of material realisation is still up, a gust of intention moves realisation a considerable distance; premonitions are induced intentionally."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFrameInsertingSlideOpenWindowCh9 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The frame: inserting a slide into the open window"@en, "Der Rahmen: ein Dia ins offene Fenster setzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "(1) Pay consistent attention to intuition and self-observation until you notice the window opening during the day. (2) With the mind actively involved, develop a slide of the goal event realised; run it over until you clearly sense the final feeling of fulfilment. (3) Take one integral frame from it (signing a contract and feeling content, the teacher shaking your hand after the exam, breasting the tape) and give it a one-word title as a hook (Victory, Yes, I did it). (4) When the mind dozes off and the window opens, quickly throw in the frame as feeling, not words, ideally as the dozing mind notices its state and before it fully wakes. (5) Repeat patiently despite failures until it is habit."@en ;
    skos:note "The source prescribes the order of steps 2 to 4 (frame first, then rehearsal with a hook, only then insertion at the open window); they are steps of one practice with no nodes of their own, so no pm:Sequencing is entered."@en ;
    skos:note "Term of the English edition: frame."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindWakesSlamsWindowCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mind wakes and slams the window"@en, "Der Verstand erwacht und schlägt das Fenster zu"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the dozing mind is involved, setting about the insertion wakes it and the window shuts instantly; the knack comes with time, patience and strong intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Because the dozing mind is involved, setting about the insertion wakes it and the window shuts instantly; the knack comes with time, patience and strong intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingFrameInsertingSlideOpenWindowCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFrameTechniqueOptionalInformationalCh9 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Frame technique is optional and informational"@en, "Rahmentechnik ist freiwillig und nur zur Information"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-warning: the frame is more complex than the other techniques and described mainly for information; if it does not work at once it may not be for you, and you should use standard slides and process visualisation. The habit of attending to the window is still useful."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFrameInsertingSlideOpenWindowCh9 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMoreFrequentIntuitiveInsightsCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "More frequent intuitive insights"@en, "Häufigere intuitive Einsichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: once one learns to catch the open window, intuitive insights come more often."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign: once one learns to catch the open window, intuitive insights come more often."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingFrameInsertingSlideOpenWindowCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'The Frame'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'SUMMARY'
#

pmc:TranserfingFocusingMeansKillsGoalCh9 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Focusing on the means kills the goal"@en, "Fokus auf die Mittel tötet das Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Summary rule: attention to the means lets the mind cross out a goal that is still elusive."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Summary rule: attention to the means lets the mind cross out a goal that is still elusive."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingFindingTrueGoalCh9."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. IX The Heart and Mind, section 'SUMMARY'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II
# (2004), part 3: chapter X Goals and Doors.
#
# The work and the tradition are declared in traditions/transerfing.ttl. This
# part types the shared system terms pmc:TranserfingTsel, pmc:TranserfingDver
# and pmc:TranserfingChuzhayaTsel; it links to the terms typed by the other
# parts and to the Stupen' I harvest (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl)
# instead of re-creating them. Two independent extraction passes ran over the
# text (A 192 records, B 163; 7 records of B without counterpart in A:
# 0 added, 6 covered, 1 not owed); a reader of the whole part added
# 3 records both passes missed. 8 records restate a Stupen' I node unchanged
# and are not written; 34 nodes restate one with a difference and say so.
# Identifiers minted here end in X10 (chapter X) to stay clear of the other
# parts until the merge.
#


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'
#

pmc:TranserfingChuzhayaTsel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Other people's goal (foreign goal)"@en, "Fremdes Ziel (Ziel anderer Menschen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A goal that is not one's own but is pressed on a person by pendulums or by other people; however attractive it looks, it is said to end only in disappointment and depletion, never in happiness, and to keep happiness in an illusory future. The chapter opens by setting out to tell such goals apart from what the soul truly strives for."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: chuzhaya tsel' (чужая цель)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOutcomeChasingFalseGoalX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outcome of chasing a false goal"@en, "Ergebnis der Jagd nach einem falschen Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pursuing a false goal either yields nothing, the effort merely feeding pendulums, or the goal is reached and turns out not to be what one wanted; the lost lifetime then goes on correcting mistakes."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Pursuing a false goal either yields nothing, the effort merely feeding pendulums, or the goal is reached and turns out not to be what one wanted; the lost lifetime then goes on correcting mistakes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingChoosingOwnThingsHeartX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing your own things with the heart (shopping method)"@en, "Die eigenen Dinge mit dem Herzen wählen (Einkaufsmethode)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) form only a general picture of the kind of item wanted, e.g. a coat, with no further conditions; (2) stroll through shops as if at an exhibition, observing without thinking or weighing pros and cons; (3) let the heart pick: the right item is recognised by an instant pull and is bought without further analysis; (4) be patient if it is not found in the first places, it is waiting somewhere; (5) at the yes/no moment let the mind finish its decision undisturbed, then immediately stop listening to others, wake up and attend to how comfortable the decision felt; (6) let go of wanting to reach it, keep importance low, forget strict planning and rely on the alternatives flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Author says it applies beyond clothes to any choice made for oneself, and offers it as practice for choosing one's own goals."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck: applies the after-decision feeling check to choosing clothes and other things for oneself, adds walking the shops as if at an exhibition, and states it fails when choosing for others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotAgoniseOverChoiceX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not agonise over the choice"@en, "Sich nicht mit der Wahl quälen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torturing oneself over a choice is said to destroy balance; the more stress, the worse the result. The mind should be kept out of the choosing, since here it is not the self but pendulum residue."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingChoosingOwnThingsHeartX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartSaysYesInstantDelightMindX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart says yes: instant delight, then the mind agrees"@en, "Das Herz sagt ja: sofortige Freude, danach stimmt der Verstand zu"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: you feel drawn to the item at once and are delighted on first sight; if the mind's later analysis also ends in yes, the thing is yours. A further sign is that you need not convince yourself of anything."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: you feel drawn to the item at once and are delighted on first sight; if the mind's later analysis also ends in yes, the thing is yours. A further sign is that you need not convince yourself of anything; for pmp:TranserfingChoosingOwnThingsHeartX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHavingPersuadeYourselfThingNotYoursX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Having to persuade yourself: the thing is not yours"@en, "Sich überreden müssen: das Ding gehört nicht zu dir"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hesitation, slight inconvenience, a faint shadow of doubt or heaviness, or catching yourself arguing that something suits you, are signs the item belongs to another person; put it aside without regret. Stated as an unequivocal criterion."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Hesitation, slight inconvenience, a faint shadow of doubt or heaviness, or catching yourself arguing that something suits you, are signs the item belongs to another person; put it aside without regret. Stated as an unequivocal criterion; concerns pmp:TranserfingChoosingOwnThingsHeartX10."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingPersuasionTest: the same rule is applied to buying things, with hesitation, slight inconvenience and a faint shadow of heaviness added as signs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotRelyOthersOpinionsWhenX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not rely on others' opinions when choosing"@en, "Sich bei der Wahl nicht auf fremde Meinungen stützen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only you can choose what is yours; comments by a shop assistant or friend are said to deepen the mind's sleep at the moment of decision."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingChoosingOwnThingsHeartX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityHeartMindReliableSupportX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of heart and mind as reliable support"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand als verlässliche Stütze"@de ;
    skos:definition "Relying on inner comfort after a final decision is said to prevent mistakes, since the union of heart and mind is a dependable anchor; the choosing process is said to contain every core Transurfing principle (low importance, waking up, script-determination, trust in the alternatives flow)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartLedChoosingYieldsDiscernmentOwnX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Heart-led choosing yields discernment of one's own things"@en, "Herzgeleitetes Wählen ergibt Unterscheidung der eigenen Dinge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practising the shopping method is said to leave one with a dependable tool for recognising what is one's own."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingChoosingOwnThingsHeartX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAbilityTellOwnThingsThingsMeantX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAbilityTellOwnThingsThingsMeantX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ability to tell your own things from things meant for others"@en, "Fähigkeit, die eigenen Dinge von den für andere bestimmten zu unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "A reliable sense, grounded in unity of heart and mind, for what is truly one's own; said to give calm confidence when choosing and protection from things meant for others, and to extend to choosing one's own goals."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMethodFailsWhenChoosingAnotherPersonX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Method fails when choosing for another person"@en, "Methode versagt bei der Wahl für einen anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart-led choice does not work, or not with the same accuracy, when choosing for someone else such as a child, because the soul cannot choose what is meant for another; rely on practical concerns or let the child choose, children being said to be good at finding their own things."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The heart-led choice does not work, or not with the same accuracy, when choosing for someone else such as a child, because the soul cannot choose what is meant for another; rely on practical concerns or let the child choose, children being said to be good at finding their own things; concerns pmp:TranserfingChoosingOwnThingsHeartX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Choose Your Own Things'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'
#

pmc:TranserfingFashionOriginatesPeopleFreePendulumsX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fashion originates with people free from pendulums"@en, "Mode entsteht bei Menschen, die von Pendeln frei sind"@de ;
    skos:definition "New trends are said to be set by people led by their own judgement and heart; their style is noticed, copied and spreads. Following fashion blindly is participation in the fashion pendulum's game and imitation of the pendulum rule to copy it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBlindlyFollowingFashionX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Blindly following fashion"@en, "Blindes Mitlaufen mit der Mode"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blind fashion-following can ruin one's appearance and is walking with inner intention toward another's goal. Yielding to the fashion pendulum is not wrong in itself provided one is aware of it and takes the benefit for oneself rather than paying tribute."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingFashionOriginatesPeopleFreePendulumsX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCreatingOwnFashionPendulumX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating your own fashion pendulum"@en, "Das eigene Modependel erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: turn from pendulums toward yourself; set the unspecific aim to appear elegant and interesting; walk the shops with the heart-led choosing method; ignore current fashion and attend only to feelings; switch off analysis and stop the instant you catch yourself reasoning; heed the faint morning-star rustle within; set no time limit, drop the desire to succeed and the pressure, lower importance, relax control; window-shop and try clothes on from curiosity; rely on the flow of alternatives; optionally run a slide of the goal that carries the feeling of attracting admiring attention, not a detailed picture of the look; give up the wish for the outlandish."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEarlyLackSuccessNoDeadlineX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Early lack of success; no deadline"@en, "Anfänglicher Misserfolg; keine Frist"@de ;
    skos:definition "At first one may not succeed; therefore no time limit should be set. If it does not work, nothing is lost."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: At first one may not succeed; therefore no time limit should be set. If it does not work, nothing is lost; concerns pmp:TranserfingCreatingOwnFashionPendulumX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSurpriseDelightWhenHeartMindUniteX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surprise and delight when heart and mind unite"@en, "Überraschung und Entzücken bei Einheit von Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: after a while unusual, original combinations turn up; when heart and mind unite one feels an incomparable mix of surprise and delight, more an astonished exclamation than a mere \"this is what I wanted\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: after a while unusual, original combinations turn up; when heart and mind unite one feels an incomparable mix of surprise and delight, more an astonished exclamation than a mere \"this is what I wanted\"; for pmp:TranserfingCreatingOwnFashionPendulumX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnFashionPracticeYieldsTrendsetterStatusX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own-fashion practice yields trendsetter status"@en, "Praxis des eigenen Stils ergibt Trendsetter-Status"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the own-fashion procedure is said to lead to original combinations and, through pendulum dynamics, to becoming a star."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCreatingOwnFashionPendulumX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBecomingTrendsetterFavouriteOwnPendulumX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBecomingTrendsetterFavouriteOwnPendulumX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a trendsetter, favourite of one's own pendulum"@en, "Zum Trendsetter werden, Liebling des eigenen Pendels"@de ;
    skos:definition "One finds an original personal style; pendulums, unable to do otherwise, are said to light up a rising star and even help, so that one may become the favourite of the pendulum one created. Said to apply to everything one does, not just clothes."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPendulumFavourites: here a person who goes their own way is made a star by the very pendulums, possibly by a pendulum of their own making, instead of being exploited by a destructive one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUniquenessSoulKeySuccessX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Uniqueness of the soul as key to success"@en, "Einzigartigkeit der Seele als Schlüssel zum Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind should add to its references that everyone owns a treasure, the soul's own uniqueness; success lies in freeing oneself from pendulums and going one's own way; one's potential is limited only by one's own intention. People fail to be themselves only because pendulums want obedient puppets."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLettingHeartChooseUnderMindsEscortX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the heart choose under the mind's escort yields unity"@en, "Das Herz unter Begleitung des Verstandes wählen lassen ergibt Einheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having the mind escort the heart into the shops and allow it to pick is the image given for producing unity of heart and mind."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCreatingOwnFashionPendulumX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityHeartMindRareQualityBehindX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of heart and mind as the rare quality behind stars"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand als seltene Eigenschaft der Stars"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which the mind accepts and follows the heart's choice; said to be so rare it can be sold at great profit, to underlie every great cultural and artistic achievement, and to be what makes stars stars."@en ;
    skos:note "Applies the shared term pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma, typed in another part of Stupen' II."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'How to Become a Trendsetter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'
#

pmc:TranserfingEachPersonsOwnLifeLineMatchingX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Each person's own life line matching their fraile"@en, "Die eigene Lebenslinie, die zur Fraile passt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every individual is a unique energetic essence with its own emission spectrum; one life line within the space of alternatives matches each fraile like a key its lock. Walking toward the right goal on one's own path, things turn out favourably; leaving it brings adversity and life as a battle. Pendulums impose their goals so that people crowd at others' doors."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLivingOwnLifeLineMinimalObstaclesX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living one's own life line: minimal obstacles, favourable circumstances"@en, "Leben auf der eigenen Lebenslinie: minimale Hindernisse, günstige Umstände"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the life line matching one's fraile, obstacles are said to be minimal, circumstances to favour one, and the goal to be reached easily."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHappinessNotBeyondObstaclesX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Happiness is not beyond the obstacles"@en, "Das Glück liegt nicht jenseits der Hindernisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "The engrained belief that success needs gruelling work and fighting for one's sunny spot is called a delusion; the core error is believing happiness awaits once obstacles are overcome. On a foreign life line no future happiness waits; it is either in the present life line now or nowhere, a mirage created by pendulums to extract energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAgainstFightingForLuck: the error is now located in expecting happiness beyond the obstacles; on a foreign life line no such happiness waits."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHappinessPresentWayOwnGoalX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Happiness in the present on the way to one's own goal"@en, "Glück in der Gegenwart auf dem Weg zum eigenen Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "When on one's own life line and path, happiness is said to be felt now, even before the goal is reached; every day becomes a holiday, and reaching the goal doubles the happiness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReachingForeignGoalDisappointmentDepletionX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reaching a foreign goal: disappointment, depletion"@en, "Erreichen eines fremden Ziels: Enttäuschung, Erschöpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many feel depleted when they finally reach a goal with great difficulty; a goal not truly one's own brings disappointment and depletion, never happiness, and movement toward it keeps happiness in an illusory future."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Many feel depleted when they finally reach a goal with great difficulty; a goal not truly one's own brings disappointment and depletion, never happiness, and movement toward it keeps happiness in an illusory future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTsel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal (one's own goal)"@en, "Ziel (das eigene Ziel)"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's own goal is what fulfils a person deeply and lastingly, not for a while, and gives a real joy of life; it would turn the whole of life into a continuous holiday. It is found by the heart, not derived from a passing need, prestige or the means."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: tsel' (цель)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergisedObstaclesEasyWorkNoBurdenX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energised, obstacles easy, work no burden"@en, "Energiegeladen, Hindernisse leicht, Arbeit keine Last"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of moving toward your goal via the door that is yours: you feel energised rather than drained, obstacles are overcome easily and work is not felt as a burden."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: Announced sign of moving toward your goal via the door that is yours: you feel energised rather than drained, obstacles are overcome easily and work is not felt as a burden."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMaximumEffortNoInspirationFatigueX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Maximum effort, no inspiration, fatigue"@en, "Maximale Anstrengung, keine Inspiration, Erschöpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "If great effort leaves one uninspired and tired, either the goal is not one's own or one is knocking at the wrong door."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If great effort leaves one uninspired and tired, either the goal is not one's own or one is knocking at the wrong door."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFeaturesForeignGoalsX10 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Features of foreign goals"@en, "Merkmale fremder Ziele"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author lists the marks of a goal not one's own: (1) it feels like an obligation, forced and punishing; (2) it means constant obstacles and struggle; (3) it is presented as fashionable and prestigious; (4) it attracts by seeming unattainable; (5) it is imposed by others; (6) it serves someone else's wellbeing; (7) it evokes inner tension. Foreign goals and doors demand much energy and bring suffering."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalFeelsLikeObligationX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal feels like an obligation"@en, "Ziel fühlt sich wie Pflicht an"@de ;
    skos:definition "If a goal feels even slightly like an enforced duty, it is foreign and should be dropped boldly; one's own goal needs no self-persuasion because it is enjoyed. Pendulums programme people to slog on in the belief that enough hard work pays off."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If a goal feels even slightly like an enforced duty, it is foreign and should be dropped boldly; one's own goal needs no self-persuasion because it is enjoyed. Pendulums programme people to slog on in the belief that enough hard work pays off."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalPresentedFashionablePrestigiousX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal presented as fashionable and prestigious"@en, "Ziel als modisch und prestigeträchtig präsentiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums dangle an attractive carrot and myths of stars' careers to lure people off their life line into copying another's path; stars succeeded precisely by not following \"do as I do\"; only one's soul knows the algorithm of one's own success."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Pendulums dangle an attractive carrot and myths of stars' careers to lure people off their life line into copying another's path; stars succeeded precisely by not following \"do as I do\"; only one's soul knows the algorithm of one's own success."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLuredFromHappiness: adds the myths of stars' careers and the rule of copying, and that stars rose by refusing it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalAttractiveBecauseSeemsUnattainableX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal attractive because it seems unattainable"@en, "Ziel reizvoll, weil es unerreichbar scheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pull of what is locked away, rooted in childhood, makes people want what is not for them; a goal whose achievement would mainly prove something to oneself or others is also misguided."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The pull of what is locked away, rooted in childhood, makes people want what is not for them; a goal whose achievement would mainly prove something to oneself or others is also misguided."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTestWantingEnjoyingWantingX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Test: wanting it or enjoying the wanting"@en, "Probe: es wollen oder das Wollen genießen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lower the importance of the goal, then ask whether you want it wholeheartedly or merely enjoy wanting it, and whether reaching it would serve to prove something; the latter answers mark a misguided goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalImposedOthersX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal imposed by others"@en, "Von anderen aufgezwungenes Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only you can set your goal; listen calmly to those who know better, then draw your own conclusions. The only exception is a casual phrase dropped without any agenda, which may act as a sign."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Only you can set your goal; listen calmly to those who know better, then draw your own conclusions. The only exception is a casual phrase dropped without any agenda, which may act as a sign."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingImposedGoal: here the goal is imposed by people who claim to know better, and an agenda-free passing remark is allowed as the one exception."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRejectOthersWhoPrescribeGoalX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Reject others who prescribe your goal"@en, "Andere abweisen, die dein Ziel vorschreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anyone presuming to tell you what to strive for is intruding into your soul; such intrusion should be stopped early."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingGoalImposedOthersX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPassingPhraseSignPointingGoalX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Passing phrase as a sign pointing to one's goal"@en, "Beiläufige Bemerkung als Zeichen für das eigene Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "An unintentional remark made with no aim of guiding you can ignite the soul; if it touches your goal the heart becomes lively and you know at once it is what you need. It must be incidental and agenda-free."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHeedingSpontaneousPhrases: the passing phrase is now read as a pointer to one's goal, recognised by the heart coming alive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalServesOthersWellbeingX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal serves others' wellbeing"@en, "Ziel dient dem Wohl anderer"@de ;
    skos:definition "A goal that does not improve one's own life, or directly serves other people's needs and prosperity, is foreign; true goals always work for one's own wellbeing and success."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A goal that does not improve one's own life, or directly serves other people's needs and prosperity, is foreign; true goals always work for one's own wellbeing and success."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuiltDutySlogansUsedPendulumsX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt and duty slogans used by pendulums"@en, "Schuld- und Pflichtparolen der Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Words like must, obligated, have to, or the call that your help is needed are pendulum means working through inner and outer importance, especially on guilt-prone people. The author insists one lives first for oneself, owes nobody anything, cannot make others happy but can harm them with one's own unhappiness."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingManipulators: adds the slogan of being needed and the claim that one lives first for oneself and owes nobody."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingGoalServesOthersWellbeingX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalEvokesInnerTensionX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal evokes inner tension"@en, "Ziel erzeugt innere Anspannung"@de ;
    skos:definition "However attractive the mind paints it, if some aspect of the goal feels off, if pleasure is mixed with anxiety or a heavy sense of burden, the goal is foreign."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: However attractive the mind paints it, if some aspect of the goal feels off, if pleasure is mixed with anxiety or a heavy sense of burden, the goal is foreign."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingInnerComfortTestGoalX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner-comfort test of a goal"@en, "Probe des inneren Wohlgefühls bei einem Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ignore prestige, apparent unattainability and the means; invite the inner voice; imagine the goal already reached and behind you and notice whether you feel good; anxiety or heaviness mixed into the pleasure reveals inner tension and a foreign goal. Repeated from the previous chapter."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck: the check is applied to a goal, imagined as already reached, with prestige, unattainability and means set aside."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnfulfilmentRunMisfortuneX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unfulfilment or run of misfortune"@en, "Unerfülltheit oder Pechsträhne"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dissatisfaction with one's position or a wave of misfortune is said to mean one fell under a destructive pendulum at some point and went through a foreign door toward a foreign goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Dissatisfaction with one's position or a wave of misfortune is said to mean one fell under a destructive pendulum at some point and went through a foreign door toward a foreign goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnGoalsSeemRealiseThemselvesX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Own goals seem to realise themselves"@en, "Eigene Ziele scheinen sich selbst zu verwirklichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: on finding one's own goals and doors, everything runs like clockwork and problems are said to disappear."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: on finding one's own goals and doors, everything runs like clockwork and problems are said to disappear."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowingTrueGoalX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing one's true goal"@en, "Das eigene wahre Ziel kennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clear awareness of what one truly wants, the goal meant for one's soul."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSeriouslyAskingWhatWantQuietX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seriously asking what you want, in quiet"@en, "In Ruhe ernsthaft fragen, was man will"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of catching thoughts about one's wishes in rushed moments, take time alone, relax and heed the faint morning-star rustle within; no deep self-absorption is required."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingQuietListeningYieldsKnowledgeGoalX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Quiet listening yields knowledge of one's goal"@en, "Stilles Hinhören ergibt Kenntnis des Ziels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking time alone to listen inwardly is said to be enough to determine one's true goal."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSeriouslyAskingWhatWantQuietX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKnowingTrueGoalX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFindingNoDesireDepletedLifeForceX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding no desire: depleted life force"@en, "Kein Wunsch zu finden: erschöpfte Lebenskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "If looking inward reveals no innermost desire, depression and apathy are clear signs that energy suffices only for bare existence; the heart cannot be without desires, one lacks the strength to hear it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If looking inward reveals no innermost desire, depression and apathy are clear signs that energy suffices only for bare existence; the heart cannot be without desires, one lacks the strength to hear it; concerns pmp:TranserfingSeriouslyAskingWhatWantQuietX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnoughLifeEnergyHearHeartsDesireX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enough life energy to hear the heart's desire"@en, "Genug Lebensenergie, um den Wunsch des Herzens zu hören"@de ;
    skos:definition "A level of life force above bare subsistence, at which the heart's innermost desire, said never to be absent, becomes audible; to be reached by raising one's energy reserves."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyReservesBeforeHearingHeartsDesireX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy reserves before hearing the heart's desire"@en, "Energiereserven vor dem Hören des Herzenswunsches"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sufficient energy is required to perceive the heart's desire; when depleted, one should first focus on raising energy reserves."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingSeriouslyAskingWhatWantQuietX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEnoughLifeEnergyHearHeartsDesireX10 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without enough energy no innermost desire is perceived; depression and apathy remain." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Other People's Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'
#

pmc:TranserfingForeignGoalsUnderNoblePretextsX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Foreign goals under noble pretexts"@en, "Fremde Ziele unter edlem Vorwand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Appeals to kind souls to save animals, soldiers, starving children or freedom fighters may plant a foreign goal; it is the kind mind, not the heart, that responds, abandoning one's own soul like leaving one's children to save another's."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAltruismCompensationSpiritualEmptinessX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAltruismCompensationSpiritualEmptinessX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Altruism as compensation for spiritual emptiness"@en, "Altruismus als Ausgleich für seelische Leere"@de ;
    skos:definition "The charitable stereotype is said to be an effect of spiritual emptiness: the mind shuts the heart in its box, emptiness grows, and pendulums offer helping others as compensation, dressed as compassion."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMaskOfTheBenefactor: charity is now explained as compensation for spiritual emptiness after the mind has shut the heart away."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfLoveYieldsGoalX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-love yields one's goal"@en, "Selbstliebe ergibt das eigene Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Learning to love oneself is said to lead to finding one's goal."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFindingInnermostGoalTurningHeartX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKnowingTrueGoalX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGreaterAbilityHelpOthersOncePathX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Greater ability to help others once on one's path"@en, "Größere Fähigkeit zu helfen, sobald man auf dem eigenen Weg ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once securely on the way to one's true goal, one is said to do many good deeds and help the poor better, because one attracts greater resources and opportunities."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnGoalBeforeAnsweringAppealsHelpX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Own goal before answering appeals for help"@en, "Eigenes Ziel vor dem Eingehen auf Hilfsappelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Help for others should come after one's own goal is clearly defined; until then be very cautious with appeals and keep importance minimal."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingGreaterAbilityHelpOthersOncePathX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingKnowingTrueGoalX10 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCautionAppealsHelpBeforeOwnGoalX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Caution with appeals for help before own goal is clear"@en, "Vorsicht bei Hilfsappellen, solange das eigene Ziel unklar ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Until one's own goal is defined, respond to appeals for help with great caution and keep inner and outer importance at a minimum."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAltruismCompensationSpiritualEmptinessX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBeingDrawnPendulumBattlesX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Being drawn into pendulum battles"@en, "Hineingezogenwerden in Pendelkämpfe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warring pendulums each cast themselves as liberator and the other as aggressor to recruit adherents inflated with importance; supporters of both war and peace end up deceived, their ideals like empty soap bubbles; spiritual emptiness deepens rather than fills."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBattleOfPendulums: adds that adherents of both camps, war and peace, end deceived, and that the battles feed on spiritual emptiness."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingBattleOfPendulums ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingTestWhereImpulseCareComesX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Test of where the impulse to care comes from"@en, "Probe, woher der Impuls zur Fürsorge kommt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Check the origin of the wish to care for others: if it comes from anywhere outside oneself, the goal is foreign; if it rises from deep in one's heart as enjoyment, e.g. delight in pets or grandchildren, the goal may be one's own."@en ;
    skos:note "When the children grow up, a new goal must be found."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFindingInnermostGoalTurningHeartX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding your innermost goal by turning to the heart"@en, "Das innerste Ziel finden durch Hinwendung zum Herzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lower importance, turn away from pendulums, release the heart from its box, appeal to it, love yourself first and take care of yourself; stated to be the only way to the path of your own goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingJudgingFeasibilityMeansFirstX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Judging feasibility and means first"@en, "Zuerst Machbarkeit und Mittel prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind evaluating from the start how realistic a goal is and calculating the means leads it to drop or shelve the goal; thinking about means rehearses scenarios of defeat and is said to tune thought energy to an unlucky life line, never to the target line."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: The mind evaluating from the start how realistic a goal is and calculating the means leads it to drop or shelve the goal; thinking about means rehearses scenarios of defeat and is said to tune thought energy to an unlucky life line, never to the target line."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalFocusYieldsOpeningPathX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Goal-focus yields the opening path"@en, "Zielfokus ergibt den sich öffnenden Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Holding the goal, not the means, in mind is said to be the only condition under which such miracles occur."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingThinkGoalNotMeansX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingApparentMiraclesUnexpectedRealisticPathOpensX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingThinkGoalNotMeansX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Think of the goal, not the means"@en, "An das Ziel denken, nicht an die Mittel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Break the conventional stereotype by holding the goal itself in mind, not the ways to reach it, so as to tune to the target line's frequency and decide to have with intent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingApparentMiraclesUnexpectedRealisticPathOpensX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Apparent miracles: an unexpected realistic path opens"@en, "Scheinbare Wunder: ein unerwarteter gangbarer Weg öffnet sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "What seemed unrealistic appears in a new light and, as if by chance, a realistic path opens; outer intention carries one to a life line with new opportunities and doors unseen from the previous line. Called a miraculous coincidence conventionally; in Transurfing no miracle."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCrowdMembersMindsAsleepUnderPendulumX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Crowd members' minds asleep under a pendulum"@en, "Schlafender Verstand des Massenmitglieds unter einem Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordinary people (the author cites wartime Nazi soldiers and teenagers in crowds) commit cruelty because the mind succumbs to a pendulum and ceases to be conscious of what it does; evil is attributed to pendulum influence rather than human nature."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEvilPendulumPlaqueMindNotHeartX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evil as pendulum plaque in the mind, not in the heart"@en, "Das Böse als Pendelbelag im Verstand, nicht im Herzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "All evil, cruelty and violence are said to stem from the greed of pendulums, not from a dark side of human nature; the heart knows no evil, which accumulates in the mind as plaque from destructive pendulum influence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstRecklessRiskTakingProvokedPendulumsX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against reckless risk-taking provoked by pendulums"@en, "Gegen leichtsinnige, von Pendeln provozierte Risiken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Slogans like nothing ventured, nothing gained provoke people to stake health or life for someone else's idea, since fear and excitement are favourite pendulum food; undue risk usually hides inferiority complexes and internal importance. A justified risk for one's own idea may be worth it; one has nothing to prove and may disregard manipulators."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMayatnik ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTrueFreedomStrengthThroughUnityHeartX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "True freedom and strength through unity of heart and mind"@en, "Wahre Freiheit und Stärke durch Einheit von Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Uniting heart and mind is said to bring true freedom and strength."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityHeartMindBeforeTrueFreedomX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of heart and mind before true freedom"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand vor wahrer Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "True freedom and strength are presented as following from the union of heart and mind."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingTrueFreedomStrengthThroughUnityHeartX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingBreakingThroughPendulumStereotypesX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking through pendulum stereotypes"@en, "Pendel-Stereotype durchbrechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without fear, refuse the stereotypes created by pendulums (forced altruism, false courage, unattainability, means-first thinking), turning instead to the heart."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBreakingStereotypesYieldsOpenDoorsX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking stereotypes yields open doors"@en, "Stereotype durchbrechen ergibt offene Türen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breaking through stereotypes yields insight into the nature of things and opens locked doors."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingBreakingThroughPendulumStereotypesX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSeeingTrueNatureThingsLockedDoorsX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingTrueNatureThingsLockedDoorsX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing the true nature of things; locked doors opening"@en, "Das wahre Wesen der Dinge sehen; verschlossene Türen öffnen sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breaking through stereotypes is said to reveal what many things truly are and to open doors that were locked."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Breaking Through Stereotypes'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'
#

pmc:TranserfingIntentionTurnsDesireGoalX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention turns desire into goal"@en, "Absicht verwandelt Wunsch in Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The essentials are to define the innermost desire and gain the will to have and to act intentionally; without intention a desire is never fulfilled; if the will is there, a way will present itself even if it cannot be seen yet. Vague formulations such as wanting to be rich and happy do not work."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNamerenie: intention is here what turns an innermost desire into a concrete goal, and a way is said to appear once the will is there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSoleGuaranteeOwnInnermostGoalThroughX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sole guarantee: own innermost goal through own door"@en, "Einzige Garantie: eigenes innerstes Ziel durch die eigene Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without a goal one drifts like a paper boat; with any goal success is uncertain; the only full guarantee is if the goal is truly one's innermost and one goes through one's door, as the fraile of the heart fits one's path like a key; nothing truly one's own can be taken away."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDefiningInnermostGoalX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Defining your innermost goal"@en, "Das innerste Ziel bestimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) do not derive the goal from a temporary need; ask what you want most from life and what would make it joyful, treating all else as pendulum husk; (2) settle on one main goal, the others follow; (3) if nothing specific comes, start from a general aim like comfort and wellbeing and ask what it means personally, refining it (e.g. from a well-paid job, which is only a door, toward becoming an outstanding specialist); (4) ask what your heart longs for and what would make life a continual holiday; (5) ignore prestige, difficulty and means; drop any sense of limits, pretending to believe if you cannot, and order boldly (yacht instead of boat); (6) do not wish with the mind; judge by your heart's relationship to the thing, not by opinion; (7) check the wish by asking how comfortable you feel inside the bubble of the goal once reached, then twice whether you really need it, measuring it against the marks of a foreign goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOneMainGoalBringsOthersAlongX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One main goal brings the others along"@en, "Ein Hauptziel zieht die übrigen nach sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Achieving the single main goal is said to bring fulfilment of all other desires; on such a life line the trappings of comfortable living come seemingly automatically."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDver a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Door"@en, "Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "The door is the way or means by which a goal is reached, for instance a job or a field of activity. One's own door is the path to one's goal lived with passion and inspiration, which energises rather than drains, even if not everything comes easily. Loved work that does not by itself give life its full meaning is a door and not a goal; where it does, goal and door coincide."@en ;
    skos:note "Russian term: dver' (дверь)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingGoTestHardGoalX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting-go test for a hard goal"@en, "Loslass-Probe bei einem schwierigen Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "If a goal is hard to attain, provisionally let it go and observe the feeling: relief indicates a foreign goal; indignation or wanting to protest indicates it may be your own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingInnerTensionTestAfterMindsDecisionX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner-tension test after the mind's decision"@en, "Probe der inneren Anspannung nach der Entscheidung des Verstandes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only after the mind has decided on a goal: imagine it already achieved and behind you; once the feeling is present, stop deliberating and listen to the heart's immediate reaction; pleasure mixed with fear, a heavy burden, urgency or obligation is the heart's no. Do not hurry the final decision; test the goal with the slide technique over time."@en ;
    skos:note "Called the only reliable criterion for choosing a goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck: applied to a goal the mind has already chosen; called the only reliable criterion, with fear, burden, urgency or duty as the signs of no."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindDecidesBeforeComfortTestX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mind decides before the comfort test"@en, "Der Verstand entscheidet vor der Wohlfühlprobe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The inner-comfort test works only on a decision the mind has already made."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingInnerTensionTestAfterMindsDecisionX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingDefiningInnermostGoalX10 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerTensionVersusInnerInhibitionX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner tension versus inner inhibition"@en, "Innere Anspannung gegenüber innerer Hemmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inhibition is the natural shyness before something unfamiliar (can this really be for me?) and can be overcome with slides; inner tension is a quiet, onerous sense of oppression amid the mind's optimism and can never be overcome by slides. Tension about the goal itself marks a foreign goal; tension about its difficulty means it is beyond the comfort zone or the door is foreign."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotReadTensionUnworthinessX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not read tension as unworthiness"@en, "Anspannung nicht als Unwürdigkeit deuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Concluding from inner tension that one is unworthy is called the worst mistake, a label imposed by pendulums; one deserves the best. At least do not hurry the final decision."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingInnerTensionVersusInnerInhibitionX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPersistentOnerousFeelingAfterSlideTestingX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Persistent onerous feeling after slide testing"@en, "Anhaltendes drückendes Gefühl nach Diaprobe"@de ;
    skos:definition "If after working with slides for some time the heavy feeling remains, it is inner tension, not inhibition; if it attaches to the goal itself, the goal is foreign."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If after working with slides for some time the heavy feeling remains, it is inner tension, not inhibition; if it attaches to the goal itself, the goal is foreign; concerns pmp:TranserfingInnerTensionTestAfterMindsDecisionX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTensionGoalsDifficultyComfortZoneDoorX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tension from the goal's difficulty: comfort zone or door"@en, "Spannung wegen der Schwierigkeit des Ziels: Komfortzone oder Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the inner tension comes from knowing the goal is hard to reach, rather than from the goal itself, the goal is said to lie outside the present comfort zone, or a foreign door has been chosen."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the inner tension comes from knowing the goal is hard to reach, rather than from the goal itself, the goal is said to lie outside the present comfort zone, or a foreign door has been chosen; concerns pmp:TranserfingInnerTensionTestAfterMindsDecisionX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalBeforeDoorX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal before door"@en, "Ziel vor Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "The goal must be firmly decided before any thought is given to the door, the means of achieving it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingChoosingDoorX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingDefiningInnermostGoalX10 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCannotSeeYourselfClearlyRoleX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cannot see yourself clearly in the role"@en, "Sich in der Rolle nicht klar sehen können"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inability to picture oneself clearly in the envisaged role may mean one is not yet ready; slides can widen the comfort zone, and the will to have will let outer intention lead to the right door."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Inability to picture oneself clearly in the envisaged role may mean one is not yet ready; slides can widen the comfort zone, and the will to have will let outer intention lead to the right door."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMoneyCannotGoalX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Money cannot be the goal"@en, "Geld kann nicht das Ziel sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Money is an abstract category for the mind; the heart cannot think abstractly and must understand and like what the money would buy (house, island). Money can only accompany another goal. While the inner accountant calculates means, the goal cannot be determined nor energy attuned to the target line."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMoneyAsAttribute: adds the reason: the heart cannot think abstractly and must know and like what the money would buy."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMoneyFirstMyth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingInnerGuardianCatchingEvasionQuestionX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner Guardian catching evasion of the question"@en, "Innerer Wächter, der das Ausweichen von der Frage bemerkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each time you catch the mind dodging the question of what you want from life, or slipping into how to achieve it, nudge yourself and let the heart order the mind to hush, since a toy is being chosen. Patience is needed because the unattainability stereotype is deepest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalBelongsPendulumWithoutThreatX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One's goal belongs to a pendulum without threat"@en, "Das eigene Ziel gehört zu einem Pendel, ohne Gefahr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freedom from destructive pendulums does not mean isolation; society is built on pendulums, and hermits lose balance on returning. One's goal will belong to a pendulum, harmless if it is the innermost desire; the pendulum is then obliged to make one its favourite, or one can create a new pendulum. The point is to exercise freedom of choice and not let pendulums take control."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingUsingPendulums: one's own goal will itself belong to a pendulum, harmless if it is the innermost desire, and hermits are said to lose balance on returning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingActiveAnalyticalSearchFailsX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Active, analytical search fails"@en, "Aktive, analytische Suche führt zu nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "The goal cannot be found by analysis and reasoning, which work from stereotypes; only the heart, which sees and feels but does not think, can identify it. Actively hunting for the path leads nowhere; wait and observe."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingPassiveSearchGoalHeldStatementX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPassiveSearchGoalHeldStatementX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Passive search for the goal with a held statement"@en, "Passive Zielsuche mit einem gehaltenen Leitsatz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not search by analysis. Let the mind set the precept of seeking whatever would turn life into a holiday and keep it running in the background; take in external information without actively searching; widen your range of interests by visiting new places (museum, cinema, trek, unfamiliar district, bookshop); set no timescale and do not make it a chore; pass each piece of information through the filter of how you feel about it; when something inspires interest, attend to the inner voice and keep the mind out, then think it through while listening inwardly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerResonanceILikeX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner resonance: I like it"@en, "Innerer Widerhall: das gefällt mir"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: sooner or later a sign or piece of information makes something inside resonate with spontaneous liking."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: sooner or later a sign or piece of information makes something inside resonate with spontaneous liking; for pmp:TranserfingPassiveSearchGoalHeldStatementX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTransformationWorldLayerOnceGoalDefinedX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transformation of the world layer once the goal is defined with intent"@en, "Verwandlung der Weltschicht, sobald das Ziel mit Absicht bestimmt ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: chest breathes freely without false goals; no more forcing oneself; permission to be happy now; lightness like spring after hibernation; depression and strain gone; the mind sheds alien junk and stops searching for means; the heart delights; doors open that were closed; the mind accepts the goal as achievable; life becomes an ongoing holiday, heart and mind walking together."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: chest breathes freely without false goals; no more forcing oneself; permission to be happy now; lightness like spring after hibernation; depression and strain gone; the mind sheds alien junk and stops searching for means; the heart delights; doors open that were closed; the mind accepts the goal as achievable; life becomes an ongoing holiday, heart and mind walking together; for pmp:TranserfingDefiningInnermostGoalX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Goals'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'
#

pmc:TranserfingConstantObstaclesPathX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Constant obstacles on the path"@en, "Ständige Hindernisse auf dem Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Continual obstacles suggest a foreign goal or a foreign door; one can work a whole life for nothing with the wrong goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Continual obstacles suggest a foreign goal or a foreign door; one can work a whole life for nothing with the wrong goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStereotypeEnforcedNecessityX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Stereotype of enforced necessity"@en, "Stereotyp der erzwungenen Notwendigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums teach people to accept life as compulsory labour, push the heart's inclinations aside until better times that never come, and split life into leisure and paid work; abandoning what one loves for financial reasons is another pendulum method to pull people off their path."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingLuredFromHappiness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProsperityActivityOneLovesWhenDoorX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prosperity from the activity one loves when door fits goal"@en, "Wohlstand aus der geliebten Tätigkeit, wenn Tür und Ziel zusammenfallen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If a loved activity is strongly tied to one's innermost goal, it is said to bring all attributes of a comfortable life; one becomes rich through the hobby, other desires are fulfilled beyond expectation, and masterpieces arise from heart-mind union, provided pendulums do not lead one astray."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingImmersionOnlyForOwnGoal: a loved activity tied to one's goal is said to bring wealth, even through a hobby, and masterpieces."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCalmlyFollowingPathWithoutPendulumTricksX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Calmly following one's path without pendulum tricks"@en, "Ruhig dem eigenen Weg folgen, ohne Pendeltricks"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pursue the activity connected to one's innermost goal calmly, not yielding to pendulum lures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFollowingPathYieldsSuccessProsperityX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Following one's path yields success and prosperity"@en, "Dem eigenen Weg folgen ergibt Erfolg und Wohlstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calmly following one's path is said to lead sooner or later to great success."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCalmlyFollowingPathWithoutPendulumTricksX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingProsperityActivityOneLovesWhenDoorX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingChoosingDoorX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing your door"@en, "Die eigene Tür wählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: do not hurry to choose; once the goal is defined, ask how it might be achieved; outer intention will offer options; consider them all and test each against the inner voice by the same principles as for the goal; ask who you want to be (money comes to what one represents, e.g. star, industrialist, specialist); ask the soul, not the mind, which reflects society's prestige advice; if the door is unclear, work with slides, widen the comfort zone, lower importance and drop attachment to the goal; give yourself permission to have."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRightDoorChoiceYieldsAbundanceX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Right door choice yields abundance"@en, "Richtige Türwahl ergibt Fülle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choosing goal and door wisely is said to yield opportunities and gains far beyond what was asked."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingChoosingDoorX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAbundanceThroughRightDoorX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAbundanceThroughRightDoorX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Abundance through the right door"@en, "Fülle durch die richtige Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through the right door chosen for oneself alone, one is said to receive so much that the initial requests (house, car, salary) appear laughable, with undreamed-of opportunities."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotRushChoiceDoorX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not rush the choice of door"@en, "Die Türwahl nicht überstürzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Never regret the time taken; a hasty choice later regretted wastes far more time and effort; the choice of goal and door may last months."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingChoosingDoorX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFastImpeccabilityDuringChoiceX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Fast of impeccability during the choice"@en, "Fasten der Untadeligkeit während der Wahl"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the months of choosing goal and door, follow Transurfing principles as strictly as possible: conscious awareness of the motives of one's actions (playing by known rules or limply obeying a pendulum); watch inner and outer importance; think of goal and door as already acquired, no prestige, unattainability or necessity; accept possible failure from the start and allow mistakes, giving defeat a watched place; keep a fallback and a spare door, do not leave the old door at once or burn bridges, spread risk; keep picturing the goal slide; also run a slide of searching for one's goal and door and filter incoming information through it, tracking whether it inspires or weighs on the heart, not one's thoughts."@en ;
    skos:note "Term of the English translation: fast of impeccability."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptPossibleFailureAdvanceX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Accept possible failure in advance"@en, "Möglichen Misserfolg von vornherein annehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If it does not work out, it was not right and need not be mourned; allow mistakes and allocate a watched place for defeat; a disappointing failure may be a landmark on the path rather than defeat."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFastImpeccabilityDuringChoiceX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepSafetyNetDoNotBurnX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Keep a safety net; do not burn bridges"@en, "Ein Sicherheitsnetz behalten; keine Brücken abbrechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Proceed cautiously: arrange a fallback and a spare door, keep the previous door for now, spread the stakes, keep other routes open."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingSafetyNet: applied to choosing a door: keep the previous door and a spare door, burn no bridges."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingChoosingDoorX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPicturingGoalSlideWidensComfortZoneX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Picturing the goal slide widens the comfort zone"@en, "Das Zieldia vorstellen erweitert die Komfortzone"@de ;
    skos:definition "Continuing to picture the goal slide is said to widen the comfort zone and tune to the target line, so that outer intention supplies needed information."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFastImpeccabilityDuringChoiceX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneAttunementTargetLineX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneAttunementTargetLineX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Widened comfort zone, attunement to the target line"@en, "Erweiterte Komfortzone, Einstimmung auf die Ziellinie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which the goal no longer seems out of reach and thought energy resonates with the target life line, so outer intention can bring information and opportunities."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartRingsOutHeartSingsMindX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart rings out; heart sings and mind is satisfied"@en, "Das Herz klingt auf; Herz singt und Verstand ist zufrieden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: at some moment the heart rings out that this is exactly what was sought; then, without rushing, keep widening the comfort zone until the clear conclusion comes that this will make life an ongoing holiday, the heart singing and the mind satisfied."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: at some moment the heart rings out that this is exactly what was sought; then, without rushing, keep widening the comfort zone until the clear conclusion comes that this will make life an ongoing holiday, the heart singing and the mind satisfied; for pmp:TranserfingFastImpeccabilityDuringChoiceX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartSingsMindDoubtsX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart sings, mind doubts"@en, "Herz singt, Verstand zweifelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the heart sings but the mind still doubts, the comfort zone must be widened again to break the delusion that the goal is unrealistic."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If the heart sings but the mind still doubts, the comfort zone must be widened again to break the delusion that the goal is unrealistic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoorPadlockedUnattainabilityStereotypeX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Door padlocked by the unattainability stereotype"@en, "Tür verriegelt durch das Stereotyp der Unerreichbarkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A door seems impregnable because the mind's stereotype of unattainability locks it; the mind accepts only facts and cannot be forced to believe; the stereotype crumbles by itself when outer intention shows new opportunities on the target line; only the target slide can bring the shift to that line."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTargetSlideYieldsTransitionTargetLineX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Target slide yields transition to the target line"@en, "Zieldia ergibt Übergang zur Ziellinie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Running the target slide is said to be the only means to shift to the target life line, where the mind sees a clear path and the stereotype falls."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneAttunementTargetLineX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotPersuadeYourselfFightStereotypeX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not persuade yourself or fight the stereotype"@en, "Sich nicht überreden und nicht gegen das Stereotyp kämpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Convincing oneself that something is achievable or fighting a stereotype is futile; that is not how a stereotype is broken."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Systematically running the target slide"@en, "Systematisch das Zieldia abspielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not try to persuade yourself or fight the stereotype; simply run the target slide regularly in the mind, described as a concrete step toward the goal; be patient, since material realisation is inert."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRunningOutPatienceX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Running out of patience"@en, "Ungeduld"@de ;
    skos:definition "Material realisation is inert, so the order is not fulfilled instantly; impatience shows a passionate desire, i.e. doubt about achievability; then return to the start, reduce importance and widen the comfort zone until real prospects appear."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Material realisation is inert, so the order is not fulfilled instantly; impatience shows a passionate desire, i.e. doubt about achievability; then return to the start, reduce importance and widen the comfort zone until real prospects appear; concerns pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTrueDoorDisguisedWorthlessX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "True door disguised as worthless"@en, "Wahre Tür als wertlos getarnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums may mask one's door as trivial; anything one does easily and willingly has meaning, and an apparently useless quirk may unlock the right door."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingDver ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHoldingQuirksUpAgainstSeriousDoorsX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Holding one's quirks up against serious doors"@en, "Die eigenen Marotten an ernsthafte Türen halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take traits deemed silly or useless that you display willingly and easily and test them against serious professions: the clown as comedian, the one who loves dressing up as a model, make-up specialist or designer, the critic of bad adverts as advertiser; turn from pendulums toward the heart to discover this."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGettingDrainedPathWrongDoorX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Getting drained on the path: wrong door"@en, "Erschöpfung auf dem Weg: falsche Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "If already on the way and one tires and becomes drained, the door is the wrong one."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If already on the way and one tires and becomes drained, the door is the wrong one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInspirationWhileWorkingTowardGoalRightX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inspiration while working toward the goal: right door"@en, "Inspiration beim Hinarbeiten auf das Ziel: richtige Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: being filled with inspiration while doing what brings one closer to the goal confirms the door is one's own."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: being filled with inspiration while doing what brings one closer to the goal confirms the door is one's own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingForeignDoorSlamsShutCriticalMomentX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Foreign door slams shut at the critical moment"@en, "Fremde Tür schlägt im entscheidenden Moment zu"@de ;
    skos:definition "A foreign door may open and things go well at first, but at the cutting edge failure strikes; then one knows the door was foreign."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: A foreign door may open and things go well at first, but at the cutting edge failure strikes; then one knows the door was foreign."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPublicDoorsVersusPrivateDoorsX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Public doors versus private doors"@en, "Öffentliche gegenüber privaten Türen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pendulums open public doors to lure adherents; crowds jostle there while the door meant for each stands empty beside it. Private doors have no crowd; those who claim to want it step aside."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnDoorClosingThroughExcessImportanceX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Own door closing through excess importance"@en, "Eigene Tür schließt sich durch Übergewicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even one's own door closes if the law of balance is grossly violated by excessive importance or putting all eggs in one basket; lowering importance reopens it."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Even one's own door closes if the law of balance is grossly violated by excessive importance or putting all eggs in one basket; lowering importance reopens it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Your Doors'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingGoalVersusDreamIntentionVersusDesireX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal versus dream, intention versus desire"@en, "Ziel gegenüber Traum, Absicht gegenüber Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intention, the will to have and to act, turns a dream into a specific goal; empty dreams change nothing."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingNamerenie: sets goal against dream as intention against desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingActingPurifiedIntentionX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting from purified intention"@en, "Aus gereinigter Absicht handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the goal is defined and the will is burning, release the grip: lower the goal's importance and drop attachment to reaching it so only intent remains; then do what the situation requires, neither craving nor forcing the outcome, as one fetches the post: simply keep taking the next step, act and create momentum regardless of outcome, letting problems resolve in the process; keep up the will to have, without needing to picture the slide constantly."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingNewspaperAttitude: the errand image becomes fetching the post; only intent purified of importance and of attachment to the result remains, and the will to have is kept up."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExcessResponsibilityEffortDiligenceCoercionX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Excess responsibility, effort, diligence, coercion"@en, "Übermäßige Verantwortung, Anstrengung, Eifer, Zwang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking on excessive responsibility, effort, extreme diligence or self-coercion is said to be the sole thing able to ruin progress; on the right path through the right door no excessive effort or forcing is needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingEffortBeyondMeasure: excess responsibility, diligence and self-coercion are named the sole thing able to ruin progress on the right path."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingActingPurifiedIntentionX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNeedingForceYourselfWrongGoalDoorX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Needing to force yourself: wrong goal or door"@en, "Sich zwingen müssen: falsches Ziel oder falsche Tür"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one must strain and force oneself, either the goal or the door is wrong."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If one must strain and force oneself, either the goal or the door is wrong."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerVersusOuterIntentionGoalPursuitX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner versus outer intention in goal pursuit"@en, "Innere gegenüber äußerer Absicht bei der Zielverfolgung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner intention insists that something must happen and thrashes about; outer intention finds that it has happened. Insisting and pressuring blocks outer intention from realising the goal in step with the flow of alternatives, since the mind cannot know how the goal should come about."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingAlongWellTroddenRoadX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving along a well-trodden road"@en, "Gehen auf einer ausgetretenen Straße"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: on the true goal through one's own door nothing can stop one while importance is minimal and one does not fight the alternatives flow; temporary difficulties need not worry."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: on the true goal through one's own door nothing can stop one while importance is minimal and one does not fight the alternatives flow; temporary difficulties need not worry."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDiagnosingCloudOverHolidayX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Diagnosing a cloud over the holiday"@en, "Eine Wolke über dem Festtag diagnostizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "When unease appears, look for where importance rose: you are forcing yourself, too impatient for the goal, or attaching excessive importance to something; relax the grip. Accept everything that comes as a gift."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnxiousThoughtsAboutPrizeNarrowComfortX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anxious thoughts about the prize: narrow comfort zone"@en, "Ängstliche Gedanken um den Gewinn: enge Komfortzone"@de ;
    skos:definition "If expecting e.g. a large sum brings worries about keeping, investing, losing it, one is not ready to have it; inner inhibitions arise with a subconscious urge to be rid of the cause, and outer intention then works against one."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: If expecting e.g. a large sum brings worries about keeping, investing, losing it, one is not ready to have it; inner inhibitions arise with a subconscious urge to be rid of the cause, and outer intention then works against one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionVersusAutoSuggestionX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention versus auto-suggestion"@en, "Absicht gegenüber Autosuggestion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-persuasion never succeeds; with intention the decision is final and beyond discussion: reaching the goal is taken as given, and doubts fall away as the comfort zone widens."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSelfPersuasionFails: set against intention, whose decision is final and needs no persuading."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstStereotypeExclusivelyPositiveThinkingX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against the stereotype of exclusively positive thinking"@en, "Gegen das Stereotyp ausschließlich positiven Denkens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author warns of a major mistake: trying to think only of successful outcomes and exclude negative ones from the script does not work, as the mind cannot be convinced all will go smoothly; it plays along but the heart still finds the hidden doubt."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAffirmationsFail: the target is now the habit of picturing only good outcomes in one's script, which the heart sees through."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAffirmationsFail ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingComposingTargetSlideWithoutScriptsX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Composing the target slide without scripts"@en, "Das Zieldia ohne Drehbuch gestalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leave out of the target slide any scenes of the act of achieving the goal; picture only the final state of your life with the goal already had, enjoy watching it, and meanwhile keep taking the next step with purified intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProcessVisualisationAlreadyGoingWellX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Process visualisation: already going well"@en, "Prozessvisualisierung: es läuft bereits gut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualising the process works on the scenery differently: it persuades the mind that things are already going smoothly, not that they will; it should track only the current link of the transfer chain and the next step."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConvincingYourselfGoodOutcomeKeepsGripX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Convincing yourself of a good outcome keeps the grip of control"@en, "Sich ein gutes Ende einreden hält den Kontrollgriff fest"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to convince oneself that all will end well keeps a fatal grip of control; relax it, do not dwell on problems that have not happened, move calmly with the flow of alternatives."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingIntentionVersusAutoSuggestionX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'
#

pmc:TranserfingNoWayMakeOneselfBelieveImpossibleX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No way to make oneself believe the impossible; order and leave the rest"@en, "Kein Weg, sich das Unmögliche glauben zu machen; bestellen und den Rest überlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One cannot persuade or force oneself to believe the impossible; drop the worry about attainability, keep stepping toward the goal, place the order properly and leave fulfilment to outer intention, pictured as a waiter. Many highly successful people are reported to say they never would have believed themselves capable."@en ;
    skos:note "The third-party report is generic, no case given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartKnowsNoMeansMindThinksX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart knows no means; mind thinks in means"@en, "Das Herz kennt keine Mittel; der Verstand denkt in Mitteln"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the heart strives and the mind worries about means, understanding between them is blocked. In dreams the heart gets what it wishes via dream intention. The mind must consider means because it acts within inner intention, whose scenarios include bad endings, so outer intention then works against one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDreamsNoCriterionHeartsDesiresX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Dreams are no criterion of the heart's desires"@en, "Träume sind kein Maßstab für die Wünsche des Herzens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only light-sleep dreams are remembered, and on waking the mind re-trims the sail of the heart to its own expectations, so dreams cannot be used to read the heart's desires."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingHeartKnowsNoMeansMindThinksX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAccessPastLifeInformationX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Access to past-life information"@en, "Zugang zu Informationen aus früheren Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many accounts are said to exist of the mind accessing past-life information under the right circumstances; the soul's past lives are normally not remembered because the mind comes into the world blank. The author leaves open whether past lives happened and declares the topic out of scope."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStopRehearsingScenariosHowEventsMayX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Stop rehearsing scenarios of how events may go"@en, "Aufhören, mögliche Verläufe durchzuspielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Scenarios within inner intention include unfavourable endings, which outer intention then serves to one's detriment; hence the insistent advice to stop thinking through possible developments."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingJudgingFeasibilityMeansFirstX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWillHavePrevailsWillActPurifiedX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Will to have prevails; will to act purified"@en, "Der Wille zu haben überwiegt; der Wille zu handeln wird gereinigt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The will to have must dominate; the will to act needs purifying as fully as possible of desire and importance, reduced to the intent to do the minimum required. Dispassionate action is not sluggish; excessive will is itself a product of importance; actions are effective to the degree inner intention is purified."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGeneralStagesLivingTargetSlideX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "From general stages to living in the target slide"@en, "Von den groben Etappen zum Leben im Zieldia"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) think through how the goal will be reached only in general terms, enough to fix the main stages, the links of the transfer chain; (2) then drop the general scenario entirely; (3) let only the target slide, the final picture without scripts, occupy your thoughts; turn it over continuously and live inside it; (4) remove desire and importance from your attitude."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLivingTargetSlideWidensComfortZoneX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Living in the target slide widens the comfort zone"@en, "Leben im Zieldia erweitert die Komfortzone"@de ;
    skos:definition "Continuously dwelling in the target slide is said to expand the comfort zone and attune thought energy to the target life line."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGeneralStagesLivingTargetSlideX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWidenedComfortZoneAttunementTargetLineX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsInflatedImportanceX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of inflated importance"@en, "Zeichen übersteigerter Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Straining to reach the goal at the earliest moment, doubting one's abilities, or fearing difficulties shows inflated importance; fearing the goal is unattainable shows strong desire."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Straining to reach the goal at the earliest moment, doubting one's abilities, or fearing difficulties shows inflated importance; fearing the goal is unattainable shows strong desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPermissionImperfectErrX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Permission to be imperfect and err"@en, "Erlaubnis, unvollkommen zu sein und zu irren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explicitly allow yourself imperfection and errors; otherwise others will not show you leniency either."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptingDefeatPreparingBackUpsBeforeX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting defeat and preparing back-ups before freedom from desire"@en, "Niederlage annehmen und Ausweichpläne bereiten vor der Freiheit vom Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accept defeat as possible in advance and have escape routes and fallback plans ready."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSafetyNetBeforeRelease: the fallback is here the condition for freeing oneself of desire, not of outer importance."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingActingPurifiedIntentionX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingSafetyNet ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without this step one cannot free oneself of desire." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClaimedAdvantageKnowingRulesGameX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Claimed advantage of knowing the rules of the game"@en, "Behaupteter Vorteil, die Spielregeln zu kennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing Transurfing's rules is said to give a huge advantage over people who play pendulum games without knowing the rules; heavier techniques are announced for later chapters. If one does not obstruct outer intention by importance-driven intensity, it is said to deliver one to the goal for certain."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingUnexpectedChangesUnfoldX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting unexpected changes unfold"@en, "Unerwartete Veränderungen sich entfalten lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When running the target slide brings unexpected changes, do not slap about trying to fix them; let go of control, do not hurry to correct a surprise, and look for the positive side of the event, which in most cases becomes visible."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation: applied to the unexpected changes outer intention brings while the target slide runs, with the advice to look for their good side."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoGrainsTruthAllBestX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two grains of truth in all is for the best"@en, "Zwei Wahrheitskörner in alles ist zum Besten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not to be believed blindly: the obvious grain is that the alternatives flow follows the lowest-energy route, problems arising from fighting the current and from plans it does not fit; the hidden, weightier grain is that if one decides to see an apparently unfavourable change as working in one's favour, so it will be, a great force to be treated in the next chapter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningApparentSetbacksFavourableTurnsPerceptionX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning apparent setbacks into favourable turns by perception"@en, "Scheinbare Rückschläge durch Wahrnehmung in günstige Wendungen verwandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perceiving an apparently unfavourable change as positive is said to make it so."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPaddleVisualisingCurrentLinkTransferChainX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The paddle: visualising the current link of the transfer chain"@en, "Das Paddel: Visualisieren des aktuellen Glieds der Übertragungskette"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unlike the slide, this includes a script, but only the fragment for the present: affirm that everything is going well now and intend that tomorrow will be better, setting the next step's intention while taking the current step, as a mother delights in today's progress of her child and expects the next small step; take pleasure in the present and step dispassionately and impeccably."@en ;
    skos:note "Term of the English translation: paddle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPaddleVisualisationYieldsRisingSuccessX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Paddle visualisation yields rising success"@en, "Paddelvisualisierung ergibt steigenden Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualising the current link with the intention of a higher next rung creates a feedback circuit of rising success."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPaddleVisualisingCurrentLinkTransferChainX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAcceleratedSteadilyRisingSuccessAlongFlowX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceleratedSteadilyRisingSuccessAlongFlowX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accelerated, steadily rising success along the flow"@en, "Beschleunigter, stetig steigender Erfolg mit dem Strom"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving with the flow can be accelerated; a feedback loop forms in which each rung supports the next, success rises like climbing a ladder and every day brings a particle of it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGettingUpsetOverSetbackBreaksRungX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Getting upset over a setback breaks the rung"@en, "Ärger über einen Rückschlag bricht die Sprosse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Upset over a setback makes one slide down the ladder, wakes the inner critic and hooks one on a pendulum; while dissatisfied with oneself and attuned to self-criticism one cannot cross to lines of happiness and good fortune."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Upset over a setback makes one slide down the ladder, wakes the inner critic and hooks one on a pendulum; while dissatisfied with oneself and attuned to self-criticism one cannot cross to lines of happiness and good fortune; concerns pmp:TranserfingPaddleVisualisingCurrentLinkTransferChainX10."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSetbackAsHook: set in the ladder of the transfer chain: upset breaks the current rung and wakes the inner critic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFlowingGameGreetingSetbacksJoyfulSurpriseX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The flowing game: greeting setbacks with joyful surprise"@en, "Das Fließspiel: Rückschläge mit freudiger Überraschung begrüßen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treat setbacks as normal and greet each with glad surprise instead of irritation, treating them as outer intention moving you toward the goal by unforeseen ways; yield to the flow and let it push you onto the proper path."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingJoyInFailure: setbacks are greeted as the work of outer intention taking unforeseen routes to the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFlowingGameYieldsFavourableTurnsX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Flowing game yields favourable turns"@en, "Fließspiel ergibt günstige Wendungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Greeting setbacks as gifts is said to let outer intention carry one along unforeseen routes toward the goal."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFlowingGameGreetingSetbacksJoyfulSurpriseX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTurningApparentSetbacksFavourableTurnsPerceptionX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotFollowOthersPathsX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not follow others' paths"@en, "Nicht den Wegen anderer folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not watch how others reach success or try to keep pace; true success belongs to the few who refuse do as I do and walk their own path."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingImitatingTheCool: applied to paths to success and the herd instinct rather than to status."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingGoalPresentedFashionablePrestigiousX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotTieDreamHelpingLovedX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not tie your dream to helping loved ones"@en, "Den eigenen Traum nicht an die Hilfe für Nahestehende knüpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's final warning: linking the dream to helping those close to you can make everything go wrong. The heart is said to be selfish and to care only for its own wellbeing; altruism originates in the mind; if the goal serves another the heart loses interest and leaves the mind to exhaust itself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingFulfilmentThroughServiceOthersIllusionX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBuratinosTwoMistakesGoalAnotherMoneyX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Buratino's two mistakes: goal for another, money as means"@en, "Buratinos zwei Fehler: Ziel für einen anderen, Geld als Mittel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illustrated by the Russian tale: the wooden boy fails and suffers because (1) his goal serves his father, not himself, and (2) he treats money as a means. Money is neither means nor goal but an attribute along the way; dwelling on money thoughts creates harmful excess potential; with a true goal money comes by itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Illustrated by the Russian tale: the wooden boy fails and suffers because (1) his goal serves his father, not himself, and (2) he treats money as a means. Money is neither means nor goal but an attribute along the way; dwelling on money thoughts creates harmful excess potential; with a true goal money comes by itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMoneyAsAttribute: adds the first mistake, a goal that serves another, and the tale as illustration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFulfilmentThroughServiceOthersIllusionX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fulfilment through service to others as illusion"@en, "Erfüllung durch Dienst an anderen als Illusion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing one's fulfilment in serving others, helping the weak, or giving oneself to another's idea is called self-deception of a mind gripped by a pendulum; the heart stays miserable in its box. It is held by people who have not found, or not looked for, their own goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnHappinessFirstAltruismAfterGoalX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Own happiness first, altruism after the goal is reached"@en, "Zuerst das eigene Glück, Altruismus nach Erreichen des Ziels"@de ;
    skos:definition "While on the path, let the heart think only of itself so as not to frighten it away from the goal; once the goal is reached, the altruistic mind may help loved ones, nature, animals, children as much as it likes, with greater resources."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingGreaterAbilityHelpOthersOncePathX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingTsel ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Realisation'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'
#

pmc:TranserfingRightGoalDoorBeforeWaveGoodX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Right goal and door before the wave of good fortune"@en, "Richtiges Ziel und richtige Tür vor der Glückswelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Riding the wave of fortune is presented as following from being on one's path through the right door, with unity of heart and mind."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRidingWaveGoodFortuneRadiatingHarmoniousX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRidingWaveGoodFortuneRadiatingHarmoniousX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Riding the wave of good fortune, radiating harmonious energy"@en, "Auf dem Kamm der Glückswelle reiten, harmonische Energie ausstrahlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the path to one's goal through the right door one is said to ride the wave of good fortune and radiate harmonious energy from ease of heart; the quality of radiated energy adjusts, things pick up, problems disappear and inspiration visits often."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingRidingTheWave: the wave is now ridden on the path to one's own goal through the right door, with frequent inspiration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDefinitionInspirationX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Definition of inspiration"@en, "Bestimmung der Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inspiration, cloaked in mystery as a fickle muse, is defined as the union of heart and mind without importance. It does not come from anywhere but is released when the importance potential drops and is clamped when the impatient mind shuts the heart back in its box."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInspirationX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inspiration"@en, "Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state of elation in which creative work becomes easy, simple and brilliant, and one can work many hours without tiring."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityHeartMindInspirationX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of heart and mind for inspiration (necessary, not sufficient)"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand für Inspiration (notwendig, nicht hinreichend)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Union of heart and mind is the essential condition for inspiration, but alone it is not enough; working on one's goal will bring the union."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingInspirationX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Working on something one is not passionate about never yields true inspiration." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPreparingWaitingInspirationDrivesAwayX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Preparing for and waiting for inspiration drives it away"@en, "Vorbereiten auf und Warten auf Inspiration vertreibt sie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Careful preparation of the workspace and expectant waiting create excess importance potential and a storm of balanced forces; inactive waiting is desire squared; the more careful the ritual the worse the outcome (as with over-prepared meetings that fail); impatience bordering on despair builds a wall between heart and mind that takes time to remove."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Careful preparation of the workspace and expectant waiting create excess importance potential and a storm of balanced forces; inactive waiting is desire squared; the more careful the ritual the worse the outcome (as with over-prepared meetings that fail); impatience bordering on despair builds a wall between heart and mind that takes time to remove."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIdleWorry: applied to preparing for and waiting on inspiration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDropImportanceInspirationX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Drop of importance for inspiration"@en, "Abfall der Bedeutsamkeit für Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Importance, found in passionate desire for the goal and in insistent striving for inspiration, must drop before inspiration is released."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingInspirationX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "While anticipation and desire hold, inspiration does not come; balanced forces scare it away." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingReleasingInspirationThreeConditionsJustStartX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Releasing inspiration: three conditions, then just start"@en, "Inspiration freisetzen: drei Bedingungen, dann einfach anfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind controls inspiration by doing the opposite of its habit: (1) let go of wanting to reach the goal, keeping only the will to have without insistence, taking it as calmly as the post; (2) forget any special preparation for the mystery; (3) stop waiting for inspiration; then simply start working without waiting to feel inspired, irrespective of first results, as if setting the table and having tea purely for one's own enjoyment, expecting no guest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStartingWorkWithoutWaitingYieldsInspirationX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Starting work without waiting yields inspiration"@en, "Ohne Warten mit der Arbeit beginnen ergibt Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under the three conditions, inspiration is said to arrive in the course of doing, since acting intentionally dissolves excess potential; the muse, struck by indifference, joins you."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReleasingInspirationThreeConditionsJustStartX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingInspirationX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMuseX10 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Muse"@en, "Muse"@de ;
    skos:definition "The muse is used as a personification of inspiration, a temperamental lady who stays away from a house beset by balanced forces and comes when ignored."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "muse; kind fairies and muses" ;
    pm:nameRole "personification of inspiration" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Inspiration'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'
#

pmc:TranserfingForeignGoalsCanReachedGreaterCostX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Foreign goals can be reached, at greater cost"@en, "Fremde Ziele sind erreichbar, mit höherem Aufwand"@de ;
    skos:definition "A foreign goal can be reached with Transurfing, but with considerably more effort; the same principles apply, followed with utmost impeccability. Choosing foreign goals and doors is the path of greatest resistance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFullResponsibilityDestinyX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Full responsibility for one's destiny"@en, "Volle Verantwortung für das eigene Schicksal"@de ;
    skos:definition "The methods require taking the helm of intention oneself; the book gives only a map and the rules; asking the author whether to drop a goal shows the principles are not grasped; only pendulums offer ready solutions."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingControlOfDestiny ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingTakingHelmIntentionOneselfX10 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without full responsibility Transurfing cannot help and the methods do not work." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTakingHelmIntentionOneselfX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking the helm of intention oneself"@en, "Das Steuer der Absicht selbst übernehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Full responsibility for one's own destiny: making one's own decisions about goals and doors instead of seeking ready answers from the author or others, since only pendulums hand out ready solutions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReachingForeignGoalOneCannotAbandonX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reaching a foreign goal one cannot abandon"@en, "Ein fremdes Ziel erreichen, das man nicht mehr aufgeben kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to accomplish a goal that is not one's own when it is too late to drop it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAchievingForeignGoalX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Achieving a foreign goal"@en, "Ein fremdes Ziel erreichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Apply all principles for one's own goal with utmost impeccability; shed desire and surplus importance potential; act emotionally detached yet consciously aware; do not battle obstacles, which mostly come from the mind fighting the flow; reduce importance and they withdraw."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHandlingObstacles: applied to reaching a goal that is not one's own, with utmost impeccability."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDetachedImpeccablePursuitYieldsForeignGoalX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Detached, impeccable pursuit yields the foreign goal"@en, "Losgelöstes, untadeliges Verfolgen ergibt das fremde Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freeing oneself of desire and importance is said to allow a foreign goal to be reached quite easily."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAchievingForeignGoalX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingReachingForeignGoalOneCannotAbandonX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDiagnosingFormidableObstaclesX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Diagnosing formidable obstacles"@en, "Gewaltige Hindernisse diagnostizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "When serious obstacles arise, analyse where importance was inflated, what was given excessive meaning and where you fought the flow; then reduce importance, detach from the situation and trust the alternatives flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDiagnosingFailures: turned into a procedure for obstacles on the way to a goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReducingImportanceYieldsImprovementX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Reducing importance yields improvement"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit senken ergibt Besserung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lowering importance and trusting the flow after diagnosis is said to make things improve."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDiagnosingFormidableObstaclesX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingObstaclesFade ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReduceImportanceBeforeChangingDoorX10 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Reduce importance before changing door"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit senken vor dem Türwechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the goal stays elusive, perhaps the door is foreign; but first lower importance and observe the effect before switching doors, since even one's own door slams when importance is excessive (e.g. all eggs in one basket) and reopens with reduced importance and an alternative route."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingChoosingDoorX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPermissionHaveOpensDoorsX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Permission to have opens doors"@en, "Erlaubnis zu haben öffnet Türen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Foreign doors that stood open tend to slam unexpectedly; if the goal is truly one's own and one gives oneself permission to have, the true door opens as suddenly; granting oneself permission to have opens even foreign doors. One may have several goals and doors, so a new goal can always still be sought."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingWorkingForeignGoalWhileHoldingOwnX10 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Working a foreign goal while holding your own goal slide"@en, "Am fremden Ziel arbeiten und zugleich das eigene Zieldia halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is no need to drop what was started; continue toward the foreign goal through the foreign door while picturing your own goal slide and looking out for your own goal meanwhile."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDualTrackYieldsSmoothShiftX10 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dual track yields smooth shift"@en, "Doppelspur ergibt sanften Wechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Holding one's own goal slide while working a foreign goal is said to lead, with time, to a painless switch."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingWorkingForeignGoalWhileHoldingOwnX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSmoothTransitionTargetLineX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSmoothTransitionTargetLineX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Smooth transition to one's target line"@en, "Sanfter Übergang zur eigenen Ziellinie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention is said in time to open unseen doors allowing a painless change of activity, orchestrating the shift to the target line smoothly."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingErrorsInevitableNoDespairSelfCriticismX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Errors are inevitable; no despair or self-criticism"@en, "Fehler sind unvermeidlich; keine Verzweiflung, keine Selbstkritik"@de ;
    skos:definition "No one can fully escape pendulums imposing foreign doors, and even with knowledge one is not immune to error; do not despair or criticise yourself harshly, use mistakes; true success grows from past failures; only people without goals avoid mistakes."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingViciousCircleOfDissatisfaction ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartOppressedForeignDoorEndsCrisisX10 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart oppressed at a foreign door ends in crisis"@en, "Das an einer fremden Tür unterdrückte Herz endet in der Krise"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knocking at foreign doors brings difficulties; the mind forces the heart to fight on, but even strong-willed people reach a limit and things end in crisis, often in an unforgivable faux pas or very basic mistakes, which can happen to anyone."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: Knocking at foreign doors brings difficulties; the mind forces the heart to fight on, but even strong-willed people reach a limit and things end in crisis, often in an unforgivable faux pas or very basic mistakes, which can happen to anyone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImpeccableSmallThingsForeignPathX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Be impeccable in small things on a foreign path"@en, "Auf fremdem Weg in kleinen Dingen untadelig sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "On a path through a foreign door expect crises and mistakes but avoid blunders; act impeccably like someone hired out; paradoxically big mistakes are pardoned sooner than small slips; expect no sympathy, least from dependants whose expectations you fail; accusers wait for small offences."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingRentYourselfOut: applied to walking through a foreign door, adding that small slips are forgiven less readily than big mistakes."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingHeartOppressedForeignDoorEndsCrisisX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBewareLovingAdvisorsManipulatorsAfterDefeatX10 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Beware loving advisors and manipulators after a defeat"@en, "Vorsicht vor liebevollen Ratgebern und Manipulatoren nach einer Niederlage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Be wary of advice from loved ones who want the best for you (e.g. parents fixing a child's life goal early); after a defeat they will say they told you so, and manipulators exploit weakness to cut you down to size; they are right only that you erred. Do not yield to others' influence; believe in yourself; in searching for your goal listen to no one, follow your heart, be persistent against pendulums and attentive to the heart."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingManipulators: adds loving relatives who mean well and the moment after a defeat when advisers close in."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingManipulators ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen2 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (2004), ch. X Goals and Doors, section 'Reviving the Goal'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .
